                                                                        Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀XRB       Galactic Binaries, including HMXBs and LMXBs                                                                            ␀␀Î␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀Adjusted position by 1.6 arcmin closer to OA / Data loss due to overwrite of on-board data storage                      archived  20200429Cyg_X1_PSF01                                      @rπVlÙ!@A®Énóç@Q÷´6zë@	ä⁄πıY¥@s¡Ω•@Îu␀[¥.@Îu?BI10014001001@∞WÀÕ5®X@∞Gwe˝ä€@π˝@␀␀␀␀@π˝@␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï‰O%s¨ê␀␀›vHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀Observations of celestial sources will be undertaken throughout the mission to determine, and then monitor changes to, the calibration of the X-ray observatory. Observations will enable the calibration of absolute flux, spectral sensitivity, point spread function, and the timing capabilities of the observatory as well as the observatory optical alignment. NuSTAR will also participate in cross-calibration campaigns with the Chandra, XMM-Newton, Swift, and Suzaku X-ray observatories.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Calibration Observations                                    ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀CAL       NuSTAR calibration campaign                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀off-axis PSF calibration                                                                                                archived  20200429Bullet_shock                                      @Z'ŒŸá+¿KÛ¿6‚Î@pü=Ÿb∑¿5C–|Ñµ›@fçs¸PH@Îu?BI@ÎuÈÏÛº70001056001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‰N˝@F␀␀›-Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Observations of a sample of nearby galaxy clusters will be undertaken to detect and characterize the controversial non-thermal component emerging at high energies and to characterize the hot thermal emission in the vicinity of shock fronts. Merger shocks in galaxy clusters are important because they allow us to study the merger phenomenon by providing indications of the velocity and geometry of mergers and also provide important clues on the physical properties of the ICM.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   Galaxy clusters and extragalactic diffuse objects           ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀GCL       Galaxy Clusters and Relics                                                                                              ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                           