pe objects weaker in the GeV band, but are strong TeV emitters detected by Cerenkov ground-based arrays.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀BLZ       Blazars                                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀␀␀                              HESS                                                                                                ␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429GalSurvey_A_MOS003                                ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Îói"–Åı@Îój^∫Ÿ40031003001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‚Û©VŸ≤␀␀ﬂHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will provide an improvement in hard X-ray (sensitivity by orders of magnitude over previous satellites, allowing us to probe more deeply into the Galaxy than ever before.  This will provide the capability of detecting large fractions of known hard X-ray populations and perhaps to find new populations.  We also plan to study diffuse X-ray reflection nebulae near the Galactic center that may provide evidence for a more active period of accretion for the supermassive black hole at Sgr A*.                                                                                                                                                                                         