-thick AGN with NuSTAR provide us with an opportunity to constrain the nature of X-ray obscurers that are characteristic among AGN, potentially without the powerful continuum to complicate things. The primary goal of this research line is to observe a few key objects across three obscuration regimes. These will yield detailed spectra of the reflection hump and reflector efficiency/covering fraction that can be compared against existing models of unobscured AGN.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀OAGN      Obscured AGN, Including Compton-Thick AGN, BALQSOs, and ULIRGs                                                          ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Arp220                                            @m6ªò«‚Ç@7}Ì(åÁ@BNóçOﬂ;@JóÂ…‰@ur◊s¸@Îò´"–Åı@Îò‹^∫Ÿ60002026002@Nƒ‹∆?@G<µsÍ≥@Òk3333@ÒÅ+3333SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï‚Ïº”␀␀ﬂHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀Observations of obscured and/or Compton-thick AGN with NuSTAR provide us with an opportunity to constrain the nature of X-ray obscurers that are characteristic among AGN, potentially without the powerful continuum to complicate things. The primary goal of this research line is to observe a few key objects across t