                                                                     Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429M83                                               ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Îôª[¥.@Îôº[¥.50002043005␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‚ËFr(␀␀ﬂ^Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Our goal is to characterize the hard X-ray properties of nearby star-forming galaxies. We will investigate the bulk hard X-ray properties of the binaries, characterize the hard X-ray emission from the "famous" ULX source M82 X-1, and place a constraint on any diffuse Inverse Compton component, which might have implications for starburst galaxies' contribution to the 10-40 keV cosmic X-ray background. We also plan to perform deep observations of Local Group galaxies M31 and M33.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              Normal galaxies                                             ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀NGS       Starburst Galaxies and Local Group Galaxies                                                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316M83                                               @iÜÈx‘˝Ù¿=ﬁÌ(åÁ@s¶	‘ï+@@	ú‡uˆ˝@∂îFsÅÿ@Îôº[¥.@Îô„"–Åı50002043006@Â!ñRΩ@ÂF‹]@Ê¥¬∞ ƒú@Ê∑¢∞ ƒúSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï‚Á‹äÂ␀␀ﬂ^Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀Our goal is to characterize the hard X-ray properties of nearby star-forming galaxies. We will investigate the bulk hard X-ray properties of the binaries, characterize the hard X-ray emission from the "famous" ULX source M82 X-1, and place a constraint on any diffuse Inverse Compton component, which might have implications for starburst galaxies' contribution to the 10-40 keV cosmic X-ray background. We also plan to perform deep observations of Local Group galaxies M31 and M33.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              Normal galaxies                                             ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀NGS       Starburst Galaxies and Local Group Galaxies                                                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                              