ine the structure of AGN jets, primarily their content and the location of the dissipation region. Emission from those sources is variable, and crucial constraints are derived from multi-band monitoring campaigns. The program includes two classes of jet-dominated AGN, those with powerful jets detected as strong GeV emitters by Fermi, and less luminous BL Lac type objects weaker in the GeV band, but are strong TeV emitters detected by Cerenkov ground-based arrays.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀BLZ       Blazars                                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀␀␀+                              HESS                                                                                                ␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429PDS_456                                           ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Îöd"–Åı@ÎödÈÏÛº60002032001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‚‰ÿ=␀␀ﬂHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR observations of bright, nearby AGN will provide the best constraints to date on the corona temperature, breaking the degeneracy between two key corona parameters, temperature and optical depth. The target sample be used to test how Comptonization models, and particularly the assumed geometry, depend on physical parameters. NuSTAR will be an ideal instrument to use in the effort to constrain black hole spin and differentiate between complex absorption and reflection models.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀AGN       AGN Physics:Black Hole Spin + Coronal Temperature                                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316PDS_456                                           @pa⁄QŒ¿,ï%F
