rtunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316GRB130925A                                        @Dò˘	kπå¿:ÿ≠´üV@k'€"–Â`¿P5£n.±ƒ@gTÍJåM@Îû@±	eÉ@Îû_?BI80002096002@„(ïHÀí@„Ãuˆ˝"@‰è( Wßá@‰çË WßáSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï„ö∏≥␀␀›–Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observa