                                      ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î±IÕ{,†@Î±K^∫Ÿ60002032009␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï·åÃÃÕ␀␀ﬂHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR observations of bright, nearby AGN will provide the best constraints to date on the corona temperature, breaking the degeneracy between two key corona parameters, temperature and optical depth. The target sample be used to test how Comptonization models, and particularly the assumed geometry, depend on physical parameters. NuSTAR will be an ideal instrument to use in the effort to constrain black hole spin and differentiate between complex absorption and reflection models.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀AGN       AGN Physics:Black Hole Spin + Coronal Temperature                                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316PDS_456                                           @pa®Xy=Ÿ¿,w¥¢3ú@$´”√a@@&™#9¿ÎÓ@cÒ»K]Ã@Î±K^∫Ÿ@Î±ûîóûg60002032010@˙»—ûÉ‰&@˙Æ	v»¥9@¸¡Œ—N;Õ@¸¡û—N;ÕSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï·Ô◊‰±~␀␀ﬂHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR observations of bright, nearby AGN will provide the best constraints to date on the corona temperature, breaking the degeneracy between two key corona parameters, temperature and optical depth. The target sample be used to test how Comptonization models, and particularly the assumed geometry, depend on physical parameters. NuSTAR will be an ideal instrument to use in the effort to constrain black hole spin and differentiate between complex absorption and reflection models.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀AGN       AGN Physics:Black Hole Spin + Coronal Temperature                                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                     XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429HESSJ1640m465                                     @oF˘	kπå¿GB«À)_@u#‰%ÆÊ2?Ω˙C˛\ë—@d£◊
=q@Î±ûîóûg@Î±ü^∫Ÿ30002021004␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï·ÔôÅS—␀␀‡Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will undertake a comprehensive program of observations of magnetars and rotation-powered pulsars, designed to study the surprising hard X-ray emission discovered by INTEGRAL from these objects and to shed light on the broad-band spectra between the soft X-ray and high-energy gamma-ray bands. With its sensitive hard X-ray response NuSTAR can extend the soft X-ray spectrum by an order of magnitude in energy, allowing detailed constraints on the high-energy emission mechanisms of these objects.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀MAG       Magnetars and Rotation-Powered Pulsars                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316HESSJ1640m465                                     @oFÉ‰%ÆÊ¿GA4ÍJå@u#Ô4÷°b?¿¸PH@d(}VlÙ@Î±ü^∫Ÿ@Î±ÁÕ{,†30002021005@¯◊⁄7K∆®@¯√PQÇ©ì@˙§V’œ™Œ@˙£÷’œ™ŒSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï·Ó˜www␀␀‡Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will undertake a comprehensive program of observations of magnetars and rotation-powered pulsars, designed to study the surprising hard X-ray emission discovered by INTEGRAL from these objects and to shed light on the broad-band spectra between the soft X-ray and high-energy gamma-ray bands. With its sensitive hard X-ray response NuSTAR can extend the soft X-ray spectrum by an order of magnitude in energy, allowing detailed constraints on the high-energy emission mechanisms of these objects.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀MAG       Magnetars and Rotation-Powered Pulsars                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀Monitoring Campaign                                                                                                     archived  20200429GRO_J1744m28                                      ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î±ÁÕ{,†@Î±Ë"–Åı80002017003␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï·ÓªB^—␀␀ﬂHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR's hard X-ray sensitivity will allow for detailed studies of fainter X-ray binaries for the first time. This will include studies of HMXBs discovered by INTEGRAL but too faint to detect pulsations, cyclotron lines, or spectral breaks that would provide evidence that they have neutron star accretors. NuSTAR's energy resolution is unprecedented, and there are spectral features such as cyclotron lines from accreting pulsars and absorption edges in type I X-ray bursts that will be accessible to NuSTAR.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀XRB       Galactic Binaries, including HMXBs and LMXBs                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316GRO_J1744m28                                      @p¢˚ÁlãD¿<≤√…ÓÀ˚?vá+I∫?›0æÌ(ç@cO&Èx‘˛@Î±Ë"–Åı@Î±ıîóûg80002017004@¿Æäﬁ␀—∑@¡Fø§?Â…@–‰ÃÃÃÕ@–dÃÃÃÕSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï·Ó?∑/␀␀ﬂHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR's hard X-ray sensitivity will allow for detailed studies of fainter X-ray binaries for the first time. This will include studies of HMXBs discovered by INTEGRAL but too faint to detect pulsations, cyclotron lines, or spectral breaks that would provide evidence that they have neutron star accretors. NuSTAR's energy resolution is unprecedented, and there are spectral features such as cyclotron lines from accreting pulsars and absorption edges in type I X-ray bursts that will be accessible to NuSTAR.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀XRB       Galactic Binaries, including HMXBs and LMXBs                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              Chandra                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀ToO                                                                                                                     archived  20200429SN2014J                                           ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î±ıîóûg@Î±ˆîóûg80002092010␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï·Ì‡ŒQ)␀␀‚ËHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀SNe Ia are profoundly radioactive events. NuSTAR is potentially sensitive to the photoabsorbed Compton-scatter continuum of the gamma-ray lines from decay of 56Ni and 56Co (inaccessible to current gamma-ray instruments) which extends down into the NuSTAR bandpass for SNe Ia within ~20 Mpc. The flux and spectral shape of this HXR component is sensitive to both the overall nucleosynthesis (level of the Compton-scatter continuum) and the amount of mixing in the ejecta (measured by the photoabsorption).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Harrison                      