program of observations of magnetars and rotation-powered pulsars, designed to study the surprising hard X-ray emission discovered by INTEGRAL from these objects and to shed light on the broad-band spectra between the soft X-ray and high-energy gamma-ray bands. With its sensitive hard X-ray response NuSTAR can extend the soft X-ray spectrum by an order of magnitude in energy, allowing detailed constraints on the high-energy emission mechanisms of these objects.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀MAG       Magnetars and Rotation-Powered Pulsars                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316PSRB1259m63                                       @hv˚~êˇó¿OÔ™ÕûÉ‰@sàŒp:˚øÓa|⁄Q@qSn.±ƒ3@Îπ≠[¥.@Îπ∆"–Åı30002017004@‡«ˆ´6z@‡æ‹bM”@·ˇßª/ÏW@·˛«ª/ÏWSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï·≈˛åS␀␀ﬁ[Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will undertake a comprehensive program of observations of magnetars and rotation-powered pulsars, designed to study the surprising hard X-ray emission discovered by INTEGRAL from these objects and to shed light on the broad-band spectra between the soft X-ray and high-energy gamma-ray bands. With its sensitive hard X-ray response NuSTAR can extend the soft X-ray spectrum by an order of magnitude in energy, allowing detailed constraints on the high-energy emission mechanisms of these objects.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀MAG       Magnetars and Rotation-Powered Pulsars                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              HESS                                                                                                ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  202004291H0707m495                                        ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Îπ∆"–Åı@Îπ∆±	eÉ60001102001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï·≈¬.E␀␀ﬁ[Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR observations of bright, nearby AGN will provide the best constraints to date on the corona temperature, breaking the degeneracy between two key corona parameters, temperature and optical depth. The target sample be used to test how Comptonization models, and particularly the assumed geometry, depend on physical parameters. NuSTAR will be an ideal instrument to use in the effort to constrain black hole spin and differentiate between complex absorption and reflection models.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀AGN       AGN Physics:Black Hole Spin + Coronal Temperature                                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  201503161H0707m495                                        @Z«X‚e,¿H»'RT`™@pAÒA [¿¿1¬M“Ò©¸@Ã/É{J#@Îπ∆±	eÉ@Î∫-"–Åı60001102002AûfÑM;Aï'≥333A·€fö‘,A·Îfö‘,SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï·ƒÍ¬s␀␀ﬁ[Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR observations of bright, nearby AGN will provide the best constraints to date on the corona temperature, breaking the degeneracy between two key corona parameters, temperature and optical depth. The target sample be used to test how Comptonization models, and particularly the assumed geometry, depend on physical parameters. NuSTAR will be an ideal instrument to use in the effort to constrain black hole spin and differentiate between complex absorption and reflection models.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀AGN       AGN Physics:Black Hole Spin + Coronal Temperature                                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar flare CME                                                                                                                   ␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429SDSSJ080941d74p534125d0                           ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î∫-"–Åı@Î∫.^∫Ÿ80001004001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï·ƒûio␀␀ﬁ[Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The goal of the Blazar program is to determine the structure of AGN jets, primarily their content and the location of the dissipation region. Emission from those sources is variable, and crucial constraints are derived from multi-band monitoring campaigns. The program includes two classes of jet-dominated AGN, those with powerful jets detected as strong GeV emitters by Fermi, and less luminous BL Lac type objects weaker in the GeV band, but are strong TeV emitters detected by Cerenkov ground-based arrays.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀BLZ       Blazars                                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316SDSSJ080941d74p534125d0                           @^óó$tSè@J“6‚ÎC@dìp£◊
=@@a#¢úwö@t‰¥¢3ú@Î∫.^∫Ÿ@Î∫AÕ{,†80001004002@€oƒ4m≈÷@€Y°a‰˜@›tì+J@›rS+JSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï·ƒE∞[␀␀ﬁ[Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The goal of the Blazar program is to determine the structure of AGN jets, primarily their content and the location of the dissipation region. Emission from those sources is variable, and crucial constraints are derived from multi-band monitoring campaigns. The program includes two classes of jet-dominated AGN, those with powerful jets detected as strong GeV emitters by Fermi, and less luminous BL Lac type objects weaker in the GeV band, but are strong TeV emitters detected by Cerenkov ground-based arrays.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀BLZ       Blazars                                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                     Swift                                                                                               ␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429Fairall_9                                         @4‰á¸π#£¿Ma„º”@rt*ô0æ¿LÈ[W>´6@Vu%F@Î∫AÕ{,†@Î∫C^∫Ÿ60001130001@HCS&¬@H5®Xy=Ÿ@J␀␀␀␀␀␀@J␀␀␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï·ƒH,␀␀ﬂ∆Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀!ïWe propose to observe the bare Seyfert 1 galaxy Fairall 9 for a net exposure time of 175 ks with both XMM and NuSTAR to study its broad-band spectral shape from the UV to the hard X-ray bands. This precise broad-band spectrum, will allow us to determine the continuum with high accuracy, enabling the removal of model degeneracies. In particular, we hope to identify the nature of the soft excess in the source and search for a high energy cut-off. Fairall 9 has been selected as a Priority A Target by the NuSTAR team, pre-approving the proposed NuSTAR observation.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Lohfink                       Anne                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀X13       The Broad-Band Spectral Shape of Fairall 9                                                                              ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20200429Fairall_9                                         @4·:í£S¿M_±[W>´@rt6‚ÎC¿LÍÓcä	@VcökP∞Ú@Î∫C^∫Ÿ@Î∫^±	eÉ60001130002@ËñÔ4÷°@Á˜~æﬂ§@ÈƒBE° ¡@Èƒ¢E° ¡SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï·√ÆÓÓÔ␀␀ﬂ∆Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀!ïWe propose to observe the bare Seyfert 1 galaxy Fairall 9 for a net exposure time of 175 ks with both XMM and NuSTAR to study its broad-band spectral shape from the UV to the hard X-ray bands. This precise broad-band spectrum, will allow us to determine the continuum with high accuracy, enabling the removal of model degeneracies. In particular, we hope to identify the nature of the soft excess in the source and search for a high energy cut-off. Fairall 9 has been selected as a Priority A Target by the NuSTAR team, pre-approving the proposed NuSTAR observation.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Lohfink                       Anne                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀X13       The Broad-Band Spectral Shape of Fairall 9                                                                              ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429Fairall_9                                         @4U2a|¿Mc∆ßÔù≤@rsä	ﬁ¿LÊ4ÍK@Vc⁄QŒ@Î∫^±	eÉ@Î∫îîóûg60001130003@ˆË´€ã¨q@ˆ€oÜYJı@¯ÉËÇ@∑Ä@¯ÑHÇ@∑ÄSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï·√‚jÛ␀␀ﬂ∆Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀!ïWe propose to observe the bare Seyfert 1 galaxy Fairall 9 for a net exposure time of 175 ks with both XMM and NuSTAR to study its broad-band spectral shape from the UV to the hard X-ray bands. This precise broad-band spectrum, will allow us to determine the continuum with high accuracy, enabling the removal of model degeneracies. In particular, we hope to identify the nature of the soft excess in the source and search for a high energy cut-off. Fairall 9 has been selected as a Priority A Target by the NuSTAR team, pre-approving the proposed NuSTAR observation.                                        