=q␀␀ﬂHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Mrk477                                            @kÉ&Èx‘˛@J¡„º”@WO‚Ç@∑Ä@Lm'ª0@K!«y¶µ@Îª"–Åı@Îª±	eÉ60061255002@—¶«‚ÇA@—öäç∏∫«@“¬„ZÖáî@“¬„ZÖáîSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï·¿’É˚␀␀ﬂHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 