 fainter X-ray binaries for the first time. This will include studies of HMXBs discovered by INTEGRAL but too faint to detect pulsations, cyclotron lines, or spectral breaks that would provide evidence that they have neutron star accretors. NuSTAR's energy resolution is unprecedented, and there are spectral features such as cyclotron lines from accreting pulsars and absorption edges in type I X-ray bursts that will be accessible to NuSTAR.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀XRB       Galactic Binaries, including HMXBs and LMXBs                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429M83                                               ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÎΩö^∫Ÿ@ÎΩöîóûg50002043009␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï·˚£uÛ␀␀ﬂ^Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Our goal is to characterize the hard X-ray properties of nearby star-forming galaxies. We will investigate the bulk hard X-ray properties of the binaries, characterize the hard X-ray emission from the "famous" ULX source M82 X-1, and place a constraint on any diffuse Inverse Compton component, which might have implications for starburst galaxies' contribution to the 10-40 keV cosmic X-ray background. We also plan to perform deep observations of Local Group galaxies M31 and M33.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              Normal galaxies                                             ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀NGS       Starburst Galaxies and Local Group Galaxies                                                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316M83                                               @iá§?Â…¿=·@N§©@s¶&Èx‘˛@@ìtºj@u$
¶L/É@ÎΩöîóûg@ÎΩÕx%◊J50002043010@Ò?bºj~˙@Ò3–C˛\í@Úâ∫kπå~@Úà⁄kπå~SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï·åÃÃÕ␀␀ﬂ^Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀Our goal is to characterize the hard X-ray properties of nearby star-forming galaxies. We will investigate the bulk hard X-ray properties of the binaries, characterize the hard X-ray emission from the "famous" ULX source M82 X-1, and place a constraint on any diffuse Inverse Compton component, which might have implications for starburst galaxies' contribution to the 10-40 keV cosmic X-ray background. We also plan to perform deep observations of Local Group galaxies M31 and M33.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              Normal galaxies                                             ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀NGS       Starburst Galaxies and Local Group Galaxies                                                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429eta_Car                                           @d&JåLò¿M⁄êñªô@q˜Æz·Hø‰$›/üæ@uœ-w1è≈@ÎΩÕx%◊J@ÎΩŒ^∫Ÿ30002040001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï·[óS␀␀ﬂ™Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀"-Eta Carinae is an extremely massive binary system whose strong winds produce a variety of high-energy X-ray and possibly gamma-ray emission. Earlier observations found interesting features in the extremely hard X-ray band: i) a flat spectral component above 9 keV toward the flux maximum; ii) strong 15-20 keV emission during an occultation of the wind-wind colliding plasma; iii) stable power-law emission above 25 keV. These features are signs of the highest energy processes yet detected in any colliding wind binary. Broad band X-ray observations around periastron are essential to understand those features. We therefore propose joint XMM-Newton and NuSTAR observations at 4 key phases around the next periastron passage of Eta Carinae in 2014.6.                                                 Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Hamaguchi                     Kenji                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀X13       Probing the Highest Energy Phenomena of Eta Carinae around Periastron in 2014                                           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316eta_Car                                           @d&˚~êˇó¿M⁄£S&@q˜ﬁ␀—∑ø‰⁄QŒ@u‘≤-V@ÎΩŒ^∫Ÿ@ÎΩ·"–Åı30002040002@‡ë•ú‡@‡”<64@·sÕ•ú‡@·sÕ•ú‡SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï·
