ission from the "famous" ULX source M82 X-1, and place a constraint on any diffuse Inverse Compton component, which might have implications for starburst galaxies' contribution to the 10-40 keV cosmic X-ray background. We also plan to perform deep observations of Local Group galaxies M31 and M33.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              Normal galaxies                                             ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀NGS       Starburst Galaxies and Local Group Galaxies                                                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316M83                                               @iáù≤-V¿=·$›/@s¶$xG@@ùIQÇ™@u#Œ_o“@ÎΩ·±	eÉ@Îæ2îóûg50002043012@˙˜ﬁhr∞!@˙ÂÉnò@¸Ó“ÚÂ@¸Ôæ“ÚÂSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï·E˘,`␀␀ﬂ^Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀Our goal is to characterize the hard X-ray properties of nearby star-forming galaxies. We will investigate the bulk hard X-ray properties of the binaries, characterize the hard X-ray emission from the "famous" ULX source M82 X-1, and place a constraint on any diffuse Inverse Compton component, which might have implications for starburst galaxies' contribution to the 10-40 keV cosmic X-ray background. We also plan to perform deep observations of Local Group 