    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀ULX       Ultraluminous X-ray Sources (ULXs)                                                                                      ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀ToO                                                                                                                     archived  20200429NGC5674                                           ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î¬[¥.@Î¬ÈÏÛº60061337001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï·›Øô␀␀ﬂHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316NGC5674                                           @kM·∞â†'@°a‰˜e˛@v:.HËß@L≈:í£@vvÅ$›/@Î¬ÈÏÛº@Î¬"x%◊J60061337002@‘/≈hr∞!@‘&r1¯†ê@’º9¿ÎÓ@’ºì9¿ÎÓSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï·ëY‚k␀␀ﬂHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        arch