1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀GPS       Galactic Plane Survey                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429IGRJ16318m4848                                    ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î«yîóûg@Î«z^∫Ÿ30001006001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‡ÁK©áe␀␀ﬂ∫Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀!ÛWe propose to observe the Compton-thick source IGR J16318-4848 with XMM-Newton simultaneously to our already approved NuSTAR science team observation. Our aim is to measure the first high signal to noise, high resolution broad band spectrum of this type of source. Our goal is to constrain the geometry of the absorber in the system further through broad-band spectroscopy, analysis of the Iron line, including the search for a Compton shoulder, and a measurement of the response of the iron line flux to continuum variations.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Wilms                         Joern                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀X13       Simultaneous XMM-Newton and NuSTAR Observations of IGR J16318-4848                                                      ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316IGRJ16318m4848                                    @n˝dZ¨¿Hlæﬂ§@@t˜¿Énòø”Å◊€Ùá˝@uP∞Ú{≥@Î«z^∫Ÿ@Î«üîóûg30001006002@Îü3CïÅ@ÎôÈa@O@Ì§ç≠B√ @Ì•ç≠B√ SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï‡ÊËNÇ␀␀ﬂ∫Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀!ÛWe propose to observe the Compton-thick source IGR J16318-4848 with XMM-Newton simultaneously to our already approved NuSTAR science team observation. Our aim is to measure the first high signal to noise, high resolution broad band spectrum of this type of source. Our goal is to constrain the geometry of the absorber in the system further through broad-band spectroscopy, analysis of the Iron line, including the search for a Compton shoulder, and a measurement of the response of the iron line flux to continuum variations.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Wilms                         Joern                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀X13       Simultaneous XMM-Newton and NuSTAR Observations of IGR J16318-4848                                                      ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429NGC3256                                           ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î«üîóûg@Î«†?BI50002042001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‡Êü€óS␀␀ﬂÆHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Our goal is to characterize the hard X-ray properties of nearby star-forming galaxies. We will investigate the bulk hard X-ray properties of the binaries, characterize the hard X-ray emission from the "famous" ULX source M82 X-1, and place a constraint on any diffuse Inverse Compton component, which might have implications for starburst galaxies' contribution to the 10-40 keV cosmic X-ray background. We also plan to perform deep observations of Local Group galaxies M31 and M33.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              Normal galaxies                                             ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀NGS       Starburst Galaxies and Local Group Galaxies                                                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316NGC3256                                           @cû1&Èy¿EÔ|Ìëhs@qSM“Ò©¸@'!-w1ê@N†>BZÓc@Î«†?BI@Î»%îóûg50002042002AÌpÑìuAÊüRΩ<An®m˙C˛Aq@m˙C˛SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï‡Âô8Çw␀␀ﬂÆHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀Our goal is to characterize the hard X-ray properties of nearby star-forming galaxies. We will investigate the bulk hard X-ray properties of the binaries, characterize the hard X-ray emission from the "famous" ULX source M82 X-1, and place a constraint on any diffuse Inverse Compton component, which might have implications for starburst galaxies' contribution to the 10-40 keV cosmic X-ray background. We also plan to perform deep observations of Local Group galaxies M31 and M33.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              Normal galaxies                                             ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀NGS       Starburst Galaxies and Local Group Galaxies                                                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                     Chandra                                                                                             ␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429NGC5995                                           ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î»%îóûg@Î»&?BI60061267001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‡ÂIÂt␀␀ﬂ¬Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targetin