etect pulsations, cyclotron lines, or spectral breaks that would provide evidence that they have neutron star accretors. NuSTAR's energy resolution is unprecedented, and there are spectral features such as cyclotron lines from accreting pulsars and absorption edges in type I X-ray bursts that will be accessible to NuSTAR.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀XRB       Galactic Binaries, including HMXBs and LMXBs                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316eta_Car                                           @d'¶µ(¿M“~˘€"—@q˜ä	ﬁø‚'RT`™e@VYûÉ‰%Ø@ÎÀ¿ÈÏÛº@ÎÀˆ±	eÉ30002010012@Û‚È:í£@Û⁄©˝ä⁄∫@ıR␀qué@ıU␀quéSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï‡âØò◊␀␀ﬂ™Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR's hard X-ray sensitivity will allow for detailed studies of fainter X-ray binaries for the first time. This will include studies of HMXBs discovered by INTEGRAL but too faint to detect pulsations, cyclotron lines, or spectral breaks that would provide evidence that they have neutron star accretors. NuSTAR's energy resolution is unprecedented, and there are spectral features such as cyclotron lines from accreting pulsars and absorption edges in type I 