                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Degenaar                      Nathalie                      NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀TOO                                                                                                                               ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀ToO                                                                                                                     archived  202004292FGLJ0630d9m2406                                  ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÎŒvÈÏÛº@ÎŒwÕ{,†60001140001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‡{∫·GÆ␀␀ﬂ˙Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀!bFor a long time high-redshift BL Lac objects were deemed not to exist. Fermi showed us that there is relevant population of BL Lacs with redshift beyond 1.0. Some of them belong to the high-synchrotron peaked (HSP) class and are among the hardest gamma-ray sources detected by Fermi showing emission up and beyond 100 GeV. This makes them the most luminous BL Lacs ever detected and rates them among the most powerful accelerators in the Universe. We plan to observe 3 extreme BL Lacs simultaneously with XMM-Newton, GROND and Swift. This will provide unprecedented coverage of the synchrotron peak from IR to hard X-ray allowing us: to understand the nature and the energetic of these objects, to answer long-standing questions on the blazar sequence and to use them as probes of the EBL.           Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Ajello                        Marco                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀X13       BL Lac Objects at the highest redshifts                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  201503162FGLJ0630d9m2406                                  @Xr^5?|Ó¿8JåLò@mOv_Ÿ¿.$M:í£@e7≤-V@ÎŒwÕ{,†@ÎŒ´[¥.60001140002@D8>BZÓ@:KD–©@Òw2ç∏ª@Òw“ç∏ªSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï‡{>ìÈ?␀␀ﬂ˙Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀!bFor a long time high-redshift BL Lac objects were deemed not to exist. Fermi showed us that there is relevant population of BL Lacs with redshift beyond 1.0. Some of them belong to the high-synchrotron peaked (HSP) class and are among the hardest gamma-ray sources detected by Fermi showing emission up and beyond 100 GeV. This makes them the most luminous BL Lacs ever detected and rates them among the most powerful accelerators in the Universe. We plan to observe 3 extreme BL Lacs simultaneously with XMM-Newton, GROND and Swift. This will provide unprecedented coverage of the synchrotron peak from IR to hard X-ray allowing us: to understand the nature and the energetic of these objects, to answer long-standing questions on the blazar sequence and to use them as probes of the EBL.           Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Ajello                        Marco                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀X13       BL Lac Objects at the highest redshifts                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar flare                   XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429LEDA2801977                                       @nÂ`Aâ7¿NíOv`@t=o␀h€å¿û“àŒp;@4Nv»¥9X@ÎŒ´[¥.@ÎŒ¨"–Åı60061268001?Ï“àŒp:˚?Ì=Ÿb∂Æ?␀␀␀␀␀␀?␀␀␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‡{ﬁ†␀␀ﬂ¬Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20200429LEDA2801977                                       @nè\(ı√¿Ní3úæ‡@t=\ë—N<¿ú(ı¬è\@4d„º”ZÜ@ÎŒ¨"–Åı@ÎŒ∂±	eÉ60061268002@“p;dZ@“j◊Í≥g°@”´6@∑Ä4@”´6@∑Ä4SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï‡zÀÚXø␀␀ﬂ¬Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                         