∂Õè␀␀‡ Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR observations of bright, nearby AGN will provide the best constraints to date on the corona temperature, breaking the degeneracy between two key corona parameters, temperature and optical depth. The target sample be used to test how Comptonization models, and particularly the assumed geometry, depend on physical parameters. NuSTAR will be an ideal instrument to use in the effort to constrain black hole spin and differentiate between complex absorption and reflection models.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀AGN       AGN Physics:Black Hole Spin + Coronal Temperature                                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Mrk3                                              @Wyﬁi≠Bƒ@Q√ïÅ$›@aÁOÑM@6ôÓÀ˚µ@`Ôˆ+jÁ’@Îœ(^∫Ÿ@Îœ9[¥.60002048010@ﬁ&?ZÖáî@ﬁ`™d√@‡Øo␀h‹@‡Øo␀h‹SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï‡x¬w`␀␀‡ Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR observations of bright, nearby AGN will provide the best constraints to date on the corona temperature, breaking the degeneracy between two key corona parameters, temperature and