ns will permit to search for variations of the reflected components on time scales spanning from a week to half a year and, when compared with previous XMM-Newton observations, up to several years. This program will allow us to both unambiguously confirm previous claims of such variations and tightly constrain                              Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Bianchi                       Stefano                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀X13       Locating the reflecting regions in the archetypal Compton-thick Sy2 NGC1068                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316NGC1068                                           @DSÅ◊€Ùàø£˜ŒŸá+@e~a|⁄Q¿J˚ÁlãD@s„	kπå~@Î‹A±	eÉ@Î‹iÕ{,†60002033004@Í6ØI∫@Í*l-‡@Ï1•„S¯@ÏÒ•„S¯SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï‡ÔP␀␀‡dHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀!We propose four, logarithmically spaced, 50 ks XMM-Newton observations of the Seyfert galaxy NGC1068, the archetypal and one of the brightest Compton-thick Seyfert 2. This source is likely accreting at a high rate, so it is expected to be intrinsically highly variable. Previous works have indeed claimed both spectral and continuum variability, although between observations performed with different spectrometers and satellites. The four proposed observations will permit to search for variations of the reflected components on time scales spanning from a week to half a year and, when compared with previous XMM-Newton observations, up to several years. This program will allow us to both unambiguously confirm previous claims of such variations and tightly constrain                              Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Bianchi                       Stefano                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀X13       Locating the reflecting regions in the archetypal Compton-thick Sy2 NGC1068                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429M31_MOS001                                        ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î‹iÕ{,†@Î‹j[¥.50026001001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‡ÜªZ•␀␀‡ÙHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Our goal is to characterize the hard X-ray properties of nearby star-forming galaxies. We will investigate the bulk hard X-ray properties of the binaries, characterize the hard X-ray emission from the "famous" ULX source M82 X-1, and place a constraint on any diffuse Inverse Compton component, which might have implications for starburst galaxies' contribution to the 10-40 keV cosmic X-ray background. We also plan to perform deep observations of Local Group galaxies M31 and M33.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              Normal galaxies                                             ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                     