 (sensitivity by orders of magnitude over previous satellites, allowing us to probe more deeply into the Galaxy than ever before.  This will provide the capability of detecting large fractions of known hard X-ray populations and perhaps to find new populations.  We also plan to study diffuse X-ray reflection nebulae near the Galactic center that may provide evidence for a more active period of accretion for the supermassive black hole at Sgr A*.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀GPS       Galactic Plane Survey                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316HD96670                                           @d€F
