hallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429MCGm5m23m16                                       ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î‡◊±	eÉ@Î‡ÿx%◊J60001046007␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏﬂˇOWú␀␀ﬂ¬Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR observations of bright, nearby AGN will provide the best constraints to date on the corona temperature, breaking the degeneracy between two key corona parameters, temperature and optical depth. The target sample be used to test how Comptonization models, and particularly the assumed geometry, depend on physical parameters. NuSTAR will be an ideal instrument to use in the effort to constrain black hole spin and differentiate between complex absorption and reflection models.                                                                                                                                                                                   