                                                              Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Orio                          Marina                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀TOO                                                                                                                               ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              Chandra                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀ToO                                                                                                                     archived  20200429Mrk3                                              ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î„°îóûg@Î„¢^∫Ÿ60002049003␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏﬂÓd‚
␀␀‡´Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀!yWe propose an intense monitoring campaign of the heavily obscured Seyfert Galaxy Markarian 3 during the XMM-Newton AO-13. We aim at: a) constraining the size of the gas clouds responsible for optically-thick reprocessing of the nuclear continuum; b) probing a hitherto poorly unexplored parameter space on the distance between the X-ray corona and the surrounding optically-thick gas. We request 10 observations of 17 ks each. Thanks to the unique combination of hard X-ray spectral shape and visibility, the proposed observations represent an extremely efficient way of using XMM-Newton during high-radiation intervals close to the perigee passages, when the feasibility of most astrophysical X-ray experiments is severely hampered.                                                                   Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Guainazzi                     Matteo                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀X13       Measuring the torus spatial scale(s) in Seyfert galaxies: a cheap XMM-Newton monitoring campaign                        ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Mrk3                                              @WuË>BZÓ@Q¿‡uˆ˝"@aËa|⁄Q@6èv_ÿ≠¨@tlÌ(åÁ@Î„¢^∫Ÿ@Î„±îóûg60002049004@ÿGjÁ’g@ÿ¸ê-‡@Ÿ¡Ω†'RT@Ÿ¬˝†'RTSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏﬂÌ…{B_␀␀‡´Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀!yWe propose an intense monitoring campaign of the heavily obscured Seyfert Galaxy Markarian 3 during the XMM-Newton AO-13. We aim at: a) constraining the size of the gas clouds responsible for optically-thick reprocessing of the nuclear continuum; b) probing a hitherto poorly unexplored parameter space on the distance between the X-ray corona and the surrounding optically-thick gas. We request 10 observations of 17 ks each. Thanks to the unique combination of hard X-ray spectral shape and visibility, the proposed observations represent an extremely efficient way of using XMM-Newton during high-radiation intervals close to the perigee passages, when the feasibility of most astrophysical X-ray experiments is severely hampered.                                                                   Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Guainazzi                     Matteo                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀X13       Measuring the torus spatial scale(s) in Seyfert galaxies: a cheap XMM-Newton monitoring campaign                        ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429AM_Her                                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î„±îóûg@Î„≤"–Åı80001037001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏﬂÌ†Öœ␀␀‡õHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀"≤The spectral components of polars -- strongly magnetic CVs -- are barely disentangled without sufficient spectral coverage. XMM-Newton plus NuSTAR can solve the riddle but the frequent low states of the brightest members prevented systematic studies of high-accretion rate polars (HARPs). We thus began TOO-like XMM-Newton observations of the brightest systems in their high states and propose to continue in AO13 with one further trigger. We will investigate the physics of the hard X-ray emitting shock, the heated accretion pole cap, the atmosphere of the white dwarf, the absorption in the shock and in the flow, the lines in the accretion flow and the reflection from the white dwarf by phase-resolved X-ray spectroscopy and high-speed OM-photometry.                                             Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Schwope                       Axel                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀X13       Magnetic accretion in high-accretion rate polars                                                                        ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316AM_Her                                            @q!F
¶L0@HÚh	‘ï@SxbM“Ú@9ÏãCïÅ@aÀ“Ò©˚Á@Î„≤"–Åı@Î„Ÿ±	eÉ80001037002@ÎM˜‡q@ÎL¿7¥¢4@Ìá®4Í@ÌäË4ÍSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏﬂÌ7`U␀␀‡õHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀"≤The spectral components of polars -- strongly magnetic CVs -- are barely disentangled without sufficient spectral coverage. XMM-Newton plus NuSTAR can solve the riddle but the frequent low states of the brightest members prevented systematic studies of high-accretion rate polars (HARPs). We thus began TOO-like XMM-Newton observations of the brightest systems in their high states and propose to continue in AO13 with one further trigger. We will investigate the physics of the hard X-ray emitting shock, the heated accretion pole cap, the atmosphere of the white dwarf, the absorption in the shock and in the flow, the lines in the accretion flow and the reflection from the white dwarf by phase-resolved X-ray spectroscopy and high-speed OM-photometry.                                             Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Schwope                       Axel                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀X13       Magnetic accretion in high-accretion rate polars                                                                        ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀ToO                                                                                                                     archived  20200429HolmbergIX_X1                                     ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î„Ÿ±	eÉ@Î„⁄?BI30002034005␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏﬂÌeC!␀␀‡©Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀dsSuzaku proposal number 91251        