                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Walton                        D.                            NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀S09       Suzaku/NuSTAR joint program for cycle 9                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              Suzaku                                                                                              ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429Mrk376                                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î„˘ÈÏÛº@Î„˙[¥.60160288001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏﬂÏÖgâ¨␀␀ﬂ%Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Mrk376                                            @["Ov_Ÿ@F◊ßÜ¬&Å@eyù≤-V@6£ä	ﬁ@uMá+J@Î„˙[¥.@Î‰^∫Ÿ60160288002@◊õü∂E°À@◊êòH@ŸUåÿD–@ŸWÿD–SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏﬂÏCπ␀␀ﬂ%Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429Mrk3                                              ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î‰^∫Ÿ@Î‰x%◊J60002049005␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏﬂÏ∞[␀␀‡´Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀!yWe propose an intense monitoring campaign of the heavily obscured Seyfert Galaxy Markarian 3 during the XMM-Newton AO-13. We aim at: a) constraining the size of the gas clouds responsible for optically-thick reprocessing of the nuclear continuum; b) probing a hitherto poorly unexplored parameter space on the distance between the X-ray corona and the surrounding optically-thick gas. We request 10 observations of 17 ks each. Thanks to the unique combination of hard X-ray spectral shape and visibility, the proposed observations represent an extremely efficient way of using XMM-Newton during high-radiation intervals close to the perigee passages, when the feasibility of most astrophysical X-ray experiments is severely hampered.                                                                   Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Guainazzi                     Matteo                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀X13       Measuring the torus spatial scale(s) in Seyfert galaxies: a cheap XMM-Newton monitoring campaign               