¶@ÎÂî?BI@ÎÂîÕ{,†60002049009@/Ø∑È˘@¥9Xb@Äè1¯†ê.@Äè1¯†ê.SCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïﬂ„∞4V␀␀‡´Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀!yWe propose an intense monitoring campaign of the heavily obscured Seyfert Galaxy Markarian 3 during the XMM-Newton AO-13. We aim at: a) constraining the size of the gas clouds responsible for optically-thick reprocessing of the nuclear continuum; b) probing a hitherto poorly unexplored parameter space on the distance between the X-ray corona and the surrounding optically-thick gas. We request 10 observations of 17 ks each. Thanks to the unique combination of hard X-ray spectral shape and visibility, the proposed observations represent an extremely efficient way of using XMM-Newton during high-radiation intervals close to the perigee passages, when the feasibility of most astrophysical X-ray experiments is severely hampered.                                                                   Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Guainazzi                     Matteo                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀X13       Measuring the torus spatial scale(s) in Seyfert galaxies: a cheap XMM-Newton monitoring campaign                        ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20200429Mrk3                                              @WwlãCïÅ@Q¿Åo␀h‹@aËßÊö‘@6êﬁ“àŒp@s´cä	@ÎÂîÕ{,†@ÎÂ£îóûg60002049010@€Súâ†'R@€I‚QŒ@›S,Xy=Ÿ@›X¨Xy=ŸSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬂ„ozÄ␀␀‡´Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀!yWe propose an intense monitoring campaign of the heavily obscured Seyfert Galaxy Markarian 3 during the XMM-Newton AO-13. We aim at: a) constraining the size of the gas clouds responsible for optically-thick reprocessing of the nuclear continuum; b) probing a hitherto poorly unexplored parameter space on the distance between the X-ray corona and the surrounding optically-thick gas. We request 10 observations of 17 ks each. Thanks to the unique combination of hard X-ray spectral shape and visibility, the proposed observations represent an extremely efficient way of using XMM-Newton during high-radiation intervals close to the perigee passages, when the feasibility of most astrophysical X-ray experiments is severely hampered.                                                                   Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Guainazzi                     Matteo                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀X13       Measuring the torus spatial scale(s) in Seyfert galaxies: a cheap XMM-Newton monitoring campaign                        ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀5/10 observations                                                                                                       archived  20200429Mkn_6                                             @Yª±[W>´@RòÚ{≤˛≈@aäYJÙÿ@9Ò£n.±ƒ@t'ÁlãCñ@ÎÂ£îóûg@ÎÂ£Õ{,†60102044001@rÁué!ñS@rﬂe+”√a@t%2 Wßá@t%2 WßáSCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïﬂ„BsK␀␀·qHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀jWe request two quasi-simultaneous NuSTAR + Suzaku-XIS pointings of the radio-loud Sy 1.5 Mkn 6 to understand the complexity of its accreting circumnuclear gas structures. A series of high-quality, broadband X-ray spectra, including coverage above 10 keV, are needed to properly quantify the variable and complex line of sight absorbers. These new observations, in conjunction with radio and previous X-ray observations, will be a unique opportunity to understand accretion modes in the innermost regions of a radio-loud AGN that has recently undergone a merger.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Markowitz                     Alex                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       COMPLEX CIRCUMNUCLEAR STRUCTURE IN RADIO-LOUD AGN: VARIABLE ABSORPTION IN MKN 6                                         ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20200429Mkn_6                                             @YΩfœAÚ@Rôﬁ␀—∑@aäYJÙÿ@9ÛÅ◊€Ùà@t" ¿Éo@ÎÂ£Õ{,†@ÎÂ¬?BI60102044002@ÓÅ
