ergy emission mechanisms of these objects.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀MAG       Magnetars and Rotation-Powered Pulsars                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316HESSJ1640m465                                     @oGS&¬¿GB WßÜ¬@u# WßÜ¬?¿Aâ7K∆®@jC&¡Ω•@ÎËû"–Åı@ÎË¬Õ{,†30002021040@Èç␀bM”@È~GÄ4m∆@ÎPOv_Ÿ@ÎR~Ov_ŸSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬂ´H'qf␀␀‡Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will undertake a comprehensive program of observations of magnetars and rotation-powered pulsars, designed to study the surprising hard X-ray emission discovered by INTEGRAL from these objects and to shed light on the broad-band spectra between the soft X-ray and high-energy gamma-ray bands. With its sensitive hard X-ray response NuSTAR can extend the soft X-ray spectrum by an order of magnitude in energy, allowing detailed constraints on the high-energy emission mechanisms of these objects.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          