                                                                                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429IRAS_F17138m1017                                  ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÎÌÁÈÏÛº@ÎÌËîóûg60101076001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïﬂx¶N û␀␀‡ÎHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀˙With the unrivaled 10-30 keV sensitivity provided by NuSTAR, we propose a snapshot program to observe a volume-limited sample of 13 luminous infrared galaxies spread across the galaxy major merger sequence. When combined with archival NuSTAR data, these observations stand to place the strongest constraints to date on the timing of SMBH growth during galaxy evolution, effectively probing the potential accretion signatures from even Compton-thick AGN (going where Chandra could not).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Bauer                         Franz                         NULL               