                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Marshall                      Herman                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO                                                                                                                               ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                                                                                                                         ␀␀␀DDT                                                                                                                     archived  20200429Mrk817                                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÎÒéx>@ÎÒè?Zé⁄60160590001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏﬂfD’Ê¯␀␀ﬂíHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Mrk817                                            @ka|⁄Q@McCïÅ%@Y∆?@Jøe˝ä⁄∫@u≈]càeï@ÎÒè?Zé⁄@ÎÒû±!´L60160590002@’iqoiD@’Yâáì›ò@÷ÂÅ≤-V@÷Ê¡≤-VSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏﬂeÛ¨ê␀␀ﬂíHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                                                                                                                         ␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429M31_Field_A                                       ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÎÒû±!´L@ÎÒü[ÃU˜50110001001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏﬂeÀ¡Õ.␀␀·Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀äWe propose a 100 ks NuSTAR exposure for each of three fields along the M31 disk as a first step in long-term monitoring of X-ray Binary (XRB) populations to LX~6e36 erg/s (4-25 keV) in an environment similar to the Milky Way (MW). These three pointings will follow ~3-12 months after the initial NuSTAR observations planned during early 2015 to connect XRB variability from hour to year-long timescales. We will (1) study individual XRBs similar to those seen in the MW but with slightly different environments and star formation histories and (2) establish a baseline for long-term monitoring. NuSTAR observations are critical as the different XRB accretion states are distinguishable at E>10 keV and only subtly different at 0.5-10 keV.                                                              Normal galaxies                                             ␀1    Hornschemeier                 Ann                           NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       MONITORING THE X-RAY BINARY POPULATIONS OF THE M31 DISK WITH NUSTAR                                                     ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316M31_Field_A                                       @%√n.±ƒ3@D¶ÛMj@^JîFsÅÿ¿5ûäqﬁi≠@]∞1&Èx’@ÎÒü[ÃU˜@ÎÒƒw␀°50110001002@ÈÄp◊s@Èq®bM”@ÎKfæﬂ§@@ÎLK.HËßSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬂeb≥ƒ÷␀␀·Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀äWe propose a 100 ks NuSTAR exposure for each of three fields along the M31 disk as a first step in long-term monitoring of X-ray Binary (XRB) populations to LX~6e36 erg/s (4-25 keV) in an environment similar to the Milky Way (MW). These three pointings will follow ~3-12 months after the initial NuSTAR observations planned during early 2015 to connect XRB variability from hour to year-long timescales. We will (1) study individual XRBs similar to those seen in the MW but with slightly different environments and star formation histories and (2) establish a baseline for long-term monitoring. NuSTAR observations are critical as the different XRB accretion states are distinguishable at E>10 keV and only subtly different at 0.5-10 keV.                                                              Normal galaxies                                             ␀1    Hornschemeier                 Ann                           NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       MONITORING THE X-RAY BINARY POPULATIONS OF THE M31 DISK WITH NUSTAR                                                     ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                     Swift                                                                                               ␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429H1743m322                                         ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÎÒƒw␀°@ÎÒ≈?Zé⁄80002040003␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïﬂe1«r␀␀‡˝Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀˙@¡We propose a large multiwavelength campaign (120 ks Chandra HETGS, NuSTAR, INTEGRAL, JVLA/ATCA, Swift) on a black hole transient to study the influence of ionized winds on relativistic jets and state transitions. With a reimagined observing strategy based on new results on integrated RMS variability and a decade of radio/X-ray monitoring, we will search for winds before the state transition to test their influence on and track their coevolution with the disk and the jet over the next ~2 months.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Neilsen                       Joseph                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀␀C16       An Integrated Approach to Winds, Jets, and State Transitions                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316H1743m322                                         @p®úæﬂ§¿@!Œ_o“@vQ—∑X‚ø˙eîØOÑ@tIn.±ƒ3@ÎÒ≈?Zé⁄@ÎÒÿ"Ë«æ80002040004@€tÓô0æ@€Z]∏∫«@›Y+4÷°b@›Y+4÷°bSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏﬂdÌ„ÔP␀␀‡˝Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀˙@¡We propose a large multiwavelength campaign (120 ks Chandra HETGS, NuSTAR, INTEGRAL, JVLA/ATCA, Swift) on a black hole transient to study the influence of ionized winds on relativistic