¶º£¿=v»¥9X@v|Ä4m≈÷?¡å~($x@t∫8ÜYJı@ÎÛæx>@ÎÛﬁ?Zé⁄90101012002@Ê6‚Î@Â≈4÷°b@Ë-rsÅ◊‹@Ë-ÚsÅ◊‹SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏﬂFTz·H␀␀‡aHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Ponti                         Gabriele                      NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO                                                                                                                               ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                     Chandera Keck                                                                                       ␀␀␀ToO                                                                                                                     archived  20200429Mrk1040                                           ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÎÛﬁ?Zé⁄@ÎÛﬂîØ‰060101002001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏﬂF&OD␀␀·%Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀)The study of the X-ray spectral components in AGN allows us in principle to infer the properties of the accretion disk and in some cases, the black hole spin. This proposal concerns the study of the nearby, Xray bright Seyfert 1 galaxy, Mrk 1040, which shows the presence of an unusually intense and highly broadened (FWHM: 60000 km/s) Fe K line, as well as a strong hard X-ray excess above 10 keV. Mrk 1040 is also rapidly variable and shows a tentative detection of lags at soft X-rays. Here we request simultaneous XMM-Newton and NuSTAR observations (160 ks and 120 ks), enabling us to determine the origin of the hard X-ray excess and ultimately the spin of the central black hole. We will also determine the presence the X-ray lags above 10 keV, as expected in disc reverberation scenarios.     Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Reeves                        James                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀X14       A hard X-ray view of the inner disc in Mrk 1040                                                                         ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Mrk1040                                           @BâÖoiD@?VœAÚ◊@b>_ˆîF¿;F8ÜYJı@`Ø¶µ(@ÎÛﬂîØ‰0@ÎÙ"Ë«æ60101002002@Óº–¡Ω•@Ó∞r„º”[@ê—N;Õ@ì∞—N;ÕSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏﬂEµI2q␀␀·%Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀)The study of the X-ray spectral components in AGN allows us in principle to infer the properties of the accretion disk and in some cases, the black hole spin. This proposal concerns the study of the nearby, Xray bright Seyfert 1 galaxy, Mrk 1040, which shows the presence of an unusually intense and highly br