ided by NuSTAR, we propose a snapshot program to observe a volume-limited sample of 13 luminous infrared galaxies spread across the galaxy major merger sequence. When combined with archival NuSTAR data, these observations stand to place the strongest constraints to date on the timing of SMBH growth during galaxy evolution, effectively probing the potential accretion signatures from even Compton-thick AGN (going where Chandra could not).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Bauer                         Franz                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       WHEN IN THE MAJOR MERGER SEQUENCE IS (OBSCURED) BLACK HOLE GROWTH TRIGGERED?                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316MCGp08m18m013                                     @bΩ<64@H<2 Wßá@e7ä	ﬁ@Ghç∏∫«@h›Ä4m≈÷@Î˘AÍ9Ö@Î˘R"Ë«æ60101071002@‘∫cÀí:*@‘∑È=Ÿc@÷69´üUõ@÷:év»¥9SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬁ˘7ÿéö␀␀·=Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀˙With the unrivaled 10-30 keV sensitivity provided by NuSTAR, we propose a snapshot program to observe a volume-limited sample of 13 luminous infrared galaxies spread across the galaxy major merger sequence. When combined with archival NuSTAR data, these observations stand to place the strongest constraints to date on the timing of SMBH growth during galaxy evolution, effectively probing the potential accretion signatures from even Compton-thick AGN (going where Chandra could not).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Bauer                         Franz                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       WHEN IN THE MAJOR MERGER SEQUENCE IS (OBSCURED) BLACK HOLE GROWTH TRIGGERED?                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429IGRJ10447m6027                                    ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î˘R"Ë«æ@Î˘S?Zé⁄30161003001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïﬁ˘‚Ã␀␀ﬂŒHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. The goals of the Galactic Legacy Survey are to expose the hidden Milky Way and reveal the wide range of astrophysics that creates high-energy emission. The program will continue NuSTAR studies of flares from Sgr A*, HMXB in a range of environments, and diffuse emission toward the Galactic Center, including the Galactic ridge emission.                                                                                                                    