"É␀␀·QHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀) We propose to perform (as a ToO) a series of 4x10ks+2x40 ks joint XMM-Newton/NuSTAR observations (spaced by a few days) of a microquasar during its outburst decline phase to follow its broadband X-ray spectral evolution with an unprecedented precision. We will perform simultaneous radio, optical and IR observations to observe the reactivation of the jet. This will allow us i) to carefully investigate the physical/geometrical changes of the disc/corona system through the transition and ii) to reveal the drivers of the quenching/reappearance of the jets during the state transitions and how they connect to the properties of the accretion flow.                                                                                                                                                        Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Petrucci                      Pierre-Olivier                NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀X14       X-ray spectral evolution of microquasars during soft-to-hard state transitions                                          ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316GX339m4                                           @oı
=p£◊¿Hg‚Ç@∑Ä@u,ﬁi≠Bƒ¿ú∆?@u√"h	‘ï@Î˘·îØ‰0@Î˘˝"Ë«æ80102011012@‰.ºπıY¥@‰-ºãCïÅ@Â¯…Öo@Â˘P…ÖoSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏﬁÙà'qf␀␀·QHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀) We propose to perform (as a ToO) a series of 4x10ks+2x40 ks joint XMM-Newton/NuSTAR observations (spaced by a few days) of a microquasar during its outburst decline phase to follow its broadband X-ray spectral evolution with an unprecedented precision. We will perform simultaneous radio, optical and IR observations to observe the reactivation of the jet. This will allow us i) to carefully investigate the physical/geometrical changes of the disc/corona system through the transition and ii) to reveal the drivers of the quenching/reappearance of the jets during the state transitions and how they connect to the properties of the accretion flow.                                                                                                                                                        Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Petrucci                      Pierre-Olivier                NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀X14       X-ray spectral evolution of microquasars during soft-to-hard state transitions                                          ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429V0332p53                                          ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î˘˝"Ë«æ@Î˘˛x>80102002007␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏﬁÙZ[«ﬂ␀␀‡éHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀*;In spite of more than forty years of studies open questions remain on the structure and physical properties of the emission regions of accreting X-ray pulsars. Here, we propose to observe the transient X-ray pulsar V0332+53 with two 20ks pointings during the decline of an outburst with XMM-Newton and NuSTAR. These joint TOO observations will allow us to observe the source both in high and low luminosity states when the accretion regime and the emission region are expected to drastically change. The unique sensitivity and broadband coverage offered by a simultaneous XMM Newton/NuSTAR observations will allow a detailed spectral and timing analysis in both states. This is essential to constrain the properties of the emission region and the critical luminosity.                                 Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Doroshenko                    Victor                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀X14       Accretion column: from dawn till dusk                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316V0332p53                                          @J‡ê-‡@Jö	ﬁ␀“@b=≤-V¿r‰éäqﬁ@]◊8}øH@Î˘˛x>@Î˙w␀°80102002008@—¢íö‘,=@—…Îo“Û@‘˜Î=»K@‘˛k=»KSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏﬁÛ¯˚‘␀␀‡éHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀*;In spite of more than forty years of studies open questions remain on the structure and physical properties of the emission regions of accreting X-ray pulsars. Here, we propose to observe the transient X-ray pulsar V0332+53 with two 20ks pointings during the decline of an outburst with XMM-Newton and NuSTAR. These joint TOO observations will allow us to observe the source both in high and low luminosity states when the accretion regime and the emission region are expected to drastically change. The unique sensitivity and broadband coverage offered by a simultaneous XMM Newton/NuSTAR observations will allow a detailed spectral and timing analysis in both states. This is essential to constrain the properties of the emission region and the critical luminosity.                                 Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Doroshenko                    Victor                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀X14       Accretion column: from dawn till dusk                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              Swift                                                                                               ␀␀␀␀ToO (2/3)                                                                                                               archived  202004293C184d1                                           @\˜Æz·H@TcàeîØ@`±Êö‘,@<√©*0U2@e≤îFsÅÿ@Î˙w␀°@Î˙x>60160300001@w2C,•z@w!Àí:)«@x†␀␀␀␀␀@x†␀␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏﬁÛÃkµ™␀␀ﬂ÷Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                     