    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar flare                                                                                                                       ␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429IGRJ19378m0617                                    ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î˙Õìrh@Î˙±!´L60101003001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏﬁÛjz␀␀·LHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀)õWe propose to make a 120 ks XMM-Newton observation coordinated with NuSTAR of the little known NLS1, IGR J19378-0617, in order to probe a broad range of variability timescales in this extremely bright, low mass source. It has been observed with XMM-Newton for only 12 ks and is clearly detected in the BAT 70-month catalog. Despite its short exposure, this source shows several interesting features that require further exploration, including a low-frequency continuum lag, even hints of high-frequency reverberation,and a low-ionization warm absorber in the RGS. It is also a hard X-ray source that will clearly be detected by NuSTAR. Given its strong variability and high count rate, has potential to reveal time lags above 10 keV.                                                                   Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Kara                          Erin                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀X14       Reverberation in the bright NLS1, IGR J19378-0617                                                             