                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Bagnoli                       Tullio                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO                                                                                                                               ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                     XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀ToO                                                                                                                     archived  20200429Cyg_X1                                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î˙‘?Zé⁄@Î˙‘Í9Ö10102001001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏﬁÔä∂Õè␀␀ﬂÿHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Observations of celestial sources will be undertaken throughout the mission to determine, and then monitor changes to, the calibration of the X-ray observatory. Observations will enable the calibration of absolute flux, spectral sensitivity, point spread function, and the timing capabilities of the observatory as well as the observatory optical alignment. NuSTAR will also participate in cross-calibration campaigns with the Chandra, XMM-Newton, Swift, and Suzaku X-ray observatories.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Calibration Observations                                    ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀CAL       NuSTAR calibration campaign                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Cyg_X1                                            @r∏π#¢úx@AïIQÇ©ì@QÃ-‡q@	AÚ◊s@u:9XbN@Î˙‘Í9Ö@Î˙„?Zé⁄10102001002@«	{ã¨q@««˝+”√a@‘™Ó_ÿ≠¨@‘≠n_ÿ≠¨SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏﬁÓØ˘Óé␀␀ﬂÿHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀Observations of celestial sources will be undertaken throughout the mission to determine, and then monitor changes to, the calibration of the X-ray observatory. Observations will enable the calibration of absolute flux, spectral sensitivity, point spread function, and the timing capabilities of the observatory as well as the observatory optical alignment. NuSTAR will also participate in cross-calibration campaigns with the Chandra, XMM-Newton, Swift, and Suzaku X-ray observatories.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Calibration Observations                                    ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀CAL       NuSTAR calibration campaign                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                     ASTROSAT                                                                                            ␀␀␀Cross-calibration                                                                                                       archived  20200429Fornax_A_Offset                                   ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î˙„?Zé⁄@Î˙‰x>60101041003␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏﬁÓÜÎÊ6␀␀·KHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀=Radio lobes produced by AGN can strongly impact their environment, so it is important to understand the energetics of these systems. Radio synchrotron emission tells us the slope of the energy distribution, but the energy and magnetic field strength are degenerate. This degeneracy is broken if one also has the inverse Compton flux produced by scattering of CMB photons, which is visible in the hard X-rays. There are few systems with detected IC lobes and even fewer where one can measure changes in the spectral index as a function of position. We will make a hard X-ray spectral index map in the best target for this type of work, Fornax A, to map the particle energy and field strength in young and old plasma.                                                                                     Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Hodges-Kluck                  Edmund                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       A HARD X-RAY MAP OF THE NEARBY RADIO GALAXY FORNAX A                                                                    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Fornax_A_Offset                                   @IHÜYJÙÒ¿Bù2a|⁄@n
