the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316SMC_X2                                            @+}„º”[¿Rlz·GÆ@rÍ<ûÏø±¿E¨”ZÖáî@otSéÛM@Î˚|Í9Ö@Î˚ê"Ë«æ90102014004@÷Éó∂E°À@÷çcP∞Ú|@ÿ¡·0æÌ@ÿ«!0æÌSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏﬁÏè+ùe␀␀‡ùHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀ToO (2/2)                                                                                                               archived  20200429SWIFTJ1009d3m4250                                 ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î˚ê"Ë«æ@Î˚êÕìrh60061098001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏﬁÏfØ7¿␀␀ﬂÊHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316SWIFTJ1009d3m4250                                 @cX‚e¿Ed64Í@q[W>´6@%¢M“Ò©¸@_≠Dg8~@Î˚êÕìrh@Î˚üÕìrh60061098002@÷TΩ„Ω@÷FC]ÃcÒ@◊›8}ø@◊‹ì8}øSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏﬁÏi␀␀ﬂÊHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429GX_1p4                                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Î˚üÕìrh@Î˚†±!´L30101040001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏﬁÎˆlwŸ␀␀·THea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀¿We propose a 50 ks NuSTAR observation of the symbiotic X-ray binary GX 1+4. This source was one of the first sources found in the direction of the galactic center. This source is an accreting X-ray pulsar with a hard spectrum and it can sometimes reach many tens of mCrab (2-60 keV) in brightness. Little is known for certain about this source, in particular the neutron star magnetic field strength and the physics of the formation of its X-ray spectrum are not well understood. We will analyze the NuSTAR spectrum and place constraints on the magnetic field strength by comparing the observed spectrum with a Becker & Wolff model for the radiation-dominated, radiative shock in the magnetically funneled accretion flow.                                                                               Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Wolff                         Michael                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       NUSTAR OBSERVATIONS OF THE SYMBIOTIC BINARY GX 1+4                                                                      ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀               