            ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. One of the principal goals of the NuSTAR extragalactic surveys is to constrain the high-energy X-ray luminosity function and trace its evolution as a function of redshift and AGN obscuration. We will continue to pursue a multi-layer survey strategy, expanding the number of deep fields, and increasing the area of shallow observations through serendipitous sources.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀ELS       Extragalactic Legacy Surveys                                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  201503162MASXJ01392400p2924067                            @8“‰éäqﬁ@=b&ÄùIR@`‚§®¡T ¿@9Ë>BZÓ@u]l"h	’@Ï␀Á?Zé⁄@Ï␀ı±!´L60260012002@‘‘,$x@‘«Íêñº@÷8!ôôôö@÷9aôôôöSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬁ“A˝π␀␀‡Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. One of the principal goals of the NuSTAR extragalactic surveys is to constrain the high-energy X-ray luminosity function and trace its evolution as a function of redshift and AGN obscuration. We will continue to pursue a multi-layer survey strategy, expanding the number of deep fields, and increasing the area of shallow observations through serendipitous sources.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀ELS       Extragalactic Legacy Surveys                                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              Chandra                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀Extragalactic Legacy Survey                                                                                             archived  202004291ES_0414p009                                      ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï␀ı±!´L@Ï␀ˆ±!´L60101035001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïﬁ—ﬁoÄí␀␀·|Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀Some BLLacs are characterized by a hard intrinsic TeV spectrum irrespective of EBL absorption, locating the Compton peak above few TeV. This is difficult to reconcile with the typically softer spectrum of the synchrotron emission observed in these objects, for standard leptonic emission models and parameters. A different particle population might be responsible. We propose NuSTAR observations to pin down the synchrotron emission of these hard TeV electrons, either as a new hard component emerging in the hard X-ray band, or by constraining the synchrotron peak in the SED at the highest X-ray energies. The result can shed light on the origin of this hard TeV emission, as yet unexplained, and on the underlying acceleration mechanism.                                                            Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Costamante                    Luigi                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       UNVEILING THE ORIGIN OF THE HARD TEV EMISSION IN BLLACS                                                                 ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  201503161ES_0414p009                                      @PJ#9¿Ï?Ò=Ÿb∂Æ@g˜Í≥g†˘¿@™@∑Ä4n@m∏:)«yß@Ï␀ˆ±!´L@Ï±!´L60101035002@‡¬Y©˚Ám@‡∫qÙá¸π@·ﬁ4M:ì@·ﬁîM:ìSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬁ—z…Â␀␀·|Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀Some BLLacs are characterized by a hard intrinsic TeV spectrum irrespective of EBL absorption, locating the Compton peak above few TeV. This is difficult to reconcile with the typically softer spectrum of the synchrotron emission observed in these objects, for standard leptonic emission models and parameters. A different particle population might be responsible. We propose NuSTAR observations to pin down the synchrotron emission of these hard TeV electrons, either as a new hard component emerging in the hard X-ray band, or by constraining the synchrotron peak in the SED at the highest X-ray energies. The result can shed light on the origin of this hard TeV emission, as yet unexplained, and on the underlying acceleration mechanism.                                                            Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Costamante                    Luigi                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       UNVEILING THE ORIGIN OF THE HARD TEV EMISSION IN BLLACS                                                                 ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              Swift                                                                                               ␀␀␀ Additional exposure time in mode 06                                                                                    archived  202004292MASXJ09034285m7414170                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï±!´L@Ïx>60160346001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïﬁ—K©áe␀␀‡Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  201503162MASXJ09034285m7414170                            @`ˇ˘rGE9¿Ré($x@rπ#¢úx¿1ŒÊ1¯†ê@e˙z·GÆ@Ïx>@Ï,w␀°60160346002@–£èW>´6@–ó¢($x@—·KØ∑È@—·ãØ∑ÈSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬁ—ˆÂ’␀␀‡Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429LMC_X4                                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï,w␀°@Ï,[ÃU˜30102041007␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïﬁ–‚	‹Z␀␀·|Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀√We propose for a series of four 20ks observations with NuSTAR and Suzaku XIS of the binary X-ray pulsar LMC X-4. This source shows 13.5 s pulsations, a 1.4 d orbital period, and a long-period (~30 d) superorbital cycle due to a warped, precessing accretion disk. This disk is heated by the pulsed hard X-ray beam from the neutron star, and observations of this thermal emission can provide a unique probe of the inner accretion flow near the magnetosphere. However this requires sensitivity and timing resolution across the full X-ray band (from below 1 keV to above 20 keV), and full sampling of a full superorbital cycle. We will take advantage of NuSTAR's exquisite high-energy sensitivity in concert with Suzaku to yield the clearest picture to date of the inner accretion flow.                  Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Hickox                        Ryan                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       SUPERORBITAL VARIATION OF LMC X-4: EXPLORING THE INNER ACCRETION FLOW WITH NUSTAR AND SUZAKU                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316LMC_X4                                            @T—ﬁi≠Bƒ¿PòQÎÖ∏@qE´üUõ=¿@?€Ùá¸π@l3IQÇ©ì@Ï,[ÃU˜@Ï;[ÃU˜30102041008@”ŒáAÚ◊@”–ÏV’–@’Æg‡ﬁ“â@’Æg‡ﬁ“âSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬁ–ëAú¢␀␀·|