               ␀␀IC 443 is the best target to study SNR-MC interaction to its brightness and proximity. Yet, its complexity with several unidentified soft X-ray (<10 keV) sources as well as their unknown relationship with the GeV emission requires high-resolution hard X-ray (>10 keV) observation for a broadband SED study. Previous INTEGRAL observation was not able to resolve the hard X-ray source 1SAX J0618.0+2227 detected in the SNR-MC interaction site. Our simulation show that NuSTAR will able to resolve the hard X-ray source and obtain high resolution spectroscopy. It will be the first confirmation of hard X-ray emission due to SNR-MC interaction and sternly constrain the model parameters.This will also shed light on understanding of other hard X-ray sources in the other SNR-MC interaction systems.     Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Zhang                         Shuo                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       HARD X-RAY MORPHOLOGY AND SPECTROSCOPY OF THE INTERACTION SITE BETWEEN THE SUPERNOVA REMNANT IC 443 AND MOLECULAR CLOUD ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316XMMU_J061804d3p22273                              @W¢_o“ @6zπıY≥–@g§}øHÄ@·GÆz·@d,qﬁi≠C@ÏîØ‰0@Ï^îØ‰030101058002@¯Úö^û	@¯‚ë‚e,@˙∑œ:˚~ë@˙∏Ø:˚~ëSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬁ«e[f«␀␀·íHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀IC 443 is the best target to study SNR-MC interaction to its brightness and proximity. Yet, its complexity with several unidentified soft X-ray (<10 keV) sources as well as their unknown relationship with the GeV emission requires high-resolution hard X-ray (>10 keV) observation for a broadband SED study. Previous INTEGRAL observation was not able to resolve the hard X-ray source 1SAX J0618.0+2227 detected in the SNR-MC interaction site. Our simulation show that NuSTAR will able to resolve the hard X-ray source and obtain high resolution spectroscopy. It will be the first confirmation of hard X-ray emission due to SNR-MC interaction and sternly constrain the model parameters.This will also shed light on understanding of other hard X-ray sources in the other SNR-MC interaction systems.     Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Zhang                         Shuo                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       HARD X-RAY MORPHOLOGY AND SPECTROSCOPY OF THE INTERACTION SITE BETWEEN THE SUPERNOVA REMNANT IC 443 AND MOLECULAR CLOUD ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                                                                                                                         ␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  202004294Cp50d11                                          ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï^îØ‰0@Ï_x>60160177001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïﬁ«,¿©Ë␀␀‡#Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  201503164Cp50d11                                          @MÎ=»K^@I{9¿ÎÌ˙@b»¨1'ø¸B√…ÓÀ˚@8‡␀␀␀␀␀@Ï_x>@Ïm[ÃU˜60160177002@‘k©*0U@‘â-w1ê@’Ä3nóç@’Ç≥nóçSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬁ∆ÓEs␀␀‡#Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                                                                                                                         ␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429NGC7469                                           ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ïm[ÃU˜@Ïn"Ë«æ60101001005␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïﬁ∆»?∑/␀␀·ßHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀)Using a multiwavelength campaign on NGC 7469, led by XMM-Newton, HST, Swift, NuSTAR, and optical, we propose to achieve new physical insights into the enigmatic AGN winds, by obtaining the deepest ever RGS spectrum of this highly accreting source. It will allow us to determine the accurate ionisation and chemical structure of the wind. Using EPIC and RGS, we will measure the response of the outflow to continuum variations, which combined with HST/COS data will unambiguously determine the location, and abundances of the outflow components.Our team pioneered this approach, and applied it successfully (14 refereed papers) to Mrk 509 that featured only a multi-year response. The unique properties of NGC 7469 make it the ideal candidate to respond on shorter, better-monitored time scales.      Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Behar                         Ehud                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀X14       Tracking Down the Ionized Outflow of NGC 7469                                                                           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316NGC7469                                           @uú…„Ω@!¥SéÛMj@T±œ™ÕûÑ¿F∑lãCïÅ@sfQŒ_@Ïn"Ë«æ@Ï~Í9Ö60101001006@’˛ ∑Ä4n@’Û·Ω•ù@◊≤QûÉ‰&@◊¥ûÉ‰&SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬁ∆ÇsK␀␀·ßHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀)Using a multiwavelength campaign on NGC 7469, led by XMM-Newton, HST, Swift, NuSTAR, and optical, we propose to achieve new physical insights into the enigmatic AGN winds, by obtaining the deepest ever RGS spectrum of this highly accreting source. It will allow us to determine the accurate ionisation and chemical structure of the wind. Using EPIC and RGS, we will measure the response of the outflow to continuum variations, which combined with HST/COS data will unambiguously determine the location, and abundances of the outflow components.Our team pioneered this approach, and applied it successfully (14 refereed papers) to Mrk 509 that featured only a multi-year response. The unique properties of NGC 7469 make it the ideal candidate to respond on shorter, better-monitored time scales.      Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Behar                         Ehud                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀X14       Tracking Down the Ionized Outflow of NGC 7469                                                                           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM HST                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀(3/7)                                                                                                                   archived  20200429IRAS00397m1312                                    ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï~Í9Ö@Ï[ÃU˜60101038001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïﬁ∆[F␀␀·íHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀The relative role of stellar emission and black-hole accretion, as mechanisms of energy production in the Universe, and their interconnection are two of the most debated topics of modern astrophysics. We propose here a 100 Ksec NuStar observation of IRAS00397-1312, the most luminous starburst in the local (z<0.3) Universe. The hard (E>10 keV) X-ray data will be unique to unveil the putative AGN component, never detected in the X-ray domain, and will allow us to delineate the intrinsic Lx and the column density of the obscuring matter. Complemented with the wealth of data at other wavelengths, the NuStar data will be fundamental to describe the circum-nuclear absorbing matter and to compare the AGN emission with the starburst emission.                                                        Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Della Ceca                    Roberto                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       PROBING COMCOMITANT STARBURST-AGN ACTIVITY: THE MOST LUMINOUS STARBURST IN THE LOCAL UNIVERSE                           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316IRAS00397m1312                                    @%wökP±¿)Ì≈÷8ÜY@\B^5?|Ó¿RÓ{≤˛≈m@s<á¸π#£@Ï[ÃU˜@Ï»w␀°60101038002@˘•ïÈ·±@˘@Ñµ‹∆@˙⁄Vﬁi≠C@˙€Fﬁi≠CSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬁ≈»'qf␀