ised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                                                                                                                         ␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429IRAS_F00183m7111                                  @ï*ô0æ¿Q∫¯7¥¢4@s)ƒõ•„T¿FÚ·GÆ{@ty¶µ@Ï-[ÃU˜@Ï-Í9Ö60101050001@sPﬁ“àŒp@sHÜYJÙÒ@tê␀␀␀␀␀@tê␀␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïﬁ√8j1N␀␀‚Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀¡We propose a 100 ks NuSTAR observation of the ultra-luminous infrared galaxy IRAS F00183-7111 at z=0.327. The mid-IR spectrum of this galaxy is characterized by deep silicate absorption and the previous X-ray observation showed that a Compton thick AGN is present in the ULIRG and dominates the large output. We aim at detecting absorbed primary emission of the obscured nucleus and a measurement of the hard X-ray spectrum above 10 keV.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Iwasawa                       Kazushi                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       FIRE UNDER ICE: ULIRG IRAS F00183-7111                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20200429IRAS_F00183m7111                                  @[•„S˜œ¿Qºò_ˆî@s*z·GÆ¿FÔE8Ô4◊@t–|Ñµ›@Ï-Í9Ö@ÏLÕìrh60101050002@Îïûúwök@ÎàÃ‘,<ü@Ìz|h€ã¨@Ì{‹h€ã¨SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬁ¬ﬂ#E␀␀‚Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀¡We propose a 100 ks NuSTAR observation of the ultra-luminous infrared galaxy IRAS F00183-7111 at z=0.327. The mid-IR spectrum of this galaxy is characterized by deep silicate absorption and the previous X-ray observation showed that a Compton thick AGN is present in the ULIRG and dominates the large output. We aim at detecting absorbed primary emission of the obscured nucleus and a measurement of the hard X-ray spectrum above 10 keV.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Iwasawa                       Kazushi                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       FIRE UNDER ICE: ULIRG IRAS F00183-7111                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429NGC7469                                           ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏLÕìrh@ÏMîØ‰060101001007␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïﬁ¬≤qÓ␀␀·ßHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀)Using a multiwavelength campaign on NGC 7469, led by XMM-Newton, HST, Swift, NuSTAR, and optical, we propose to achieve new physical insights into the enigmatic AGN winds, by obtaining the deepest ever RGS spectrum of this highly accreting source. It will allow us to determine the accurate ionisation and chemical structure of the wind. Using EPIC and RGS, we will measure the response of the outflow to continuum variations, which combined with HST/COS data will unambiguously determine the location, and abundances of the outflow components.Our team pioneered this approach, and applied it successfully (14 refereed papers) to Mrk 509 that featured only a multi-year response. The unique properties of NGC 7469 make it the ideal candidate to respond on shorter, better-monitored time scales.      Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Behar     