 Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316IGRJ12391m1612                                    @gπ…ÓÀ˚¿0+Ö∏QÏ@r•√a@O@GV5?|Ìë@fyiDg8@ÏIx>@ÏX?Zé⁄60061232002@‘⁄/ˆ+jË@‘–$†ê-‡@÷LÑÃÃÃÕ@÷MÑÃÃÃÕSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬁ¥1˜®␀␀‡AHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429J143459d27m014432d8                               ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏX?Zé⁄@ÏX±!´L60101083001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïﬁ¥HpC␀␀·∂Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀One of the major science drivers of NuSTAR is to uncover the growth of supermassive black holes that are hidden behind large columns of gas and dust, and a particular focus is the powerful obscured quasars that have previously proven difficult to detect and characterize. Here we propose to observe a sample of four quasars, selected based on mid-IR photometry from WISE and SDSS, that represent the "typical" obscured quasar population and complement previous studies of specific quasar subsets with more complicated selection effects. These 126 ks total observations will use NusTAR's high-energy sensitivity to provide the best measurements of heavy obscuration in "typical" mid-IR selected quasars, and constrain their contributions to the hard cosmic X-ray background.                           Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Hickox                        Ryan                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       THE SEARCH FOR EXTREME ABSORPTION IN ``TYPICAL'' WISE-SELECTED OBSCURED QUASARS                                         ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316J143459d27m014432d8                               @kXò_ˆîø˚πıY≥–}@uªª/ÏV÷@J!-w2@eÚ%ÆÊ1˘@ÏX±!´L@ÏuÍ9Ö60101083002@‰oH¬&Äù@‰cñm≈÷9@Âﬂ®1&È@Â‡»1&ÈSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬁ≥µ0Ï®␀␀·∂Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀One of the major science drivers of NuSTAR is to uncover the growth of supermassive black holes that are hidden behind large columns of gas and dust, and a particular focus is the powerful obscured quasars that have previously proven difficult to detect and characterize. Here we propose to observe a sample of four quasars, selected based on mid-IR photometry from WISE and SDSS, that represent the "typical" obscured quasar population and complement previous studies of specific quasar subsets with more complicated selection effects. These 126 ks total observations will use NusTAR's high-energy sensitivity to provide the best measurements of heavy obscuration in "typical" mid-IR selected quasars, and constrain their contributions to the hard cosmic X-ray background.                           Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Hickox                        Ryan                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       THE SEARCH FOR EXTREME ABSORPTION IN ``TYPICAL'' WISE-SELECTED OBSCURED QUASARS                                         ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  202004292MASXJ10195855m0234363                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏuÍ9Ö@ÏvîØ‰060260015001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïﬁ≥à—Y‚␀␀‡AHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. One of the principal goals of the NuSTAR extragalactic surveys is to constrain the high-energy X-ray luminosity function and trace its evolution as a function of redshift and AGN obscuration. We will continue to pursue a multi-layer survey strategy, expanding the number of deep fields, and increasing the area of shallow observations through serendipitous sources.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀ELS       Extragalactic Legacy Surveys                                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                