ˇü␀␀·“Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀˙With the unrivaled 10-30 keV sensitivity provided by NuSTAR, we propose a snapshot program to observe a volume-limited sample of 13 luminous infrared galaxies spread across the galaxy major merger sequence. When combined with archival NuSTAR data, these observations stand to place the strongest constraints to date on the timing of SMBH growth during galaxy evolution, effectively probing the potential accretion signatures from even Compton-thick AGN (going where Chandra could not).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Bauer                         Franz                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       WHEN IN THE MAJOR MERGER SEQUENCE IS (OBSCURED) BLACK HOLE GROWTH TRIGGERED?                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316IRAS_F18293m3413                                  @qc¡Ω•¿Aˆ˝!ˇ.?± [¿6„¿&>≈m\˙≠@a„∏QÎÖ@Ï“x>@Ï·"Ë«æ60101077002@’BÆ°a‰˜@’3␀h€å@÷¢p}øH@÷¢p}øHSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏﬁöyD•[␀␀·“Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀˙With the unrivaled 10-30 keV sensitivity provided by NuSTAR, we propose a snapshot program to observe a volume-limited sample of 13 luminous infrared galaxies spread across the galaxy major merger sequence. When combined with archival NuSTAR data, these observations stand to place the strongest constraints to date on the timing of SMBH growth during galaxy evolution, effectively probing the potential accretion signatures from even Compton-thick AGN (going where Chandra could not).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Bauer                         Franz                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       WHEN IN THE MAJOR MERGER SEQUENCE IS (OBSCURED) BLACK HOLE GROWTH TRIGGERED?                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429UDS_MOS015                                        ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï·"Ë«æ@Ï‚?Zé⁄60111015001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïﬁö(ı¬è␀␀‡dHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. One of the principal goals of the NuSTAR extragalactic surveys is to constrain the high-energy X-ray luminosity function and trace its evolution as a function of redshift and AGN obscuration. We will continue to pursue a multi-layer survey strategy, expanding the number of deep fields, and increasing the area of sha