␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏﬁL˝X^␀␀‚Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀We propose three short (25 ks) observations of the super-Eddington neutron-star low-mass X-ray binary GX 5-1. The properties of super-Eddington accretion flows onto neutron stars are still poorly understood. The aim of our observations is to test proposed models for the spectral evolution in this type of source, by simultaneously constraining the continuum and reflection features (in particular the Fe line) in the spectrum. NuSTAR is uniquely capable of doing so. By observing GX 5-1 we also complete NuSTAR's coverage of neutron-star low-mass X-ray binaries across the entire luminosity range of this class, allowing for a detailed comparison between subclasses.                                                                                                                                     Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Homan                         Jeroen                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       THE SUPER-EDDINGTON ACCRETION FLOW IN GX 5-1                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316GX_5m1                                            @p‰ÛMj¿9<64@:í£SøÍï*ô0æ@cbd¬¯7µ@Ï·Í9Ö@ÏÙÍ9Ö30102056002@≈»‰õ•„T@∆ÿ$•zxl@€éËßÁ@€ç‹ËßÁSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬁ}ÍIìà␀␀‚Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀We propose three short (25 ks) observations of the super-Eddington neutron-star low-mass X-ray binary GX 5-1. The prop