ü␀␀·ZHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will be able to observe solar hard X-ray sources 200 times fainter than our current capabilities allow. This increase in sensitivity will open the door to truly pioneering observations, providing diagnostics for solar flare and, in particular, for nanoflare observations. Almost as important is NuSTAR's advantage in dynamic range, the ability to see a faint source (e.g. coronal source at the reconnection point) at the same time as a brighter one (e.g. source at the magnetic footpoint of a flare).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     Solar System Objects                                        ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀SOL       Solar Observations + Solar Axions                                                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Sol_16113_AR2532_1                                ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏñîØ‰0@Ïó"Ë«æ20101015001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬁduyæ␀␀·ZHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will be able to observe solar hard X-ray sources 200 times fainter than our current capabilities allow. This increase in sensitivity will open the door to truly pioneering observat