g absorbed primary emission of the obscured nucleus and a measurement of the hard X-ray spectrum above 10 keV.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Iwasawa                       Kazushi                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N01       FIRE UNDER ICE: ULIRG IRAS F00183-7111                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316IRAS_F00183m7111                                  @ÑÍJåM¿QπÖoiD@s*	‘ï+¿FÙ”ZÖáî@WQ7K∆ß@ÏîØ‰0@Ï:[ÃU˜60101050004@È∂,_ˆî@È®¶tSéÛ@ÎÄ˘€"—@ÎÑ–˘€"—SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬁ_é ÜB␀␀‚Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀¡We propose a 100 ks NuSTAR observation of the ultra-luminous infrared galaxy IRAS F00183-7111 at z=0.327. The mid-IR spectrum of this galaxy is characterized by deep silicate absorption and the previous X-ray observation showed that a Compton thick AGN is present in the ULIRG and dominates the large output. We aim at detecting absorbed primary emission of the obscured nucleus and a measurement of the hard X-ray spectrum above 10 keV.                                                                                                                                                                      