                  Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316WKK1263                                           @gÀüUõ=¿LÔ™ÕûÉ‰@r◊ë—N;Õ@9XbM”@qjsÅ◊€ı@Ï:Í9Ö@ÏFw␀°60160510002@œ˙¬üæv…@œÔ◊lãCñ@—§ËßÁ@—§ËßÁSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬁ_!/hL␀␀‡©Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429NGC_7582                                          ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏFw␀°@ÏFÕìrh60201003001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïﬁ^¯öºﬂ␀␀‚+Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀1¿We request a 90ks simultaneous XMM-Newton/NuSTAR observation of NGC7582 in order to quantify the Compton reflection and absorption variability. Previous measurements of the exceptionally strong reflection features have suffered from lack of high-quality data above 10 keV, preventing robust comparisons between observations. Additionally, NGC7582 has undergone recent spectral changes which could be due to a decrease in the average luminosity of the source or increased obscuration. Thus far, X-ray spectral investigations have been unable to fully break the degeneracy between these two models, however monitoring of the variability of the spectral components will help to distinguish which scenario best describes the geometry of circumnuclear material in this source.                             Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Rivers                        Elizabeth                     NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀X15       Probing for Variable Reflection and Absorption in NGC 7582                                                              ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316NG