.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀ToO                                                                                                                     archived  20200429SWIFT_J1416d9m4640                                ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï´x>@Ï¨w␀°60201033001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏÁb\¢RÆ␀␀‚4Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀UHeavily obscured accretion is believed to represent an extremely important phase in the growth of supermassive black holes, and to play an important role in shaping the observed spectrum of the Cosmic X-ray Background. So far however, only a small number of Compton-thick AGN are known. Our group recently carried out a detailed study of ~830 Swift/BAT AGN, finding CT absorption in 55 objects. We propose here to observe 28 local CT AGN with NuSTAR, with the aim of accurately constraining their column density and luminosity. This will allow us to sample the low and high-luminosity bins of CT accretion, as well as the NH> 5e24 cm^-2 range. With this we will study the luminosity-function of CT AGN, and the evolution of CT material with the physical characteristics of the accreting system.      Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Ricci                         Claudio                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N02       Compton-Thick Accretion In The Local Universe With NuSTAR                                                               ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316SWIFT_J1416d9m4640                                @j»v»¥9X¿G[)^û	@s€VlÙ!@+ïÅ$›/@ráπå~($@Ï¨w␀°@Ï∫Õìrh60201033002@’Äá¸π$@‘˛:í£@÷afcä	@÷afcä	SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏÁb~KÂ␀␀‚4Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀UHeavily obscured accretion is believed to represent an extremely important phase in the growth of supermassive black holes, and to play an important role in shaping the observed spectrum of the Cosmic X-ray Background. So far however, only a small number of Compton-thick AGN are known. Our group recently carried out a detailed study of ~830 Swift/BAT AGN, finding CT absorption in 55 objects. We propose here to observe 28 local CT AGN with NuSTAR, with the aim of accurately constraining their column density and luminosity. This will allow us to sample the low and high-luminosity bins of CT accretion, as well as the NH> 5e24 cm^-2 range. With this we will study the luminosity-function of CT AGN, and the evolution of CT material with the physical characteristics of the accreting system.      Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Ricci                         Claudio                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N02       Compton-Thick Accretion In The Local Universe With NuSTAR                                                               ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429SWIFT_J2242d4m3711                                ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï∫Õìrh@Ïª±!´L60201039001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏÁb≤âJ∑␀␀‚4Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀UHeavily obscured accretion is believed to represent an extremely important phase in the growth of supermassive black holes, and to play an important role in shaping the observed spectrum of the Cosmic X-ray Background. So far however, only a small number of Compton-thick AGN are known. Our group recently carried out a detailed study of ~830 Swift/BAT AGN, finding CT absorption in 55 objects. We propose here to observe 28 local CT AGN with NuSTAR, with the aim of accurately constraining their column density and luminosity. This will allow us to sample the low and high-luminosity bins of CT accretion, as well as the NH> 5e24 cm^-2 range. With this we will study the luminosity-function of CT AGN, and the evolution of CT material with the physical characteristics of the accreting system.      Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Ricci                         Claudio                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N02       Compton-Thick Accretion In The Local Universe With NuSTAR                                                               ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                           