survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                                                                                                                         ␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429IRAS_13224m3809                                   ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï9"Ë«æ@Ï:"Ë«æ60202001001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï›¶Vê‡Ö␀␀·Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀0ËThe Narrow-Line Seyfert 1 galaxy IRAS13224-3809 shows strong iron-K and L broad lines and high-frequency soft X-ray time lags indicating reflection from the innermost regions about a rapidly spinning black hole. It persistently varies with high amplitude changes every 2 to 3 days. The peak frequency and energy spectrum of the lags varies with flux, probably due to changes in size of the corona. We propose a Very Large Programme consisting of a 1.5Ms observation of this object, which will enable the full range of flux levels to be studied, yielding a dynamic picture of the changing height and size of the corona and transforming our understanding of how luminous black hole accretion operates.                                                                                                     Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Fabian                        Andrew                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀X15        Mapping the inner accretion flow: dynamic reverberation in IRAS 13224-3809                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316IRAS_13224m3809                                   @i*©*0U¿C7OÑM@s_◊€Ùá˝@8@∑Ä4n@uÙ„S˜ŒŸ@Ï:"Ë«æ@Ïnx>60202001002@Ç4•ú‡@{àÙá¸π@ÒΩÙjO@Ò¿§jOSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï›•ﬂb:h␀␀·Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀0ËThe Narrow-Line Seyfert 1 galaxy IRAS13224-3809 shows strong iron-K and L broad lines and high-frequency soft X-ray time lags indicating reflection from the innermost regions about a rapidly spinning black hole. It persistently varies with high amplitude changes every 2 to 3 days. The peak frequency and energy spectrum of the lags varies with flux, probably due to changes in size of the corona. We propose a Very Large Programme consisting of a 1.5Ms observation of this object, which will enable the full range of flux levels to be studied, yielding a dynamic picture of the changing height and size of the corona and transforming our understanding of how luminous black hole accretion operates.                                                                                                     Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Fabian                        Andrew                        NULL               