      ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429NGC_3783                                          ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï"»?Zé⁄@Ï"»îØ‰060101110001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï›4 "‰␀␀‚áHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ÊWe propose a simultaneous observation of the Seyfert 1 AGN NGC 3783 with Chandra (160 ks) and NuSTAR (80 ks). Our primary aim is to address the highly disparate measurements of supermassive black hole spin in this source that have been reported in the literature. The high signal-to-noise (S/N), high resolution, broadband X-ray spectra uniquely enabled by this joint observing campaign will allow us to definitively deconvolve the primary continuum, absorption and reprocessed emission components in NGC 3783 for the first time. The signatures of relativistic reflection from the inner disk can then be isolated and the spin of the black hole measured accurately and precisely.                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Brenneman                     Laura                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀C17       A Long Look at NGC 3783 with Chandra/HETG and NuSTAR                                                                    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316NGC_3783                                          @e◊'ª/ÏW¿B‹á¸π#£@qÛ¥¢3ú@6˝≈÷8ÜY@B¡Ω•ù@Ï"»îØ‰0@Ï"Ëx>60101110002@‰&|Ìëh@‰z˘	k∫@Â´ üæv…@ÂÆ†üæv…SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï›3√„-"␀␀‚áHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ÊWe propose a simultaneous observation of the Seyfert 1 AGN NGC 3783 with Chandra (160 ks) and NuSTAR (80 ks). Our primary aim is to address the highly disparate measurements of supermassive black hole spin in this source that have been reported in the literature. The high signal-to-noise (S/N), high resolution, broadband X-ray spectra uniquely enabled by this joint observing campaign will allow us to definitively deconvolve the primary continuum, absorption and reprocessed emission components in NGC 3783 for the first time. The signatures of relativistic reflection from the inner disk can then be isolated and the spin of the black hole measured accurately and precisely.                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Brenneman                     Laura                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀C17       A Long Look at NGC 3783 with Chandra/HETG and NuSTAR                                                                    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              Chandra                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀(1/2)                                                                                                                   archived  20200429Circinus_ULX5                                     ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï"Ëx>@Ï"ËÍ9Ö90201034001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï›3ôˆÊ␀␀·”Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Non-Proposal ToOs 