                         ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. One of the principal goals of the NuSTAR extragalactic surveys is to constrain the high-energy X-ray luminosity function and trace its evolution as a function of redshift and AGN obscuration. We will continue to pursue a multi-layer survey strategy, expanding the number of deep fields, and increasing the area of shallow observations through serendipitous sources.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀ELS       Extragalactic Legacy Surveys                                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316UDS_MOS033                                        @AR@∑Ä4n¿⁄QŒ@e9Æz·H¿MÓœAÚ◊@foﬁ␀—∑@Ï(Õìrh@Ï(@±!´L60111033002@ÁŸëÜ¬&Å@Á»Ù8ÜYK@ÈàÕì›óˆ@ÈâMì›óˆSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï›´<M^␀␀·QHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. One of the principal goals of the NuSTAR extragalactic surveys is to constrain the high-energy X-ray luminosity function and trace its evolution as a function of redshift and AGN obscuration. We will continue to pursue a multi-layer survey strategy, expanding the number of deep fields, and increasing the area of shallow observations through serendipitous sources.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀ELS       Extragalactic Legacy Surveys                                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                                                                                                                         ␀␀␀Extragalactic Legacy Survey / Kp=5                                                                                      archived  202004293C_382                                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï(@±!´L@Ï(Bw␀°60202015007␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï›{ÏGM␀␀‚øHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ÁWe propose a joint NuSTAR/XMM monitoring of the broad-line radio galaxy (BLRG) 3C 382, consisting of 5x20 ks observations spaced by 10-15 days. 3C 382 is an ideal radio-loud source to obtain high sensitivity measurements over a broad (UV/hard X-rays) high-energy range, which will allow us to: 1) study the UV/X-ray spectrum of a BLRG with unprecedented accuracy and test physically motivated Comptonization models, 2) understand the origin of the puzzling reflection component, and 3) investigate the nature of the soft X-ray excess. These observations will allow for a direct comparison with radio-quiet Seyfert 1s, in particular with a similar, successful NuSTAR/XMM monitoring of NGC 4593.                                                                                                           Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Ursini                        Francesco                     NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N02       NuSTAR/XMM Monitoring Of The Broad-Line Radio Galaxy 3C 382                                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  201503163C_382                                            @qkÔ4÷°b@@W
