TAR extragalactic surveys is to constrain the high-energy X-ray luminosity function and trace its evolution as a function of redshift and AGN obscuration. We will continue to pursue a multi-layer survey strategy, expanding the number of deep fields, and increasing the area of shallow observations through serendipitous sources.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀ELS       Extragalactic Legacy Surveys                                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀Extragalactic Legacy Survey                                                                                             archived  20200429NGC_1052                                          ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï5?î»)¯@Ï5@èFj60201056001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‹Ëﬁá∆Z␀␀„ Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ÃWe propose a 60 ks NuSTAR observation of NGC 1052 with simultaneous XMM-Newton coverage in order to accurately model the reflection features in this source. NGC 1052 is a LINER with a low Eddington rate that has shown hints of a broad Fe Ka line but no Compton reflection hump in the past. A short NuSTAR observation of the source, indicated that there may indeed be Compton reflection in this source and a harder continuum than previously thought. Unfortunately, lack of statistics and low resolution in the Fe K bandpass of the current data negate the possibility of a robust measurement. A longer broadband observation will allow us to robustly measure the reflection signatures and simultaneous XMM coverage will allow us to carefully and consistently test for relativistic reflection.           Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Rivers                        Elizabeth                     NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N02       Testing For Relativistic Reflection In Ngc 1052                                                                         ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316NGC_1052                                          @D ñªò«„¿ êâ†'RT@fº±ƒ2 X¿Mj~˘€#@sÜ␀—∑Y@Ï5@èFj@Ï5j±9Ò60201056002@Ì-Hûö@Ì{&¡æ@ÔT4=p£◊@ÔVÙ=p£◊SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï‹Ëmjíe␀␀„ Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀ÃWe propose a 60 ks NuSTAR observation of NGC 1052 with simultaneous XMM-Newton coverage in order to accurately model the reflection features in this source. NGC 1052 is a LINER with a low Eddington rate that has shown hints of a broad Fe Ka line but no Compton reflection hump in the past. A short NuSTAR observation of the source, indicated that there may indeed be Compton reflection in this source and a harder continuum than previously thought. Unfortunately, lack of statistics and low resolution in the Fe K bandpass of the current data negate the possibility of a robust measurement. A longer broadband observation will allow us to robustly measure the reflection signatures and simultaneous XMM coverage will allow us to carefully and consistently test for relativistic reflection.           Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Rivers                        Elizabeth                     NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N02       Testing For Relativistic Reflection In Ngc 1052                                                                         ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429Mrk595                                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï5j±9Ò@Ï5kèFj60160119001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‹Ë<ñ/…␀␀·≤Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                    