 ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429CXOJ022727d5p333443                               ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï5y±9Ò@Ï5z#Ü30201003001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‹Á’=ç␀␀„]Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀2sA sub-sample of bright Ultraluminous X-ray Sources (L X~(1-5)x10^40 erg/s) shows peculiar powerlaw like spectra, with no high energy turn-off and short-term variability at the level of ~10%. These sources might host Intermediate Mass Black Holes (IMBHs) in a low/hard state, although their apparently flat spectral shape may be the effect of poor counting statistics. Here we propose simultaneous, deep XMMNewton and NuSTAR observations of four such objects to find evidence either of the X-ray properties (powerlaw spectra and short term variability) that should characterize sub-Eddington accretion onto an IMBH or of the characteristic spectral curvature of the `Ultraluminous state'.                                                                                                                 Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Pintore                       Fabio                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀X15       Searching for IMBH candidates among Ultraluminous X-ray Sources                                                         ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316CXOJ022727d5p333443                               @Bk•„S˜œ@@∆4ÍK@b}øHÃ¿9Y¿ÎÌ˙D@t˚ÁlãD@Ï5z#Ü@Ï5óî»)¯30201003002@‰”`ûö@‰ƒóLò_