506d47p03                                ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï8àÕ´∏1@Ï8â?r‘£60201044001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‹ŸXÔ±␀␀„<Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀{Flat-spectrum radio-loud narrow line Seyfert 1 galaxies (F-RLNLS1s) define a newly discovered class of AGNs that appears to occupy a distinct locus in the parameter space of AGNs. They add a third dimension to the eigenvector-1 defined by black hole mass and accretion rate, with inclusion of BH spin. In models of scale-invariant disk-jet emission, radio emission defines the jet power while X-ray emission defines the accretion disk emission. The observed properties of F-RLNLS1s appear to defy this universality. The NuSTAR energy range of 3--79 keV is of particular interest as we expect it to reveal the physics of the ``disk-jet connection'' by probing accretion disk emission as well as relativistic jet emission. We propose NuSTAR observations of 3 F-RLNLS1s, 2 of which are gamma-ray loud.  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Mathur                        Smita                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N02       Unexplored Parameter Space Of Flat-Spectrum Radio-Loud Narrow-Line Seyfert-1 Galaxies And The Disk-Jet Connection       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316SDSS_J150506d47p03                                @lIº£n/@¶L/É{J@FsÅ◊‹@I9a‰˜e˛@d·è≈Åo@Ï8â?r‘£@Ï8‹±9Ò60201044002@¸/}o“Û@¸ﬂó$tT@˛3ë	‘ï@˛5!	‘ïSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï‹ÿ∏!_Ù␀␀„<Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                            