d Quasars                                 ␀1    Wong                          Ka-Wah                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N02       Completing A Missing Chapter In Hard X-Ray Of The M87 AGN                                                               ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316M87                                               @gw*0U2a@(‘˝Û∂E¢@qØI∫^5?@R¢Ê1¯†ê@cÂkπå~(@Ï8ÌÍM@Ï9[‰õø60201016002@ËîÀ\(ı√@ËÅªGÆ{@Ítœ@N§©@ÍuO@N§©SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï‹◊µíÀ␀␀„<Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀ËM87 hosts a 3-6 billion solar mass black hole with an exceptional relativistic jet. It has been regularly monitored in radio to TeV bands. However, four orders of magnitude of energy from ~10 keV to 100 MeV is missing from the central s relativistic particle population is eventually injected into the interstellar medium (ISM), co                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Wong                          Ka-Wah                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N02       Completing A Missing Chapter In Hard X-Ray Of The M87 AGN                                                               ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              Chandra                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429SWIFT_J0919d2p5528                                ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï9[‰õø@Ï9#Ü60201036001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‹◊àπ␀␀„<Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀UHeavily obscured accretion is believed to represent an extremely important phase in the growth of supermassive black holes, and to play an important role in shaping the observed spectrum of the Cosmic X-ray Background. So far however, only a small number of Compton-thick AGN are known. Our group recently carried out a detailed study of ~830 Swift/BAT AGN, finding CT absorption in 55 objects. We propose here to observe 28 local CT AGN with NuSTAR, with the aim of accurately constraining their column density and luminosity. This will allow us to sample the low and high-luminosity bins of CT accretion, as well as the NH> 5e24 cm^-2 range. With this we will study the luminosity-function of CT AGN, and the evolution of CT material with the physical characteristics of the accreting system.      Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Ricci                         Claudio                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N02       Compton-Thick Accretion In The Local Universe With NuSTAR                                                               ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                        