            ␀␀âMulti-year and multi-frequency monitoring of the classical TeV blazars Mrk 421 and Mrk 501 is an important resource in the effort to understand the physics of relativistic jets. These objects are among the very small number of sources whose broadband SED can be characterized simultaneously by the currently existing instruments. We request NuSTAR observations as a part of two planned campaigns in 2016 and 2017 on these two objects. Only NuSTAR is sensitive enough to provide time-resolved hard X-ray spectroscopy on the short timescale over which the proposed targets vary. NuSTAR is therefore ideally suited to complement the UV and soft X-ray observations with Swift, and the VHE gamma-ray observations with MAGIC and VERITAS, in constraining the rapid variability of the targets' broadband SED.Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Paneque                       David                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N02       Extensive Multi-Frequency Monitoring Of The Classical Tev Blazars Mrk 421 And Mrk 501                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316MRK_421                                           @d¬)«y¶µ@C–Â`Aâ@fyAÚ◊s@P2±ƒ2 X@Apê-‡@Ï=˝#Ü@Ï>xVb‹60202048008@ﬁ~˜;dZ@ﬁmû~˘€#@‡q‚\ë—N@‡r¬\ë—NSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï‹øhd‹␀␀„nHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀âMulti-year and multi-frequency monitoring of the classical TeV blazars Mrk 421 and Mrk 501 is an important resource in the effort to understand the physics of relativistic jets. These objects are among the very small number of sources whose broadband SED can be characterized simultaneously by the currently existing instruments. We request NuSTAR observations as a part of two planned campaigns in 2016 and 2017 on these two objects. Only NuSTAR is sensitive enough to provide time-resolved hard X-ray spectroscopy on the short timescale over which the proposed targets vary. NuSTAR is therefore ideally suited to complement the UV and soft X-ray observations with Swift, and the VHE gamma-ray observations with MAGIC and VERITAS, in constraining the rapid variability of the targets' broadband SED.Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Paneque                       David                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N02       Extensive Multi-Frequency Monitoring Of The Classical Tev Blazars Mrk 421 And Mrk 501                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                     MAGIC VERITAS                                                                                       ␀␀␀(4/4) / Kp=5                                                                                                            archived  20200429GRS_1915p105                                      ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï>xVb‹@Ï>xVb‹90201053001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‹ø:gÍ√␀␀‚Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                                   