ed by the decay of their enormous magnetic fields. Magnetars exhibit dramatic variability including major outbursts - a hallmark of their emission. These outbursts allow us to probe the extreme physics at work in the Universe's largest known magnetic fields. Understanding the evolution of these outbursts will place stringent constraints on physical models of magnetars, including their crusts, cores, atmospheres, coronae, and magnetospheres. In this proposal, we request Chandra and NuSTAR Target-of-Opportunity observations of a major magnetar outburst in AO18 in order to put detailed physical models to the test, and as an anchor for multiwavelength follow-up.                                                                    Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Kaspi                         V M                           NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀C18       Target-of-Oppurtunity Chandra Observations of Magnetars in Outburst                                                     ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316PSR_J1622m4950                                    @n∑m\˙¨⁄¿HÏ∆?@t‹u%F?©ôôôôôö@j`Aâ7K«@ÏCÍM@ÏCDxVb‹80202051002@È∆1˝ä⁄∫@È≥˛ØOÑ@ÎõIóˆ+k@Îõ)óˆ+kSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï⁄»qÓ-␀␀„áHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  KMagnetars are highly magnetized young neutron stars that are powered by the decay of their enormous magnetic fields. Magnetars exhibit dramatic variability including major outbursts - a hallmark of their emission. These outbursts allow us to probe the extreme physics at work in the Universe's largest known magnetic fields. Understanding the evolution of these outbursts will place stringent constraints on physical models of magnetars, including their crusts, cores, atmospheres, coronae, and magnetospheres. In this proposal, we request Chandra and NuSTAR Target-of-Opportunity observations of a major magnetar outburst in AO18 in order to put detailed physical models to the test, and as an anchor for multiwavelength follow-up.                                                                    Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Kaspi                         V M                           NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀C18       Target-of-Oppurtunity Chandra Observations of Magnetars in Outburst                                                     ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              Chandra                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀(1/3)                                                                                                                   archived  202004292MASXJ21391374m2646315                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏCDxVb‹@ÏCE#Ü60362025001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï⁄»8!_Ù␀␀‚$Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. One of the principal goals of the NuSTAR extragalactic surveys is to constrain the high-energy X-ray luminosity function and trace its evolution as a function of redshift and AGN obscuration. We will continue to pursue a multi-layer survey strategy, expanding the number of deep fields, and increasing the area of shallow observations through serendipitous sources.                                                                                                            