           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  202004292MASSiJ1346085p732053                             @iÕ4÷°aÂ@RU¬è\(ˆ@]m$›/@EìxF‹]?ˇ∞ ƒõ•„@ÏI+?r‘£@ÏI6xVb‹60160556002@—ã.&ÄùI@—zÜæﬂ§@@“£KUõ=@“£KUõ=SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï⁄lË¨Ò5␀␀‚VHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀in CVZ                                                                                                                  arc