   NULL                          USA                           ␀CAL       NuSTAR calibration campaign                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                                                                                                                         ␀␀␀Calibration / Kp=6                                                                                                      archived  20200429NGC_1313_X1                                       @H“⁄πıY¥¿Pû1¯†ê.@q∂(åÁ∞¿FN;Õ5®X@_Ä>BZÓc@ÏK˛±9Ò@ÏKˇî»)¯30302016003␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï⁄X·ên␀␀‰dHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀IWe request 5x75ks NuSTAR observations of the ultraluminous X-ray source (ULX) NGC1313 X-1 (375ks in total), to be coordinated with the very large XMM-Newton (750ks) and Chandra (500ks) follow-up programs our team has been awarded to study its extreme (~0.2-0.25c) outflow. The addition of NuSTAR observations to these programs will allow us to perform multi-epoch broadband spectroscopy, robustly determining the continuum and thus allowing us to better study the ionization structure and variability of this outflow, as well as undertaking broadband spectral variability studies for comparison with other ULXs. NGC1313 X-1 is the only source for which this is currently possible, so it is vital we take advantage of this unique opportunity.                                                           Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Walton                        Dominic                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N03       MULTI-EPOCH BROADBAND X-RAY SPECTROSCOPY OF THE ULTRALUMINOUS X-RAY SOURCE NGC1313 X-1                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                         