nóçOﬂ@Z–|Ñµ›@ÏM)xVb‹@ÏM*?r‘£30301029001@téÁØ∑È@tÅÒA [¿@u‡␀␀␀␀␀@u‡␀␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï⁄U-¸5␀␀„ÊHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀We propose NuSTAR observations of the newly discovered gamma-ray (GR) binary LMC P3 simultaneous to our already approved XMM-Newton AO-16 observations. LMC P3 is 4x more luminous than similar systems in gamma-rays and 10x in X-ray and radio. This extreme behavior may be driven by a large spin-down power from the suspected pulsar, as well as a high UV photon seed density of the O5 III star, but the details of the high energy emission region remain perplexing. With the high spectral and temporal resolution of NuSTAR, we will probe the physical conditions of this emission region with the first high S/N spectrum above 10 keV, and search for signatures of a NS or BH. Our study of LMC P3, the first extra-galactic GR binary, is the first step towards characterizing the GR binary population.      Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Coley                         Joel                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N03       LMC P3: AN EXTREME PARTICLE ACCELERATOR                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20200429LMC_P3                                            @U␀ ƒõ•„¿P„»K]Ãd@q[E° ¿É¿@
