and diffuse emission toward the Galactic Center, including the Galactic ridge emission.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               Normal galaxies                                             ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀GLS       Galactic Plane Legacy Surveys                                                                                           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316SMC_Deep_MOS02                                    @)>ﬂ§?Â…¿RQ° ¿É@rÒ[¿6„¿E·=Ÿb∑@gWÛ∂E°À@ÏNﬁèFj@ÏNÔ?r‘£50311002006@›=˙∞ ƒú@›#%+”√a@ﬂHúÍJå@ﬂJ‹ÍJåSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï⁄K˙˘çw␀␀‚ìHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. The goals of the Galactic Legacy Survey are to expose the hidden Milky Way and reveal the wide range of astrophysics that creates high-energy emission. The program will continue NuSTAR studies of flares from Sgr A*, HMXB in a range of environments, and diffuse emission toward the Galactic Center, including the Galactic ridge emission.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               Normal galaxies                                             ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀GLS       Galactic Plane Legacy Surveys                                                                                           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀(3/2) GLS                                                                                                               archived  20200429PKS_0227m369                                      @B≥˜ŒŸá¿B['ª/Ï@nÑÎC,•¿P—$›/@b©Â…‰@ÏNÔ?r‘£@ÏNÔ±9Ò60367002001@quêñªô@q`K∆ßÔû@ré␀—∑Y@ré␀—∑YSCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï⁄K…ìà'␀␀„ÊHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀≈We propose to observe 4 blazars at z>2, detected in the gamma-rays by Fermi/LAT and in the soft X-rays, but not yet observed at energies larger than 10 keV. They are among the most powerful blazars and they host black holes whose masses exceed 1e9 Msun. The total requested time of 80 ks is sufficient to establish flux and slope of their X-ray continuum in order to estimate their total electromagnetic output and peak frequency, combined with the Fermi gamma-ray data. This will shed light on the jet-accretion relation, on the controversy about the blazar sequence at its high power extreme, and about the formation epoch of supermassive black holes in jetted quasars.                                                                                                                                 Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Ghisellini                    Gabriele                      NULL               