                                                                   ␀␀]Ï␀␀␀␀Solar CME                                                                                                                         ␀␀␀ToO / Kp=8 / Solar flare 250:2350 M3.9 251:0219 M1.3 251:0339 M1.2 251:0740 M8.1 251:1509 M2.9                          archived  20200429IRAS_18325m5926                                   ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏRñ±9Ò@ÏRó#Ü60301028001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï⁄ÔzÄ␀␀‰Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀÷Here we propose a simultaneous NuSTAR and XMM-Newton (100+50ks) observation of IRAS 18325-5926, a highly variable type-2 Seyfert galaxy and one of the very few with a claim of a broad FeK profile. Archival data have previously been insufficient to distinguish between a relativistically broadened Fe line and a blend of narrow Gaussians. However, we will be able to break the degeneracy thanks to the uninterrupted coverage of the NuSTAR bandpass extending well >10keV. Additionally, this source shows one of the clearest low-frequency lag-energy spectra to date with lags well defined up to 10keV. With NuSTAR we will extend our lag analysis up to >50keV, providing some of the most robust tests of Fourier-based inter-band time lag models to date.                                                   Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Lobban                        Andrew                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N03       SPECTRAL TIMING STUDIES OF IRAS 18325-5926                                                                              ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                            