                              ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  201503161ES0152p022                                       @<‹ãCïÅ@ñá+J@cV’œ™Œ¿Lhç∏∫«@rÇ©ì·@ÏZ	#Ü@ÏZ?r‘£60160080002@‘É“è\(ˆ@‘t+J@’€£4÷°b@’€£4÷°bSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏŸaV©&N␀␀‚€Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                                                                                                                         ␀␀␀Kp=5                                                                                                                    archived  20200429M31_Field_D                                       ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏZ?r‘£@ÏZèFj50312001001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏŸa,wÿè␀␀‰HHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ÚThe sensitivity and spatial resolving power of NuSTAR have allowed the study of individual neutron stars and black holes in other galaxies at hard energies for the first time, but they are nearly all more luminous than the population of sources probed in detail in the Milky Way. With a NuSTAR legacy survey of M31, we have finally detected sources at these lower luminosities, allowing a direct comparison of M31's neutron star and black hole accretors to the Milky Way's in the crucial window above 10 keV. We propose 4 additional pointings of M31 to double the number of >10^37 erg/s detected at hard energies to ensure the shape of the luminosity function is more robust to low number fluctuations. Also, we will classify the brightest sources, which is only possible with hard band data.        Normal galaxies                                             ␀1    Wik                           Daniel                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N03       TOWARD A BETTER CENSUS OF BLACK HOLES AND NEUTRON STARS IN THE DISK OF M31                                              ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316M31_Field_D                                       @'H1&Èx’@E≈÷8ÜY@^qÃcÒA ¿4«ˆ+jÁ’@!6‚ÎC@ÏZèFj@ÏZ:èFj50312001002@Á]HQÎÖ@ÁGﬁÕûÉ‰@Ëı≈¢úwö@Ëˆe¢úwöSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏŸ`“∞␀␀‰HHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀ÚThe sensitivity and spatial resolving power of NuSTAR have allowed the study of individual neutron stars and black holes in other galaxies at hard energies for the first time, but they are nearly all more luminous than the population of sources probed in detail in the Milky Way. With a NuSTAR legacy survey of M31, we have finally detected sources at these lower luminosities, allowing a direct comparison of M31's neutron star and black hole accretors to the Milky Way's in the crucial window above 10 keV. We propose 4 additional pointings of M31 to double the number of >10^37 erg/s detected at hard energies to ensure the shape of the luminosity function is more robust to low number fluctuations. Also, we will classify the brightest sources, which is only possible with hard band data.        Normal galaxies                                             ␀1    Wik                           Daniel                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N03       TOWARD A BETTER CENSUS OF BLACK HOLES AND NEUTRON STARS IN THE DISK OF M31                                              ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                                                                                                                         ␀␀␀Kp=6                                                                                                                    archived  20200429V405_Aur                                          ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏZ:èFj@ÏZ:±9Ò30460007001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏŸ`ûË›}␀␀‚€Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. The goals of the Galactic Legacy Survey are to expose the hidden Milky Way and reveal the wide range of astrophysics that creates high-energy emission. The program will continue NuSTAR studies of flares from Sgr A*, HMXB in a range of environments, and diffuse emission toward the Galactic Center, including the Galactic ridge emission.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀GLS       Galactic Plane Legacy Surveys            