ments, and diffuse emission toward the Galactic Center, including the Galactic ridge emission.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀GLS       Galactic Plane Legacy Surveys                                                                                           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀GLS                                                                                                                     archived  202004294U_0614p09                                        ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï][‰õø@Ï]?r‘£30363002001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏŸ@{ÏGM␀␀‰]Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀˛We propose to observe the neutron star low-mass X-ray binaries and Atoll sources GX 3+1, 4U 0614+09, 4U 1735-44, 4U 1746-37, and 4U 1702-43, for 20 ks each. Our primary goal is to increase the number of neutron stars with clear, robust indications of relativistic reflection from the inner disk. These observations will also address the radial extent of the inner disk in Atoll sources, which likely accrete at a low Eddington fraction similar to the black hole low/hard state. Our final goal is to find examples of disks that extend very close to stellar surfaces in order to obtain limits on neutron star radii.                                                                                                                                                                                           Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Miller                        Jon                           NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N03       NEUTRON STARS AND THEIR INNERMOST ACCRETION FLOWS                                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  201503164U_0614p09                                        @Wì√a@O@"OÉ{J#:@iM“Ò©¸¿<j~˘€#@g¿6‚Î@Ï]?r‘£@Ï]&èFj30363002002@”lÀí:@”}¶˚~ë␀@÷w¨∆?@÷yl∆?SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏŸ@¢≥≈␀␀‰]Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀˛We propose to observe the neutron star low-mass X-ray binaries and Atoll sources GX 3+1, 4U 0614+09, 4U 1735-44, 4U 1746-37, and 4U 1702-43, for 20 ks each. Our primary goal is to increase the number of neutron stars with clear, robust indications of relativistic reflection from the inner disk. These observations will also address the radial extent of the inner disk in Atoll sources, which likely accrete at a low Eddington fraction similar to the black hole low/hard state. Our final goal is to find examples of disks that extend very close to stellar surfaces in order to obtain limits on neutron star radii.                                                                                                                                                                                           Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Miller                        Jon                           NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N03       NEUTRON STARS AND THEIR INNERMOST ACCRETION FLOWS                                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429PMN_J1028m0844                                    ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï]&èFj@Ï]&±9Ò60373001001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏŸ?‰Pg)␀␀‰hHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀œMeV blazars, that have larger-than-average jet powers, accretion luminosities and black hole masses are best studied in the hard X-ray domain where they display extremely hard X-ray continua. Observations in this domain probe the acceleration & emission mechanisms, the bulk Lorentz factor. We propose to observe with NuSTAR the 4 highest-redshift that have ever been detected at gamma-rays and that do not have any observation between 10 keV and 100 MeV. We will complement the NuSTAR exposure with observations with Fermi, Swift, and SARA to obtain an high-quality simultaneous SED for all these sources. Moreover, optical spectroscopy will be performed for 3 targets lacking a kinematic measurement of the black hole mass. All this will greatly enhance our knowledge of this elusive source class. Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Paliya                        Vaidehi                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N03       CHASING THE MOST POWERFUL BLAZARS                                                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                          