) are a new class of AGN detected at GeV energies by Fermi which extend the domain of relativistic jets sources down to lower black hole masses. We have 8m Gemini near-IR spectra of some objects and estimated black hole masses from their Balmer and Paschen line profiles. We also now have VLT time (2017). We propose NuSTAR (with standard short SWIFT) observations of 3 gamma-ray NLS1s to build broad band SEDs which we will fit with our newly developed models for the jet and disc components. We will use the results to determine the relationship between the gamma-ray NLS1s, and the similarly high Eddington ratio flat spectrum gamma-ray radio quasars to determine how the jet properties relate to black hole mass.                                             Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Ward                          Martin                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N03       HARD X-RAY OBSERVATIONS OF GAMMA-RAY DETECTED SEYFERTS                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316B2_0954p25                                        @bß1è≈Å@9GçOﬂ;d@i®ﬁ␀—∑@IgUõ=»@d’F
