␀␀␀␀@ÏiÉ±9Ò@ÏiÑÍM80302302005␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏÿöÕ-„Ô␀␀‰ÌHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀9ÕBlack hole transients (BHT) are the only class of black holes (BH) which samples a wide range of accretion rates and accretion states during their month to year long outbursts. BHT classically show two types of outflows: collimated radio-jets ubiquitous during the canonical hard state and highly ionised X-ray winds during the soft state. We propose a combined XMM+NuSTAR monitoring campaign of an high inclination BHT, to shed light on the evolution of the wind while the source transits through the intermediate states.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Ponti                         Gabriele                      NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀X16       Tracing the evolution of BH winds through the intermediate states                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Swift_J1658d2m4242                                @o“éäqﬁj¿EWX‚e@urqué!ñ?–£n.±ƒ@d:«À)_@ÏiÑÍM@Ïiö[‰õø80302302006@€ï$ÎÌ˙D@€•å~($@‡◊ã4ÍK@‡◊Î4ÍKSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïÿö1ñê·␀␀‰ÌHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀9ÕBlack hole transients (BHT) are the only class of black holes (BH) which samples a wide range of accretion rates and accretion states during their month to year long outbursts. BHT classically show two types of outflows: collimated radio-jets ubiquitous during the canonical hard state and highly ionised X-ray winds during the soft state. We propose a combined XMM+NuSTAR monitoring campaign of an high inclination BHT, to shed light on the evolution of the wind while the source transits through the intermediate states.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Ponti                         Gabriele                      NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀X16       Tracing the evolution of BH winds through the intermediate states                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀(3/5) ToO                                                                                                               archived  20200429MCGm02m08m039                                     ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ïiö[‰õø@Ïiõ[‰õø60360010001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏÿôÅ¥Ë␀␀„bHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. One of the principal goals of the NuSTAR extragalactic surveys is to constrain the high-energy X-ray luminosity function and trace its evolution as a function of redshift and AGN obscuration. We will continue to pursue a multi-layer survey strategy, expanding the number of deep fields, and increasing the area of shallow observations through serendipitous sources.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀ELS       Extragalactic Legacy Surveys                                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316MCGm02m08m039                                     @Fåø±[W?¿&‹æﬂ§@@g˜ÎÖ∏R¿LÿD–©@u(◊s¸@Ïiõ[‰õø@Ïi∞±9Ò60360010002@⁄»?I∫@⁄≥›° ¿É@‹®‘¬¯7µ@‹≠T¬¯7µSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïÿô2Xø&␀␀„bHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. One of the principal goals of the NuSTAR extragalactic surveys is to constrain the high-energy X-ray luminosity function and trace its evolution as a function of redshift and AGN obscuration. We will continue to pursue a multi-layer survey strategy, expanding the number of deep fields, and increasing the area of shallow observations through serendipitous sources.                                                                                                             