=p§␀␀„sHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. The goals of the Galactic Legacy Survey are to expose the hidden Milky Way and reveal the wide range of astrophysics that creates high-energy emission. The program will continue NuSTAR studies of flares from Sgr A*, HMXB in a range of environments, and diffuse emission toward the Galactic Center, including the Galactic ridge emission.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀GLS       Galactic Plane Legacy Surveys                                                                                           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316V1432_Aql                                         @rqìtº¿$–â†'RT@<€≤˛≈m]¿.ûöu@bIv_ÿ≠¨@Ïl¶xVb‹@ÏlºÍM30460004002@⁄å9»K^@⁄qô‡q@‹ò¨÷°aÂ@‹õl÷°aÂSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïÿm∫Ä0å␀␀„sHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. The goals of the Galactic Legacy Survey are to expose the hidden Milky Way and reveal the wide range of astrophysics that creates high-energy emission. The program will continue NuSTAR studies of flares from Sgr A*, HMXB in a range of environments, and diffuse emission toward the Galactic Center, including the Galactic ridge emission.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀GLS       Galactic Plane Legacy Surveys                                                                                           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀IP sample                                                                                                               archived  20200429RX_J1347d5m1145                                   ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏlºÍM@ÏlΩ±9Ò70301001003␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏÿmâÙüJ␀␀‰‡Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀)We propose to observe a merging galaxy cluster RX J1347.5-1145 at z=0.451 with NuSTAR to 1) distinguish between thermal and non-thermal origins of the excess hard component detected by Suzaku and 2) identify its peak position in hard X-rays. If the measured spectrum follows a power-law, we will achieve either the first detection of the non-thermal hard X-ray emission from galaxy clusters or the thermal emission in excess of 25 keV. If it is thermal, we will significantly improve both accuracy of gas temperature and limits on the magnetic field strength in this distant cluster. NuSTAR's hard X-ray spectroscopy and imaging capability are crucial for this study.                                                                                                                                     Galaxy clusters and extragalactic diffuse objects           ␀1    Ota                           Naomi                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N03       UNVEILING THE NATURE OF HARD X-RAY EXCESS IN A DISTANT GALAXY CLUSTER RX J1347.5-1145                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316RX_J1347d5m1145                                   @i›~êˇó$¿'e8Ô4÷°@t=T`™d√@HÄÿD–©@f^$xG@ÏlΩ±9Ò@ÏlÊèFj70301001004@Ë ıIQÇ™@Ëæqv@ÈÎJè\(ˆ@ÈÏØ\(ı√SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏÿmH,␀␀‰‡Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀)We propose to observe a merging galaxy cluster RX J1347.5-1145 at z=0.451 with NuSTAR to 1) distinguish between thermal and non-thermal origins of the excess hard component detected by Suzaku and 2) identify its peak position in hard X-rays. If the measured spectrum follows a power-law, we will achieve either the first detection of the non-thermal hard X-ray emission from galaxy clusters or the thermal emission in excess of 25 keV. If it is thermal, we will significantly improve both accuracy of gas temperature and limits on the magnetic field strength in this distant cluster. NuSTAR's hard X-ray spectroscopy and imaging capability are crucial for this study.                                                                                                                                     Galaxy clusters and extragalactic diffuse objects           ␀1    Ota                           Naomi                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N03       UNVEILING THE NATURE OF HARD X-RAY EXCESS IN A DISTANT GALAXY CLUSTER RX J1347.5-1145                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429SN2017gas                                         @s≈m\˙≠@Mí:)«z@W.∞ ƒõ¶@(ÛMjO@d◊Ø∑È@ÏlÊèFj@ÏlÁèFj80202052003␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïÿl’Ê¯	␀␀‰’Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    KContrary to expectations from current stellar evolutionary models, recent observations uncovered the ejection of shells of material by massive stars in the years before the supernova (SN) explosion. The physical mechanism behind the impulsive mass ejection synchronized with the stellar core-collapse is unclear. Here we propose a coordinated Chandra-NuSTAR effort to map the evolution of the broad-band X-ray spectrum of 1 nearby (d<50 Mpc) strongly interacting SN and enable progress. Our program is designed to characterize the medium around strongly interacting SN, which originate from stellar progenitors with the most extreme mass loss before explosion. The overarching goal is to constrain the nature of the physical process responsible for mass loss in evolved massive stars.                Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Margutti                      R                             NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀C18       Mapping extreme mass loss from evolved massive stars with coordinated Chandra-NuSTAR observations                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316SN2017gas                                         @s&ÄùIR@Mìtºj@W.5?|Ìë@(˝VlÙ!@dæØOÑM@ÏlÁèFj@Ïm
