␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏmÚÕ´∏1@ÏmÛxVb‹30302019007␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïÿg¥%Ì␀␀ÂYHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀òUnderstanding the nature of the corona and disk-coronal interaction is a forefront challenge. While NuSTAR is the leading instrument at probing the high-energy spectral reflection component, NICER provides a complementary view of the thermal accretion disk. Both instruments handle bright sources without suffering from pileup effects. NICER is carrying out a monitoring program on Cyg X-1, the black-hole source for which disk and reflection components are most strongly intermingled, and with a disk that is cool and out of reach for NuSTAR alone. We ask for 6x20 ks NuSTAR observations of Cyg X-1 to be carried out at any time. NICER will work with NuSTAR to coordinate these observations and the NICER allotment is already approved.                                                                Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Steiner                       James                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N03       A NUSTAR & NICER LOOK AT COMPTONIZATION, REFLECTION, AND THERMAL EMISSION IN CYGNUS X-1                                 ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Cyg_X1                                            @rπ‘ï*ô@Aú–©*0@Q–bM“Ú@	<”ZÖáî@b≤h	‘ï@ÏmÛxVb‹@ÏnèFj30302019008@¡,¢3ú@¡¸ﬁcä	@÷“qóˆ+k@÷“qóˆ+kSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏÿeØzÄ␀␀ÂYHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀òUnderstanding the nature of the corona and disk-coronal interaction is a forefront challenge. While NuSTAR is the leading instrument at probing the high-energy spectral reflection component, NICER provides a complementary view of the thermal accretion disk. Both instruments handle bright sources without suffering from pileup effects. NICER is carrying out a monitoring program on Cyg X-1, the black-hole source for which disk and reflection components are most strongly intermingled, and with a disk that is cool and out of reach for NuSTAR alone. We ask for 6x20 ks NuSTAR observations of Cyg X-1 to be carried out at any time. NICER will work with NuSTAR to coordinate these observations and the NICER allotment is already approved.                                                                Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Steiner                       James                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N03       A NUSTAR & NICER LOOK AT COMPTONIZATION, REFLECTION, AND THERMAL EMISSION IN CYGNUS X-1                                 ␀␀␀è␀␀␀␀                              NICER                                                                                               ␀␀␀(4/6) / data gap 143s                                                                                                   archived  20200429FO_Aqr                                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏnèFj@Ïn±9Ò30460002001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïÿe}àÈ†␀␀„{Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. The goals of the Galactic Legacy Survey are to expose the hidden Milky Way and reveal the wide range of astrophysics that creates high-energy emission. The program will cont