                                    ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏpπèFj@ÏpπÕ´∏140301005001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏÿN=ç␀␀Â.Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ˆThat SNRs accelerate particles to CR energies is no longer in doubt, but there are many questions yet to be answered. We still lack detailed knowledge about the efficiency of the process of particle acceleration at SNR shocks, the effect of CR production on the evolution of SNRs, and the properties of magnetic fields in these systems and how these are amplified. In order to address these outstanding issues, we propose to observe the SW region of SNR RCW 86 with NuSTAR, with a 200 ks pointing (shown in Fig. 1). This will allow us to: (1) determine the morphology of the non-thermal X-ray emission in this region in the NuSTAR band, and contrast it to observations with XMM-Newton and Chandra, (2) constrain the spectral shape of the electron population that underlies the non-thermal emission.  Non-ToO Supernovae, Supernova Remnants, and Galactic diffuse␀1    Castro                        Daniel                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N03       A HARD (X-RAY) LOOK AT THE SW REGION OF SNR RCW 86                                                                      ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316RCW_86_SW                                         @kà'RT`™¿OTº£@s∞j~˘€#¿4÷°a‰˜@où{J#9¡@ÏpπÕ´∏1@Ïq5xVb‹40301005002AK|wŒŸA+`™d√A«≥+”√aA…ì+”√aSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏÿM ù≈ò␀␀Â.Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                 