                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀ToO                                                                                                                     archived  20200429NVSSJ122810m092702                                ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏqXèFj@ÏqX±9Ò60464096001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏÿLI2q␀␀„êHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316NVSSJ122810m092702                                @g`¨1&È¿"À)^û@rO	‘ï+@JÉ∂E° ¡@u˘¥¢3ú@ÏqX±9Ò@Ïqh?r‘£60464096002@‘œ±5®Xy@‘¿˚∆ßÔû@÷\ıÆÊ1˘@÷^uÆÊ1˘SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏÿL’Ê¯␀␀„êHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429NGC_1792                                          ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ïqh?r‘£@Ïqi#Ü60371001001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏÿK÷Ò˜®␀␀‰˝Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ùWe propose for a total of 150 ks NuSTAR and 30 ks XMM-Newton observations to characterise the intrinsic power and obscuring properties of four of the nearest active galactic nuclei (AGN) to us. We are carrying out the first complete and direct measurement of the column density (N_H) distribution of AGN in a local volume-limited (D < 15 Mpc) AGN survey using primarily NuSTAR. Prior to our program, only 50% of the AGN had reliable obscuration measurements. We have recently improved this to 75%, and found a Compton-thick AGN fraction of at least 30%. This is higher than that directly measured in flux-limited AGN samples. NuSTAR observations of these four targets will be crucial in bringing the local N_H distribution of AGN to 100% completeness.                                                 Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Annuar                        Ady                           NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N03       A COMPLETE CENSUS OF THE COMPTON-THICK AGN POPULATION IN OUR COSMIC BACKYARD                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                             