LN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀ToO                                                                                                                     archived  202004293C273                                             ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ïr6±9Ò@Ïr8èFj80301602001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏÿCÏ®d␀␀‰NHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ÛThe gamma-ray flaring of the jet in 3C273 is a rare event and seen just twice over the last 5 years. Only once before has a hard X-ray instrument been pointed at 3C273 during such a confirmed event, and we request 75ks to observe the impact of the bright jet state on the X-ray band. NuSTAR is the only observatory currently capable of probing the hard X-ray turnover with sufficient sensitivity during such a rare event, and the observation will provide unprecedented details on this complex transition region between AGN and jet, and perhaps once and for all solve the mystery of whether the curvature of the hard X-ray spectrum comes primarily from the accretion flow of the AGN component, or from a SSC+ERC jet.                                                                                     Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Madsen                        Kristin                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N03       CATCHING THE FLARING JET OF 3C 273                                                                                      ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  201503163C273                                             @gg∑X‚@␀V8ÜYJı@r‡qv@P∏QÎÖ?˜z·GÆ{@Ïr8èFj@ÏrfÕ´∏180301602002@Ì´iS&@Ìù–äqﬁj@ ’ÿ≠´ü@#ÿ≠´üSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏÿCR}'“␀␀‰NHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀ÛThe gamma-ray flaring of the jet in 3C273 is a rare event and seen just twice over the last 5 years. Only once before has a hard X-ray instrument been pointed at 3C273 during such a confirmed event, and we request 75ks to observe the impact of the bright jet state on the X-ray band. NuSTAR is the only observatory currently capable of probing the hard X-ray turnover with sufficient sensitivity during such a rare event, and the observation will provide unprecedented details on this complex transition region between AGN and jet, and perhaps once and for all solve the mystery of whether the curvature of the hard X-ray spectrum comes primarily from the accretion flow of the AGN component, or from a SSC+ERC jet.                                                                                     Proposed ToOs