O       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀ToO                                                                                                                     archived  20200429NGC_2623                                          ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏrÕ#Ü@ÏrŒèFj60374010001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïÿ?ƒ\ä␀␀ÂHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ÊMajor gas-rich galaxy mergers play a significant role in galaxy evolution and SMBH growth. However, we still do not know exactly when and how in the last stages of the merger sequence the observed dramatic SMBH growth phase and its feedback on the environment start. Thanks to its unprecedented E>10 keV sensitivity and imaging capabilities, NuSTAR can strongly contribute to answer these questions. We propose to carry out ten observations of galaxies in the final stages of galaxy mergers which are known to host an AGN. The NuSTAR data will allow to infer the intrinsic luminosity and amount of obscuration in these AGN, and to understand whether feedback removes part of the obscuring material around coalescence.                                                                                   Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Ricci                         Claudio                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N03       PROBING THE GROWTH, OBSCURATION AND FEEDBACK OF SUPERMASSIVE BLACK HOLES IN THE FINAL STAGES OF GALAXY MERGERS          ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLA