00429SDSS_J103315d71p5252                              ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏsÔ[‰õø@ÏsÔÍM60468003001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïÿ6VÑ␀␀ÂHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ùThe X-ray spectral analysis of Compton thick (CT-, i.e., having intrinsic obscuration NH>1E24 cm^-2) active galactic nuclei (AGN) is key to understand the physics of the obscuring material surrounding accreting supermassive black holes. We propose to target with a combined NuSTAR/XMM-Newton observation three candidate CT-AGN selected from the BAT 100-month survey. Thanks to the excellent count statistics, we will be able to assess if these sources are in fact CT-AGN. We will also constrain several spectral parameters (e.g., relative importance of the scattered component versus the direct one, geometry of the obscuring torus, equivalent width of the Iron emission line). This analysis will refine our knowledge on the true intrinsic fraction of CT-AGN and their contribution to the CXB.       Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Marchesi                      Stefano                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       HEAVILY OBSCURED AGN: THE PHYSICS BEHIND THE OBSCURATION                                                                ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316SDSS_J103315d71p5252                              @c»ﬂ§?Â…@JlÙ!-w@c kP∞Ú|@J¡ [¿7@u¶∏QÎÖ@ÏsÔÍM@ÏtÍM60468003002@›ÿU[W>´@›∏ÎX‚@‡@xG@‡	‡xGSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïÿ6+Ö∏␀␀ÂHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀ùThe X-ray spectral analysis of Compton thick (CT-, i.e., having intrinsic obscuration NH>1E24 cm^-2) active galactic nuclei (AGN) is key to understand the physics of the obscuring material surrounding accreting supermassive black holes. We propose to target with a combined NuSTAR/XMM-Newton observation three candidate CT-AGN selected from the BAT 100-month survey. Thanks to the excellent count statistics, we will be able to assess if these sources are in fact CT-AGN. We will also constrain several spectral parameters (e.g., relative importance of the scattered component versus the direct one, geometry of the obscuring torus, equivalent width of the Iron emission line). This analysis will refine our knowledge on the true intrinsic fraction of CT-AGN and their contribution to the CXB.       Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Marchesi                      Stefano                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       HEAVILY OBSCURED AGN: THE PHYSICS BEHIND THE OBSCURATION                                                                ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429GX304m1                                           ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏtÍM@ÏtÍM90401326001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ïÿ5˘\Î$␀␀„∂Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar fla