␀ELS                                                                                                                     archived  20200429Her_X1                                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏÅZ[‰õø@ÏÅZ±9Ò30402009001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï◊29D•[␀␀ÊïHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀¥We propose to continue the study of the long-term evolution of the cyclotron line energy in Her X-1. The long-term decay of Ecyc discovered in data taken between 1993 and 2012, was confirmed by a precise measurement by NuSTAR in August 2015, firmly establishing a decay by 5 keV over the last 20 yrs. However, the last observing campaign in 2016, had provided evidence that the decay has ended. This was confirmed by the latest NuSTAR observation in August 2017. It is now the question whether we will (at some time) see a new increase, similar to the one that was observed between 1990 and 1993. It is likely that we see a change in the structure of the local B-field. We propose to continue the monitoring of Her X-1 during Cycle-4 with two observations of 30 ks each (about half a year apart).    Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Staubert                      Ruediger                      NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       MONITORING THE CYCLOTRON LINE ENERGY IN HERCULES X-1: IS THERE A TURN-UP AFTER THE LONG DECAY?                          ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Her_X1                                            @oÕ‹∆?@Aß4÷°aÂ@M≤-V@B÷ìtº@tôRΩ<6@ÏÅZ±9Ò@ÏÅqÕ´∏130402009002@€ç#πå~(@€ƒe¯†ê.@·Ÿ•