“`Aâ7@JåM@ÚN|$›/@ÚOL$›/SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï◊+Î<M^␀␀ÂôHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀2We propose three joint XMM-Newton and NuSTAR observations of the black hole binary H 1743-322, each covering a single XMM-Newton orbit and 70ks of NuSTAR time, sampling different stages of spectral evolution during the rise to outburst. This builds upon our recent discovery that the iron line centroid energy in this source varies systematically over the course of a 4s QPO cycle, providing strong evidence that the QPO is driven by relativistic precession. We now aim to sample the same source when displaying a range of higher QPO frequencies to explore the evolution of the iron line profile phase dependence with QPO frequency and compare with the prediction of relativistic precession. We will trigger the observations from Swift monitoring throughout the outburst.                             Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Ingram                        Adam                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀X15       Iron line Doppler tomography with quasi-periodic oscillations                                                           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀(3/3)                                                                                                                   archived  20200429MAXI_J1820p070                                    ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏÇú±9Ò@ÏÇù#Ü90401309032␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï◊+®d‹␀␀‰Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targe