me from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀SADA rally / INERTIAL only                                                                                              archived  20150316GRS_1758m258                                      ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏÇºxVb‹@ÏÇΩ?r‘£30401030001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï◊"œΩ@␀␀ÂâHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀∂We propose a 50 ks observation of the Galactic microquasar GRS 1758-258 with NuSTAR, to obtain a high quality hard X-ray spectrum in the low-hard state. An observation with Suzaku has revealed the presence of a relativistic wind (v ~ 0.1c). Here we aim to utilize the excellent hard X-ray sensitivity of NuSTAR to constrain the properties of this outflow, and how it relates to the observed accretion flow geometry. As this system is known to power large radio jets, its study will aid our understanding of the conditions necessary for the formation of relativistic outflows and how these relate to the accretion geometry in the low-hard state.                                                                                                                                                            Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Reynolds                      Mark                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       CONSTRAINING THE RELATIVISTIC OUTFLOW IN THE MICRO-QUASAR GRS 1758-258                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316GRS_1758m258                                      @p‰çOﬂ;d¿9√˜ŒŸá@lq≤ïÍøÚ?º@tËñRΩ<6@ÏÇΩ?r‘£@ÏÇ›èFj30401030002@‰á*Èx‘˛@‰ÖwÓÀ˚@ÁCj~˘€@ÁD»j~˘€SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï◊"J=p§␀␀ÂâHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀∂We propose a 50 ks observation of the Galactic microquasar GRS 1758-258 with NuSTAR, to obtain a high quality hard X-ray spectrum in the low-hard state. An observation with Suzaku has revealed the presence of a relativistic wind (v ~ 0.1c). Here we aim to utilize the excellent hard X-ray sensitivity of NuSTAR to constrain the properties of this outflow, and how it relates to the observed accretion flow geometry. As this system is known to power large radio jets, its study will aid our understanding of the conditions necessary for the formation of relativistic outflows and how these relate to the accretion geometry in the low-hard state.                                                                                                                                                            Galactic Compact Sources             