d based on community input. One of the principal goals of the NuSTAR extragalactic surveys is to constrain the high-energy X-ray luminosity function and trace its evolution as a function of redshift and AGN obscuration. We will continue to pursue a multi-layer survey strategy, expanding the number of deep fields, and increasing the area of shallow observations through serendipitous sources.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀ELS       Extragalactic Legacy Surveys                                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              Swift                                                                                               ␀␀␀␀ELS                                                                                                                     archived  20200429W28                                               ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏÖÃ#Ü@ÏÖÕ#Ü40401006001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï÷ﬂ≠	{B␀␀Â•Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀OWe propose a 100-ks NuSTAR observation of Supernova Remnant W28. In Suzaku data, we detected the FeI Ka line, which can probably be attributed to K-shell ionization of Fe in an ambient molecular cloud by sub-relativistic particles accelerated in W28. In the hard X-ray band, nonthermal bremsstrahlung from the same population of the particles is expected. A NuSTAR observation enables us to detect nonthermal bremsstrahlung, which is direct evidence of sub-relativistic particles accelerated in W28. Furthermore, we can determine whether the particles are electrons or protons based on the equivalent width of the FeI Ka line with respect the nonthermal bremsstrahlung continuum. Also, the flux and slope of the bremsstrahlung can constrain the amount and spectrum of the particles.                  Non-ToO Supernovae, Supernova Remnants, and Galactic diffuse␀1    Okon                          Hiromichi                     NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       EXPLORATION OF NONTHERMAL BREMSSTRAHLUNG FROM SUB-RELATIVISTIC PARTICLES ACCELERATED IN SUPERNOVA REMNANT W28           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316W28                                               @pÁº£n¿7AT…Öo@mw1è≈øîØOÑM@t›4ÍK@ÏÖÕ#Ü@ÏÜ?r‘£40401006002@˜¢Å¶L/É@¯Jó$tT@˙aµ8ÜYK@˙dÖ8ÜYKSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï÷ﬁÀ¡Õ.␀␀Â•Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀OWe propose a 100-ks NuSTAR observation of Supernova Remnant W28. In Suzaku data, we detected the FeI Ka line, which can probably be attributed to K-shell ionization of Fe in an ambient molecular cloud by sub-relativistic particles accelerated in W28. In the hard X-ray band, nonthermal bremsstrahlung from the same population of the particles is expected. A NuSTAR observation enables us to detect nonthermal bremsstrahlung, which is direct evidence of sub-relativistic particles accelerated in W28. Furthermore, we can determine whether the particles are electrons or protons based on the equivalent width of the FeI Ka line with respect the nonthermal bremsstrahlung continuum. Also, the flux and slope of the bremsstrahlung can constrain the amount and spectrum of the particles.                  Non-ToO Supernovae, Supernova Remnants, and Galactic diffuse␀1    Okon                          Hiromichi                     NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       EXPLORATION OF NONTHERMAL BREMSSTRAHLUNG FROM SUB-RELATIVISTIC PARTICLES ACCELERATED IN SUPERNOVA REMNANT W28           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀idiagnostics_off 2018:298 2201Z                                                                                         archived  20200429IGR_J17195m4100                                   ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏÜ?r‘£@ÏÜî»)¯30460005001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï÷ﬁê6ù␀␀‰8Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. The goals of the Galactic Legacy Survey are to expose the hidden Milky Way and reveal the wide range of astrophysics that creates high-energy emission. The program will continue NuSTAR studies of flares from Sgr A*, HMXB in a range of environments, and diffuse emission toward the Galactic Center, including the Galactic ridge emission.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀GLS       Galactic Plane Legacy Surveys                                                                                           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316IGR_J17195m4100                                   @p=â†'RT¿DÑV’œ™Œ@u≠z·GÆø˛äqﬁi≠C@vâ†'RT@ÏÜî»)¯@ÏÜ3Õ´∏130460005002@‹ÿökP±@‹∂(Énò@ﬁﬂ<«‚ÇA@ﬁﬂ|«‚ÇASCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï÷ﬁ;‘Ñ␀␀‰8Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. The goals of the Galactic Legacy Survey are to expose the hidden Milky Way and reveal the wide range of astrophysics that creates high-energy emission. The program will continue NuSTAR studies of flares from Sgr A*, HMXB in a range of environments, and diffuse emission toward the Galactic Center, including the Galactic ridge emission.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀GLS       Galactic Plane Legacy Surveys                                                                                           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀IP sample                                                                                                               archived  20200429SDSSJ0122p0100                                    ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏÜ3Õ´∏1@ÏÜ4Õ´∏160467001001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï÷ﬁÎÖ␀␀Â™Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀YDespite decades of searching, observationally confirmed cases of dual AGNs are extremely rare, and most have been discovered serendipitously. Using the all-sky WISE survey, we identified a population of over 200 interacting galaxies that display extreme red mid-IR colors thus far exclusively associated in extragalactic sources with powerful AGNs, despite showing no signatures of activity in the optical. We were recently awarded 340ks of Chandra time to observe the 15 brightest MIR-selected dual AGN candidates with separations of a few kpc, of which 8 display two nuclear X-ray point sources consistent with dual AGNs.We propose follow-up NuSTAR observations of our sample to constrain the intrinsic absorption of the systems and determine the AGN bolometric luminosity.                         Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Satyapal                      Shobita                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       WISE DISCOVERY OF THE LARGEST SAMPLE OF OBSCURED DUAL AGNS: A NUSTAR FOLLOW-UP                                          ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316SDSSJ0122p0100                                    @4ñ_ÿ≠´ü?ÔGÆz·H@a