ing the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. The goals of the Galactic Legacy Survey are to expose the hidden Milky Way and reveal the wide range of astrophysics that creates high-energy emission. The program will continue NuSTAR studies of flares from Sgr A*, HMXB in a range of environments, and diffuse emission toward the Galactic Center, including the Galactic ridge emission.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀GLS       Galactic Plane Legacy Surveys                                                                                           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316SwiftJ005139d2m721704                             @)Ÿ¶µ(¿Ræﬂ§@@rÔéäqﬁj¿F[√a@O@r	…„Ω@Ïâ÷î»)¯@ÏâÚ±9Ò30361003004@‚≠	ú‡u˜@‚°À“Ò©¸@‰ëÜ„º”[@‰ìÊ„º”[SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï÷–îì'␀␀‰WHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. The goals of the Galactic Legacy Survey are to expose the hidden Milky Way and reveal the wide range of astrophysics that creates high-energy emission. The program will continue NuSTAR studies of flares from Sgr A*, HMXB in a range of environments, and diffuse emission toward the Galactic Center, including the Galactic ridge emission.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀GLS       Galactic Plane Legacy Surveys                                                                                           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀(2/3) TOO GLS SMC survey                                                                                                archived  20200429Gamma2_Velorum                                    ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏâÚ±9Ò@ÏâÛ?r‘£30402031003␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï÷–h≈6˛␀␀ÂƒHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ºOur NuSTAR observations of two massive colliding wind binary systems presented clear evidence of high-energy, non-thermal emission, which probably originate from inverse-Compton (IC) of stellar photons by high-energy electrons accelerated at the wind-wind colliding (WWC) shocks. However, the observed emission is nearly constant unlike the WWC thermal emission, and this is not expected from the standard IC mechanism. To understand the emission mechanism, we need more colliding wind binary systems with different stellar parameters. We propose two NuSTAR observations of another colliding wind binary system, gamma2 Velorum, which shows signatures of WWC X-ray activity and has a GeV gamma-ray counterpart, to detect high-energy non-thermal emission.                                               Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Hamaguchi                     Kenji                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       DETECTION OF NON-THERMAL X-RAY EMISSION FROM GAMMA2 VELORUM                                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Gamma2_Velorum                                    @^õqué!ñ¿G©Dg8~@pk_o“Û¿–©*0U@g≥õ=»K@ÏâÛ?r‘£@ÏäÍM30402031004@‰ªfOv@‰°OÕ5®X@Ê`{X‚@Ê`€X‚SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï÷–
