X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ïë’[‰õø@Ïë÷î»)¯80401316001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï÷Râb¸ñ␀␀ÂRHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀We propose to undertake a 60 ks NuSTAR target-of-opportunity observation of a new or known black hole transient during a bright, hard outburst phase. The goals of this program are to 1) determine whether the accretion disk is truncated in the bright hard state via modeling the disk reflection spectrum 2) test an apparent anti-correlation between winds and jets in soft and hard states by making a very sensitive search for winds in a hard state 3) searching for quasi-periodic oscillations (QPOs) in the power spectrum and compare with theoretical models. This observation will be supported by a network of ground-based observatories, and X-ray monitoring.                                                                                                                                              Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Xu                            Yanjun                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       THE BRIGHT HARD STATE OF A TRANSIENT BLACK HOLE BINARY IS THE ACCRETION DISK TRUNCATED?                                 ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316MAXI_J1631m479                                    @n˙›/üæ¿G·Ç©ì·@u:)«yß?‡‚e+”√@bFÀ˚µt@Ïë÷î»)¯@ÏëÏ?r‘£80401316002@¡yò	‘ï@¬he+‘@›5óK∆ß@›5K∆ßSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï÷PŒW˝␀␀ÂRHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀We propose to undertake a 60 ks NuSTAR target-of-opportu