 are a small class of neutron stars mainly powered by their huge magnetic fields. They go through long stretches of quiescence, interrupted by periods of activity, via short X-ray bursts, large giant flares and yearly-timescale X-ray outbursts. Observations performed during, or immediately after such periods yield the largest amount of information on magnetars' emission, allowing one to test the theoretical models on a variety of phenomena and source states. We propose a Joint XMM (85ks) and NuSTAR (170ks) ToO program (1 trigger of 4 observations over a few months) aimed at gathering new physical insight on magnetars crust, field configuration, magnetospheres, and evolution.                                                                   Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Rea                           Nanda                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀X15       Prompt XMM-Newton and NuSTAR study of magnetar outbursts                                                                ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀(2/4) ToO                                                                                                               archived  20200429NGC_5256                                          ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏìSÍM@ÏìT±9Ò60465005001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï÷B␀␀‰´Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. One of the principal goals of the NuSTAR extragalactic surveys is to constrain the high-energy X-ray luminosity function and trace its evolution as a function of redshift and AGN obscuration. We will continue to pursue a multi-layer survey strategy, expanding the number of deep fields, and increasing the area of shallow observations through serendipitous sources.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀ELS       Extragalactic Legacy Surveys                                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316NGC_5256                                          @iíãCïÅ@H'˘rGE9@Y i≠B√ @P∫^5?|Ó@a˚¬è\(ˆ@ÏìT±9Ò@Ïìl#Ü60465005002@ﬂà(ºj~˙@ﬂb	!ˇ.I@‡ŸòÃÃÃÕ@‡€xÃÃÃÕSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï÷A√Qän␀␀‰´Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. One of the principal goals of the NuSTAR extragalactic surveys is to constrain the high-energy X-ray luminosity function and trace its evolution as a function of redshift and AGN obscuration. We will continue to pursue a multi-layer survey strategy, expanding the number of deep fields, and increasing the area of shallow observations through serendipitous sources.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀ELS       Extragalactic Legacy Surveys                                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              Swift                                                                                               ␀␀␀␀ELS                                                                                                                     archived  20200429Her_X1                                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ïìl#Ü@Ïìlî»)¯30402034001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï÷Aó‰±~␀␀Ê7Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ÀWe propose a series of four 20 ks observations with NuSTAR and XMM of the Galactic binary X-ray pulsar Hercules X-1, which has a 35 day superorbital period caused by a warped, precessing accretion disk. The hard beam from the neutron star heats this disk and the corresponding reprocessed, thermal emission provides a unique opportunity for observation of magnetic-dominated accretion. Our proposed analysis requires good spectral and timing resolution across the full energy band (<1 keV to >20 keV) in order to constrain both the soft emission from the disk and the pulsar beam. For the first time, we will track a complete precession of Her X-1's accretion disk with full hard X-ray coverage to gain the clearest picture to date of the structure and kinematics of the magnetized accretion flow.   Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Brumback   