 ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. One of the principal goals of the NuSTAR extragalactic surveys is to constrain the high-energy X-ray luminosity function and trace its evolution as a function of redshift and AGN obscuration. We will continue to pursue a multi-layer survey strategy, expanding the number of deep fields, and increasing the area of shallow observations through serendipitous sources.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀ELS       Extragalactic Legacy Surveys                                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              Swift                                                                                               ␀␀␀␀NuLANDS                                                                                                                 archived  20200429Her_X1                                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ïì˚?r‘£@Ïì¸xVb‹30402034003␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï÷=i∑‘␀␀Ê7Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ÀWe propose a series of four 20 ks observations with NuSTAR and XMM of the Galactic binary X-ray pulsar Hercules X-1, which has a 35 day superorbital period caused by a warped, precessing accretion disk. The hard beam from the neutron star heats this disk and the corresponding reprocessed, thermal emission provides a unique opportunity for observation of magnetic-dominated accretion. Our proposed analysis requires good spectral and timing resolution across the full energy band (<1 keV to >20 keV) in order to constrain both the soft emission from the disk and the pulsar beam. For the first time, we will track a complete precession of Her X-1's accretion disk with full hard X-ray coverage to gain the clearest picture to date of the structure and kinematics of the magnetized accretion flow.   Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Brumback                      Mckinley                      NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       A DEFINITIVE INVESTIGATION OF THE MAGNETIZED ACCRETION FLOW IN THE X-RAY PULSAR HER X-1 WITH NUSTAR AND XMM             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Her_X1                                            @oœ≈Åo␀@AØüæv…@M‘˝Û∂F@B“êñªô@eÍsÅ◊€ı@Ïì¸xVb‹@ÏîÍM30402034004@’á¸"h	’@’mŒªò«„@◊8~}VlÙ@◊:˛}VlÙSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï÷="Ã
ü␀␀Ê7Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀ÀWe propose a series of four 20 ks observations with NuSTAR and XMM of the Galactic binary X-ray pulsar Hercules X-1, which has a 35 day superorbital period caused by a warped, precessing accretion disk. The hard beam from the neutron star heats this disk and the corresponding reprocessed, thermal emission provides a unique opportunity for observation of magnetic-dominated accretion. Our proposed analysis requires good spectral and timing resolution across the full energy band (<1 keV to >20 keV) in order to constrain both the soft emission from the disk and the pulsar beam. For the first time, we will track a complete precession of Her X-1's accretion disk with full hard X-ray coverage to gain the clearest picture to date of the structure and kinematics of the magnetized accretion flow.   Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Brumback                      Mckinley                      NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       A DEFINITIVE INVESTIGATION OF THE MAGNETIZED ACCRETION FLOW IN THE X-RAY PULSAR HER X-1 WITH NUSTAR AND XMM             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              NICER                                                                                               ␀␀␀␀(2/4)                                                                                                                   archived  20200429Swift_J1858d6m0814_SADA_19045                     ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏîÍM@Ïî±9Ò90501004001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï÷<¸M^p␀␀‰´Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) 