wo bright (FX>5 10^-13 cgs, LX>10^46 erg/s) radio-quiet QSOs at z>2, plus short XMM exposures for each of them: our total time request is 320k NuSTAR and 70ks XMM. By looking at rest-frame energies up to 300 keV, our goal is to measure unambiguously the presence of spectral cut-offs at rest-frame energies up to E_c=500 keV. This is not possible for local targets, where NuSTAR is just sensitive to E_c<250 keV. The two brightest sources of a sample of four have been successfully observed in Cycle 3. These observations allowed to measure for the first time E_c in distant, luminous QSOs. The proposed observations will allow to build a a small but unique sample of high-z, high-LX QSOs with accurate E_c measurements, to test current coronal models.             Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Lanzuisi                      Giorgio                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       THE HIGH-ENERGY CUT-OFF IN HIGH-Z/HIGH-L QSO                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429XBootes_003                                       ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ïúõ#Ü@ÏúõÕ´∏160365003001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï€Ìe[f«␀␀‰ÛHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. One of the principal goals of the NuSTAR extragalactic surveys is to constrain the high-energy X-ray luminosity function and trace its evolution as a function of redshift and AGN obscuration. We will continue to pursue a multi-layer survey strategy, expanding the number of deep fields, and increasing the area of shallow observations through serendipitous sources.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀ELS       Extragalactic Legacy Surveys                                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316XBootes_003                                       @k	…ÓÀ˚@Aæv»¥9X@NÊz·GÆ@Q©*0U2@Q¿Ù!-w@ÏúõÕ´∏1@Ïúø[‰õø60365003002@Á4O'ª/Ï@Á]ﬁ␀“@ÈÉ»K^@È„»K^SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï€Ìîbõ␀␀‰ÛHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. One of the principal goals of the NuSTAR extragalactic surveys is to constrain the high-energy X-ray luminosity function and trace its evolution as a function of redshift and AGN obscuration. We will continue to pursue a multi-layer survey strategy, expanding the number of deep fields, and increasing the area of shallow observations through serendipitous sources.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀ELS       Extragalactic Legacy Surveys                                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀ELS                                                                                                                     archived  20200429SWIFTJ0838d9p2617                                 ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ïúø[‰õø@Ïú¿èFj60462003001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï÷nÓÓÔ␀␀‰ÛHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1