_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀YDespite decades of searching, observationally confirmed cases of dual AGNs are extremely rare, and most have been discovered serendipitously. Using the all-sky WISE survey, we identified a population of over 200 interacting galaxies that display extreme red mid-IR colors thus far exclusively associated in extragalactic sources with powerful AGNs, despite showing no signatures of activity in the optical. We were recently awarded 340ks of Chandra time to observe the 15 brightest MIR-selected dual AGN candidates with separations of a few kpc, of which 8 display two nuclear X-ray point sources consistent with dual AGNs.We propose follow-up NuSTAR observations of our sample to constrain the intrinsic absorption of the systems and determine the AGN bolometric luminosity.                         Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Satyapal                      Shobita                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       WISE DISCOVERY OF THE LARGEST SAMPLE OF OBSCURED DUAL AGNS: A NUSTAR FOLLOW-UP                                          ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316SDSSJ1221p1137                                    @g'v_ÿ≠¨@':üæv»¥@q<≤˛≈m]@R:YJÙÿ@!–ÿD–©@ÏûŒ[‰õø@ÏûÂ±9Ò60467002002@›&è¿6„@‹ˆ∆ßÔû@ﬂGyN;Õ6@ﬂJ9N;Õ6SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï’Ò√ö[»␀␀ÊjHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀YDespite decades of searching, observationally confirmed cases of dual AGNs are extremely rare, and most have been discovered serendipitously. Using the all-sky WISE survey, we identified a population of over 200 interacting galaxies that display extreme red mid-IR colors thus far exclusively associated in extragalactic sources with powerful AGNs, despite showing no signatures of activity in the optical. We were recently awarded 340ks of Chandra time to observe the 15 brightest MIR-selected dual AGN candidates with separations of a few kpc, of which 8 display two nuclear X-ray point sources consistent with dual AGNs.We propose follow-up NuSTAR observations of our sample to constrain the intrinsic absorption of the systems and determine the AGN bolometric luminosity.                         Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Satyapal                      Shobita                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       WISE DISCOVERY OF THE LARGEST SAMPLE OF OBSCURED DUAL AGNS: A NUSTAR FOLLOW-UP                                          ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  202004292MASXJ21561518p1722525                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏûÂ±9Ò@ÏûÊÕ´∏160161772001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï’Òò^i␀␀ÂHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  201503162MASXJ21561518p1722525                            @tëU2a|@1l‡uˆ˝"@RÅXbM”¿<_ÏV’œ´@apHËßÁ@ÏûÊÕ´∏1@Ïû˜?r‘£60161772002@’π-F
