icipated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              NICER                                                                                               ␀␀␀␀ToO                                                                                                                     archived  20200429MRK0315                                           ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ïü#Ü@ÏüÕ´∏160361015001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï’7`U␀␀ÂHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. One of the principal goals of the NuSTAR extragalactic surveys is to constrain the high-energy X-ray luminosity function and trace its evolution as a function of redshift and AGN obscuration. We will continue to pursue a multi-layer survey strategy, expanding the number of deep fields, and increasing the area of shallow observations through serendipitous sources.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀ELS       Extragalactic Legacy Surveys                                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316MRK0315                                           @u†ô0æÌ@6®ßÊö‘@W#'ª/Ï¿@Ì*ô0æ@b$.±ƒ2 @ÏüÕ´∏1@Ïü1î»)¯60361015002@Ÿ9ˆ Wßá@ŸjO@€\ƒõ•„@€‹ƒõ•„SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï’ÔÂïn␀␀ÂHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀NuSTAR will continue both Galactic and Extragalactic legacy Surveys during the extended mission with programs selected based on community input. One of the principal goals of the NuSTAR extragalactic surveys is to constrain the high-energy X-ray luminosity function and trace its evolution as a function of redshift and AGN obscuration. We will continue to pursue a multi-layer survey strategy, expanding the number of deep fields, and increasing the area of shallow observations through serendipitous sources.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀A    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀ELS       Extragalactic Legacy Surveys                                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar CME                     Swift                                                                                               ␀␀␀NuLANDS / Kp=7                                                                                                          archived  20200429MCG_03_58_007                                     ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ïü1î»)¯@Ïü2#Ü60502004001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï’Ô∏ÀHp␀␀Ê¶Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀H7We propose a monitoring campaign of 4x60 ks simultaneous XMM & 4x40 ks NuSTAR observations of MCG-03-58-007, which is a powerful and variable disk wind. A Suzaku observation unveiled the presence of a high ionization, high Nh and fast (v~ 0.1c) wind launched from within a few 100Rg from the black hole. A follow-up 130ks simultaneous XMM/NuSTAR observation confirmed the presence of the wind and showed a Nh~1e24cm-2 variation in a day, which we ascribe to an increase of the Nh of the wind. Such dramatic variability places MCG-03-58-007 among the unique objects, and makes it an ideal AGN to map the inner disk-wind. With the new observations we will: probe the origin of the Nh variations, reveal the structure of the wind and determine how the wind responds to the continuum.                    Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Braito                        Valentina                     NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀X18       Monitoring the extremely variable fast disk wind in MCG-03-58-007                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316MCG_03_58_007                                     @uf≥–|Ñ∂¿39x‘˝Û∂@DÎ)^û	¿Nh™d¬¯8@`#è≈Åo@Ïü2#Ü@ÏüOxVb‹60502004002@‰AF
