ck hole. With the existing 50 ksec observation, we plan to perform a simultaneous fit to the spectra using modern disk atmosphere models, where we attempt to describe the spectra with a common mass, distance, spin, and system inclination. These results will be compared to and used to 'normalize' a similar fit to existing RXTE spectra. The posterior probably estimates from these fits will be combined with theoretical models of disk color correction factors to make a prediction of the likely range of the black hole system parameters, and help verify that it is indeed a maximally spinning black hole.                                                                                            Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Nowak                         Michael                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       USING NUSTAR TO ASSESS THE MASS, SPIN, DISTANCE, AND FE LINE OF 4U 1957+11                                              ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  201503164U_1957p11                                        @rΩßÔù≤-@'|C,•zx@Ió+I∫¿"N_o“ @`QQÇ©ì@ÏüPèFj@Ïüm±9Ò30402011006@‚≥	kπå@‚‘â†'R@‰Øäi≠Bƒ@‰∞*i≠BƒSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï’Ó§±~K␀␀ÊtHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀ÕWe propose three, 35 ksec observations of 4U 1957+11, potentially the most rapidly spinning Galactic black hole. With the existing 50 ksec observation, we plan to perform a simultaneous fit to the spectra using modern disk atmosphere models, where we attempt to describe the spectra with a common mass, distance, spin, and system inclination. These results will be compared to and used to 'normalize' a similar fit to existing RXTE spectra. The posterior probably estimates from these fits will be combined with theoretical models of disk color correction factors to make a prediction of the likely range of the black hole system parameters, and help verify that it is indeed a maximally spinning black hole.                                                                                            Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Nowak                         Michael                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       USING NUSTAR TO ASSESS THE MASS, SPIN, DISTANCE, AND FE LINE OF 4U 1957+11                                              ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀(3/3)                                                                                                                   archived  20200429ESO533_50                                         ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ïüm±9Ò@Ïün?r‘£60061312001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï’Óx!_Ù␀␀ÂHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316ESO533_50                                         @u+a|⁄Q¿9•õ=»K@;íÒ©˚Ám¿M†Xy=Ÿ@`KÜ¬&Äù@Ïün?r‘£@Ïü}ÍM60061312002@÷k6ïÈ·±@÷BW~êˇó@◊ÓÆnóçP@◊ÓÆnóçPSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï’Ó3cæƒ␀␀ÂHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429Circinus_X1                                       ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ïü}ÍM@Ïü~±9Ò30401013001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï’Ì˙Ä0å␀␀ÊtHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀%No direct measurements currently exist of the magnetic field of an accreting neutron star at its birth. We propose to use the unparalleled NuSTAR hard X-ray sensitivity to observe the youngest known accreting neutron star low-mass X-ray binary, the puzzling Cir X-1 with an age of 5000 years. With a 60 ks observation in the source's low flux state, we will constrain Cir X-1's accretion geometry, aiming for a first estimate of the magnetic field in this very young neutron star, and characterise its ill-understood persistent low flux state.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Van Den Eijnden               Jakob                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       THE MAGNETIC FIELD OF THE YOUNGEST ACCRETING NEUTRON STAR                                                               ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                   