␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï®€ÍM@Ï®‹î»)¯60502053001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï’∂≠À©á␀␀ÁπHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ùOn Sept 22, 2017, the IceCube observatory reported the detection of the high-energy astrophysical neutrino candidate event IC170922A. A large multiwavelength observation campaign of the neutrino location involving led to the detection of enhanced broadband EM emission from the blazar TXS 0506+056. This detection represents the first evidence for an electromagnetic counterpart to the high-energy astrophysical neutrinos detected by IceCube. The soft-to-hard X-ray emission from the source provides the most sensitive diagnostics of the hadronic contribution to the source SED. We here propose an ambitious observational program of TXS 0506+056 involving NuSTAR, Swift, VERITAS and Fermi.                                                                                                               Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    SANTANDER                     J_MARCOS                      NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N05       PROBING THE HADRONIC EMISSION FROM THE CANDIDATE NEUTRINO BLAZAR TXS 0506+056                                           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316TXS_0506p056                                      @SXÍJå@ÁRT`™e@hhÉ‰%ÆÊ¿3‘ÍJåM@`Á¸π#¢ú@Ï®‹î»)¯@Ï®Ó#Ü60502053002@’˙√a@@’‘VT`™e@◊{∏␀␀␀␀@◊|x␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï’∂f¯	␀␀ÁπHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀ùOn Sept 22, 2017, the IceCube observatory reported the detection of the high-energy astrophysical neutrino candidate event IC170922A. A large multiwavelength observation campaign of the neutrino location involving led to the detection of enhanced broadband EM emission from the blazar TXS 0506+056. This detection represents the first evidence for an electromagnetic counterpart to the high-energy astrophysical neutrinos detected by IceCube. The soft-to-hard X-ray emission from the source provides the most sensitive diagnostics of the hadronic contribution to the source SED. We here propose an ambitious observational program of TXS 0506+056 involving NuSTAR, Swift, VERITAS and Fermi.                                                                                                               Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    SANTANDER                     J_MARCOS                      NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N05       PROBING THE HADRONIC EMISSION FROM THE CANDIDATE NEUTRINO BLAZAR TXS 0506+056                                           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              Swift                                                                                               ␀␀␀␀(1/5)                                                                                                                   archived  202004293C410                                             ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï®Ó#Ü@Ï®Ô#Ü60463069001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï’∂<}Í␀␀ÂWHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+