ç␀␀Ê‚Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀We have discovered a new member of the rare and poorly understood class of high-mass gamma-ray binaries: 3FGL J1405.4-6119. The system shows gamma-ray, radio and X-ray modulation on its 13.7 day period, with different patterns at each waveband. The existing X-ray data, while clearly showing the period, are insufficient to perform phase-resolved spectroscopy, which is needed to investigate the physics driving the emission and its orbital variability.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    CORBET                        ROBIN                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N05       PHYSICAL PROCESSES IN THE NEW GAMMA-RAY BINARY 3FGL J1405.4-6119                                                        ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  201503163FGL_J1405d4m6119                                 @jgÈ˘rG¿N©a‰˜e˛@sxµsÍ≥?€¢úwökQ@ +Ö∏QÏ@Ï´ÍÍM@Ï¨(ÍM30502015004@ı1:BZÓc@ıw“àŒp@ˆµÊS&¬@ˆ∏6S&¬SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï’•¬ß°Ú␀␀Ê‚Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀We have discovered a new member of the rare and poorly understood class of high-mass gamma-ray binaries: 3FGL J1405.4-6119. The system shows gamma-ray, radio and X-ray modulation on its 1