                                                             Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀ToO                                                                                                                     archived  20200429UGC11397                                          ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï¨K±9Ò@Ï¨L#Ü60161704001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï’§”Wõ‡␀␀ÂvHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316UGC11397                                          @qﬁ ¿Éo@@ÈÖoiD@P-\˙¨ŸË@(˝IQÇ©ì@ K]ÃcÒA@Ï¨L#Ü@Ï¨\±9Ò60161704002@÷˘q„º”@÷ ÂY≥–}@ÿÅvÄùIR@ÿÅ6ÄùIRSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï’§è\(ˆ␀␀ÂvHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429EXO_1846m031                                      ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï¨\±9Ò@Ï¨]?r‘£80502303003␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï’§f5⁄’␀␀Ê”Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    7I¡We propose a large multiwavelength campaign (120 ks Chandra HETGS, NuSTAR, JVLA/ATCA, NICER, Swift, Gemini) on a black hole transient to study the influence of ionized winds on relativistic jets and state transitions. With a reimagined observing strategy based on new results on integrated RMS variability and a decade of radio/X-ray monitoring, we will search for winds during and after the state transition to test their influence on and track their coevolution with the disk and the jet over the next 2-3 months. Our spectral and timing constraints will provide precise probes of the accretion geometry and accretion/ejection physics.                                                                                                                                                                   Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Neilsen                       J                             NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀C20       An Integrated Approach to Winds, Jets, and State Transitions                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316EXO_1846m031                                      @q§ßÊö‘¿Õ“Ò©˚Á@=«†˘	k∫øÊHËßÊõ@uâÔù≤-@Ï¨]?r‘£@Ï¨p#Ü80502303004@÷ 4∫«À@÷_˚Ùá¸π@‹q¨ÿD–@‹rlÿD–SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï’£œå¥á␀␀Ê”Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  7I¡We propose a large multiwavelength campaign (120 ks Chandra HETGS, NuSTAR, JVLA/ATCA, NICER, Swift, Gemini) on a black hole transient to study the influence of ionized winds on relativistic jets and state transitions. With a reimagined observing strategy based on new results on integrated RMS variability and a decade of radio/X-ray monitoring, we will search for winds during and after the state transition to test their influence on and track their coevolution with the disk and the jet over the next 2-3 months. Our spectral and timing constraints will provide precise probes of the accretion geometry and accretion/ejection physics.                                                                                                                                                                   Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Neilsen                       J                             NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀C20       An Integrated Approach to Winds, Jets, and State Transitions                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              Chandra                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀(2/4) ToO                                                                                                               archived  20200429GRO_J2058p42                                      ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï¨p#Ü@Ï¨pÕ´∏190501336001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï’£§Pg)␀␀ÂvHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, bu