icipated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀(1/2) ToO / Sun proximity no CHU4                                                                                       archived  201503162MASXJ14302986p1339117                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏπM?r‘£@ÏπN[‰õø60463047001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï’e(î´m␀␀Â’Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  201503162MASXJ14302986p1339117                            @k5HÀí:@+Lø±[W?@Gy¶µ@O∏Xy=Ÿ@hΩiDg8@ÏπN[‰õø@Ïπ]#Ü60463047002@”Ü˘ôôôö@”b˙˛≈m]@‘Ìô/üæ@‘Óô/üæSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï’d‡∂a␀␀Â’Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              Chandra                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429Maffei_1                                          ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ïπ]#Ü@Ïπ^èFj50401005003␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï’d≥ß¢␀␀ÁCHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀≤As NuSTAR enters its sixth year of operations, it has yet to perform a deep observation of an elliptical galaxy to study the low-mass X-ray binary (LMXB) population associated with older stellar ages. Maffei 1 is the nearest giant elliptical galaxy at 3.4 Mpc and as such provides a unique environment to investigate the accreting black hole (BH) and neutron star (NS) populations in the sensitive E>10 keV bandpass. Due to its proximity, it is the only elliptical where the resolved X-ray binary (XRB) population can be studied at hard X-ray energies until a next generation hard X-ray telescope is flown. We request a 200 ks NuSTAR observation of the giant elliptical galaxy Maffei 1 to study the formation channels of NS and BH populations both in globular cluster (GC) and field environments.    Normal galaxies                                             ␀1    Vulic                         Neven                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       THE GIANT ELLIPTICAL GALAXY HIDING IN OUR BACKYARD: THE RESOLVED X-RAY BINARY POPULATION IN MAFFEI 1                    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Maffei_1                                          @CòbM“Ò™@M“ïÈ·∞ä@`¯Ì(åÁøÊQŒ_p@'R WßÜ¬@Ïπ^èFj@Ïπ¶ÍM50401005004@¯ÌBò_˜@¯∫“·∞â†@˙ßçµ‹∆?@˙´ùµ‹∆?SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï’d-Çÿ␀␀ÁCHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀≤As NuSTAR enters its sixth year of operations, it has yet to perform a deep observation of an elliptical galaxy to study the low-mass X-ray binary (LMXB) population associated with older stellar ages. Maffei 1 is the nearest giant elliptical galaxy at 3.4 Mpc and as such provides a unique environment to investigate the accreting black hole (BH) and neutron star (NS) populations in the sensitive E>10 keV bandpass. Due to its proximity, it is the only elliptical where the resolved X-ray binary (XRB) population can be studied at hard X-ray energies until a next generation hard X-ray telescope is flown. We request a 200 ks NuSTAR observation of the giant elliptical galaxy Maffei 1 to study the formation channels of NS and BH populations both in globular cluster (GC) and field environments.    Normal galaxies                                             ␀1    Vulic                         Neven                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N04       THE GIANT ELLIPTICAL GALAXY HIDING IN OUR BACKYARD: THE RESOLVED X-RAY BINARY POPULATION IN MAFFEI 1                    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              Chandra                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429NGC_925_ULX3                                      ¿X¿␀␀