s well as the observatory optical alignment. NuSTAR will also participate in cross-calibration campaigns with the Chandra, XMM-Newton, Swift, and Suzaku X-ray observatories.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Calibration Observations                                    ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀CAL       NuSTAR calibration campaign                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Kepler                                            @pk@∑Ä4n¿5l¨1&È@ÕOﬂ;dZ@IÓÀ˚µ@c¶ø±[W?@Ï≈“[‰õø@Ï∆±9Ò10601005002@¯F@'ª/Ï@¯ﬁ2a|@˘¸Û9Xb@˘¸√9XbSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï‘ˆ®|e§␀␀ÊLHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀Observations of celestial sources will be undertaken throughout the mission to determine, and then monitor changes to, the calibration of the X-ray observatory. Observations will enable the calibration of absolute flux, spectral sensitivity, point spread function, and the timing capabilities of the observatory as well as the observatory optical alignment. NuSTAR will also participate in cross-calibration campaigns with the Chandra, XMM-Newton, Swift, and Suzaku X-ray observatories.                                                                                                       