␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‘∆]≠RM␀␀ÊLHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316IRAS05589p2828                                    @V°!ˇ.HÈ@<qƒ2 W®@f√¶µ(@ıé!ñRΩ@t»•ú‡v@Ï»§ÍM@Ï»∫#Ü60061062002@‹ñÈ©˚Ám@‹[>◊s¸@ﬁük/ÏV÷@ﬁ†k/ÏV÷SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï‘∆
ûá∆␀␀ÊLHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429Mrk_142                                           ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï»∫#Ü@Ï»∫±9Ò60560028001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‘≈›dÄÛ␀␀ÁøHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀Super-Eddington accretion periods are expected to be extremely important to explain the fast growth of the first supermassive black holes. However, among all accretion modes, this phase is still the least understood one, and it is still largely debated what are the physical properties of the accretion flow and of the X-ray source at very high accretion rates. We propose here a systematic broad-band X-ray study of super-Eddington AGN at z < 0.1 by simultaneously observing three sources with NuSTAR and XMM-Newton. These three AGN have the highest Eddington ratios in the SEAMBHs sample, which contains exclusively objects with black hole masses estimated from reverberation mapping, making the Eddington ratio estimates extremely reliable.                                                         Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    RICCI                         CLAUDIO                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N05       THE FIRST SYSTEMATIC BROAD-BAND X-RAY STUDY OF EXTREME ACCRETION ONTO SUPERMASSIVE BLACK HOLES WITH NUSTAR AND XMM      ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Mrk_142                                           @cäYJÙÿ@I‘Ìëhr∞@d!6zêó@JÉã¨q≥@2n.±ƒ3@Ï»∫±9Ò@Ï»ÔÕ´∏160560028002@Ú]§uˆ˝"@Ú5<Œp:˚@Ûû¶µ@ÛüÈ¶µSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï‘≈s|ç␀␀ÁøHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀Super-Eddington accretion periods are expected to be extremely important to explain the fast growth of the first supermassive black holes. However, among all accretion modes, this phase is still the least understood one, and it is still largely debated what are the physical properties of the accretion flow and of the X-ray source at very high accretion rates. We propose here a systematic broad-band X-ray study of super-Eddington AGN at z < 0.1 by simultaneously observing three sources with NuSTAR and XMM-Newton. These three AGN have the highest Eddington ratios in the SEAMBHs sample, which contains exclusively objects with black hole masses estimated from reverberation mapping, making the Eddington ratio estimates extremely reliable.                                                         Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    RICCI                         CLAUDIO                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N05       THE FIRST SYSTEMATIC BROAD-BAND X-RAY STUDY OF EXTREME ACCRETION ONTO SUPERMASSIVE BLACK HOLES WITH NUSTAR AND XMM      ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429ESO137_34                                         @oÇ©ì·¿M†˘	k∫@tê©˚Álã¿§%ÆÊ1˘@gÄYJÙÿ@Ï»ÔÕ´∏1@Ï»Ò#Ü60061272003␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï‘≈;ã0*␀␀ÊLHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           