   NULL                                                        ␀X17       Prompt XMM-Newton and NuSTAR study of magnetar outbursts                                                                ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀(4b/4) ToO                                                                                                              archived  20200429Mrk_335                                           ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï”[‰õø@Ï”[‰õø80502636003␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï”"Æ¶ï␀␀ÁXHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀OMrk 335 is a NLSy1 highly variable in flux and spectral shape. We aim to observe it with NuSTAR when it is in an intermediate state. We request an observation of 140 ks to be performed simultaneously with our accepted TOO Chandra/HETG and NICER observations. NuSTAR observations will help us to constrain the continuum, reflection properties and the broadened Fe-K line. The simultaneous observation with HETGS will give us information on the absorbers structures, as these winds are particularly visible in an intermediate state, and NICER will help to constrain the strong soft excess. The broad-band spectral analysis including NuSTAR, HETGS, NICER and possibly optical observations on this particular state will help to understand the structure and behavior of this variable source.              Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    BOISSAY MALAQUIN              ROZENN                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N05       INVESTIGATION ON MRK 335 IN AN INTERMEDIATE STATE                                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                         