U∂l␀␀ÊÕHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316NGC2788A                                          @`Ú¶L/É{¿Q±[W>´@q¿≠B√…Ô¿,=ÃcÒA @R2ìtº@ÏÿgÕ´∏1@ÏÿvÕ´∏160160344002@÷ûB«À)@÷o␀h€å@ÿE%*ô1@ÿIÂ*ô1SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏÿáÒÆ÷©␀␀ÊÕHea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429PSR_J1357m6429                                    @j%4÷°aÂ¿PÍ≥g†˘@s\␀␀␀␀␀¿nóçP@ä=p£◊
@ÏÿvÕ´∏1@Ïÿw?r‘£40660006001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏÿáÕß@⁄␀␀Ë:Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀PThe proposal seeks a unique opportunity to collect legacy NuSTAR data and explore pulsar wind nebula (PWN) astrophysics at the deepest level through multi-wavelength SEDs, in synergy with the existing and near-future TeV gamma-ray telescopes. NuSTAR observations of 8 additional PWNe will complete the sampling of all 22 TeV-PWNe detectable by NuSTAR. Our targets includes PWNe detected by HAWC above 50 TeV, PWNe crushed by reverse SNR shocks, a young PWN in the Galactic Center and the archetype Vela nebula. Some of the nebulae may contain a hadronic outflow which produces TeV gamma-rays via interacting with the ISM or dense clouds. NuSTAR can probe sub-PeV electron populations through X-ray synchrotron spectra and allow us to perform spectro-imaging studies of PWNe above 10 keV.             Non-ToO Supernovae, Supernova Remnants, and Galactic diffuse␀1    Mori                          Kaya                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N06       NUSTAR HARD X-RAY SURVEY OF PULSAR WIND NEBULAE IN SYNERGY WITH TEV GAMMA-RAY TELESCOPES                                ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316PSR_J1357m6429                                    @j%˝ä⁄πı¿P ]càeï@s\"–Â`B¿RΩ<6@;dZ¨@Ïÿw?r‘£@ÏÿØèFj40660006002@ˆû,ö@ˆnG‡uˆ˝@¯,ì#9¿Ï@¯-”#9¿ÏSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏÿÀÏ®d␀␀Ë:Hea_10Apr2020_V6.27.1_nustardas_01Apr20_v1.9.2                                  ␀␀PThe proposal seeks a unique opportunity to collect legacy NuSTAR data and explore pulsar wind nebula (PWN) astrophysics at the deepest level through multi-wavelength SEDs, in synergy with the existing and near-future TeV gamma-ray telescopes. NuSTAR observations of 8 additional PWNe will complete the sampling of all 22 TeV-PWNe detectable by NuSTAR. Our targets includes PWNe detected by HAWC above 50 TeV, PWNe crushed by reverse SNR shocks, a young PWN in the Galactic Center and the archetype Vela nebula. Some of the nebulae may contain a hadronic outflow which produces TeV gamma-rays via interacting with the ISM or dense clouds. NuSTAR can probe sub-PeV electron populations through X-ray synchrotron spectra and allow us to perform spectro-imaging studies of PWNe above 10 keV.             Non-ToO Supernovae, Supernova Remnants, and Galactic diffuse␀1    Mori                          Kaya                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N06       NUSTAR HARD X-RAY SURVEY OF PULSAR WIND NEBULAE IN SYNERGY WITH TEV GAMMA-RAY TELESCOPES                                ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200429AT2019wey                                         @Q9sÍ≥g°@K¥º£@b·Ø∑È@ì&¡Ω•@cúç∏ª@ÏÿØèFj@Ïÿ∞[‰õø90601315003␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏÿÀ™íd‚␀␀ÊÕHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, 