                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Sokoloski                     Jennifer                      NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀X19       lucy@astro.columbia.edu                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200811NGC1106                                           ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï€ß[‰õø@Ï€®?r‘£60160130001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï€¬dÄÚ∫␀␀Ê‚Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316NGC1106                                           @ETÌëhr∞@Dÿ∑Ä4m∆@b.3úæ‡¿0j~˘€#@_iN;Õ5®@Ï€®?r‘£@Ï€∂Õ´∏160160130002@’ŒµÖoi@’ú≠<64@◊B$—∑Y@◊B$—∑YSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï€¬L¥á␀␀Ê‚Hea_11Aug2020_V6.28_nustardas_19Jun20_v2.0.0                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200811ABELL_3395                                        ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï€∂Õ´∏1@Ï€∑±9Ò70601003001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï€¬*íd‚␀␀ËVHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀BClusters of galaxies are the largest virialized objects in the universe. Since the unknown physics lies at high energy phenomena and the mergers of these objects are the most energetic events in the universe, they are inherently interesting. Shocks and turbulence driven by these mergers as well as their interaction with cosmic web structures are yet to be understood, and our knowledge of the pre-merger dynamics is limited. We propose to observe the cluster Abell 3395, which is at a pre-merger state. We aim to obtain the first observational evidence of the interaction between shock heated regions and intercluster filaments, as well as to unveil the dynamics of the merger. NuSTAR's high sensitivity at hard X-ray energy band will enable precise measurements of high temperature regions.       Galaxy clusters and extragalactic diffuse objects           ␀1    Tumer                         Aysegul                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N06       PRE-MERGER DYNAMICS OF ABELL 3395                                                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀               