                   archived  20200811SWIFTJ1448d2m8033                                 @kπ33333¿T#º@s:–©*0¿2¶lÙ!-@9åø±[W?@Ï›÷[‰õø@Ï›◊?r‘£60464116001@y&[¿6„@xÙ8}øH@z¿␀␀␀␀␀@z¿␀␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï›„‰h¨Ò␀␀Ê˜Hea_11Aug2020_V6.28_nustardas_19Jun20_v2.0.0                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20200811SWIFTJ1448d2m8033                                 @k∏[¿6„¿T#xF‹]@s:≥–|Ñ∂¿2ßRT`™e@9ï8Ô4÷°@Ï›◊?r‘£@Ï›ﬂ[‰õø60464116002@“ö]IQÇ™@“pú7¥¢4@”·˝˚Álã@”„}˚ÁlãSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï›„—äm¸␀␀Ê˜Hea_11Aug2020_V6.28_nustardas_19Jun20_v2.0.0                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀Kp=5                                                                                                                    archived  20200811Vela_X1                                           ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï›ﬂ[‰õø@Ï›ﬂÍM90602328003␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï›„∏	+␀␀Ê˜Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Vela_X1                                           @`Ò$›/¿D@ËßÊõ@pmË>BZÓ@AΩ•ú‡@_Vzêñº@Ï›ﬂÍM@Ï›Á?r‘£90602328004@¬ºàeîØO@¬Õ[6zë@«Ú£&¡æ@«Ú£&¡æSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ïﬁﬂ1Æ◊␀␀Ê˜Hea_11Aug2020_V6.28_nustardas_19Jun20_v2.0.0                                    ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀(2/3) ToO / idiagnostics                                                                                                archived  20200811ABELL_478                                         ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï›Á?r‘£@Ï›ËèFj70660002001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏﬁƒDDD␀␀ËkHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀›Galaxy clusters are the most massive virialized objects in the universe, and their growth over cosmic time is sensitive to the underlying cosmology. Cluster cosmology requires accurate mass measurements, which generally depend on temperature measurements. Unfortunately, the main sources for X-ray temperatures are Chandra and XMM, which systematically disagree with each other. The hard band sensitivity of NuSTAR, however, has the potential to resolve this discrepancy and reduce the error budget on cluster-derived cosmological parameters. We propose deep observations of 4 low redshift, relaxed clusters, with extensive XMM and Chandra (and future XRISM) data, where both calibration and physical differences can be assessed in the simplest possible systems.          