ed  20200811FRB_20200120E                                     ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏÁﬁ±9Ò@ÏÁﬂ?r‘£80701506001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏÁ„âÂt␀␀Ë±Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    WSLFast Radio Bursts (FRBs) are a new class of astrophysical transient of unknown origins. The CHIME/FRB project is now operational and discovering several FRBs per day. A fraction of the sources are repeating and can potentially be localized to arcsecond precision using radio interferometers. These precise localizations will enable a deep search for X-ray counterparts of the radio bursts. Some models, notably those involving magnetars, predict X-ray bursts along with FRBs which may be detectable with Chandra or NuSTART for nearby sources. We therefore propose for 54 ks of Chandra ToO observations to be scheduled along with 15 hr of Effelsberg and 27 ks of NuSTAR observations on a well-localized CHIME/FRB repeater.                                                                               Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Scholz                        Paul                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀C22       Simultaneous Chandra, NuSTAR and Radio Observations of CHIME-discovered repeating FRBs                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316FRB_20200120E                                     @b±ò«‚ÇA@Q7,•zxl@aƒd¬¯7µ@DÑ”ZÖáî@aè*0U2a@ÏÁﬂ?r‘£@ÏÁÌ[‰õø80701506002@◊7èiDg8@◊ºÍJå@ÿ”p€ã¨q@ÿ’∞€ã¨qSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏË^†#␀␀Ë±Hea_11Aug2020_V6.28_nustardas_19Jun20_v2.0.0         