on of multi-phase outflows.                                 Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Bianchi                       Stefano                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N06       BUILDING SUBWAYS: THE NUSTAR LINE                                                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20200811LBQS1338m0038                                     @i´éÛMjøÎ“Ú‰éä@t|~êˇó$@M‹˙¨ŸË>@f˛\ë—N@ÏÍÿ?r‘£@ÏÍˇ[‰õø60661020002@È8Ìw1è≈@Ë˙Ò€"–Â@Í˜Õª/ÏW@Í¯mª/ÏWSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏÎÃ;*␀␀ËÕHea_11Aug2020_V6.28_nustardas_19Jun20_v2.0.0                                    ␀␀úA Large Program (1.58 Ms) has been granted in XMM-Newton AO18 and 27 orbits have been awarded in HST Cycle 27 to study Supermassive Black Hole Winds in X-rays (SUBWAYS), designed to provide direct support on feedback models by deriving constraints on the energetics and duty cycle of Ultra-Fast Outflows (UFOs) in Active Galactic Nuclei. We ask now for NuSTAR observations of the 20 SUBWAYS sources (630 ks) without archival NuSTAR data. The availability of NuSTAR data above 10 keV is crucial for the objectives of SUBWAYS, and will maximise the outcome of this ambitious Large Program. The proposed observations represent a fundamental step to maintain NuSTAR science upfront during the next decade in the physically motivated investigation of multi-phase outflows.                                 Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Bianchi                       Stefano                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N06       BUILDING SUBWAYS: THE NUSTAR LINE                                                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20200811PG0844p349                                        ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏÍˇ[‰õø@ÏÎ␀#Ü60463024001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏÎ#G}àÍ␀␀Á`Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀S