ties to combine NuSTAR s capability for highly sensitive remote X-ray observation with PSP s powerful suite of in-situ instruments. By arranging these co-observations, the capacity of NuSTAR and PSP will be used in tandem to examine connectivity between the corona and the inner heliosphere. Additionally, solar observations performed at these times will allow the NuSTAR observatory to continue to contribute to the rich, multi-instrument solar datasets achieved when the heliophysics community unites in support of each PSP perihelia.    Solar System Objects                                        ␀1    Duncan                        Jessie                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N06       COORDINATED NUSTAR OBSERVATION IN SUPPORT OF SIX EARTH-SIDE PARKER SOLAR PROBE PERIHELIA                                ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR only                                                                                                            archived  20150316IGRJ16318_SADA_21014                              ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÏÎï±9Ò@ÏÎñÕ´∏190601014001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏÎ¬ ˛›␀␀ÁgHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                                   