                                                          Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316SRGA_J181414d6m225604                             @qx‘˝Û∂¿6Ê‚ÎC-@ õ"–Â`B¿ #9¿ÎÓ@cLò_˜@Ï˜èèFj@Ï˜®ÍN90701314002@·∑v„º”[@·ã9…‰@„:¨1'@„:¨1'SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï˜›9æG␀␀Á¬Hea_11Aug2020_V6.28_nustardas_19Jun20_v2.0.0                                    ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀ToO PI De                                                                                                               archived  20210315M82                                               ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï˜®ÍN@Ï˜©ÍN30602027003␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï˜›W;␀␀È6Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀EThe galaxy M82 harbors two notable ultraluminous X-ray sources (ULX): M82 X-2, the archetipal pulsating ultraluminous X-ray source (PULX), and M82 X-1, a IMBH candidate. The extreme luminosity of ULXs, and the observation of strong winds from these sources, suggests that these sources are undergoing strongly super-Eddington accretion. The supply of matter that powers these accreting systems is likely to come from Roche Lobe overflow from a more massive companion star, and should produce changes of orbital period observable in time scales of ~years. This program aims at detecting this orbital period derivative through pulsar timing in M82 X-2, and study in detail the quasi-periodic oscillations from both ULXs.                                                                                  Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Bachetti                      Matteo                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N06       BROADBAND TIMING OF THE ULTRALUMINOUS X-RAY SOURCES IN M82: ORBITAL DECAY, QPOS, AND MORE.                              ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STE