¶L0¿B9Ç©ì·@n~($x¿@q·∞â†'@5WökP∞Ú@Ï˘?±9Ò@Ï˘@[‰õø60160232001@wô⁄QŒ@wa∫^5?}@yL¸PH@yL¸PHSCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï˘ED’Ê¯␀␀Á–Hea_11Aug2020_V6.28_nustardas_19Jun20_v2.0.0                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20210315PKS0521m36                                        @T,bM“Ò™¿B9ÓÀ˚µ@nàŒp:˚¿@s]ÃcÒA@5Ç&ÄùIR@Ï˘@[‰õø@Ï˘PÍN60160232002@÷¯”√a@÷≈√∑È˘@ÿ~Ÿâ7K«@ÿ~Ÿâ7K«SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ï˘aÓz·␀␀Á–Hea_11Aug2020_V6.28_nustardas_19Jun20_v2.0.0                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic su