¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ï˙ûxVb‹@Ï˙û±9Ò80701332001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ï˙£z”†␀␀ËëHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀bWe propose a 50 ks NuSTAR TOO observation of a transient black hole (BH) source during outburst. Using Swift/XRT to determine the source state, we will trigger the NuSTAR observation when the source transitions from the hard state to its intermediate state. Modeling of reflection features in the source spectrum will be used to measure the BH spin, as well as constrain the environment of the innermost accretion disk. We will only target sources that have not yet been observed by NuSTAR during outburst, whether that means an entirely new BH candidate or a previously known BH source that has been in quiescence since the launch of NuSTAR. Examples of such sources include GRO J1655-40 and 4U 1543-475, allowing us to test different methods for measuring the black hole spin.                      Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Coughenour                    Benjamin                      NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N07       SPIN AND REFLECTION IN A BLACK HOLE TRANSIENT                                                                           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316MAXI_J1803m298                                    @pÏÂ`Aâ7¿=Ã∆??≈÷8ÜYK¿£◊
