e components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316FBQSJ1159p2914                                    @fz7¥¢3ú@=8r∞ ƒú@h‰’œ™Õü@SÑ«‚Ç@∏@v~˘€"—@Ïˇ—èFj@Ïˇ›?r‘£60463037004@—/S3333@—~xl"h@“_LÿD–@“_LÿD–SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÏˇÏóÉö\␀␀ËHea_11Aug2020_V6.28_nustardas_19Jun20_v2.0.0                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20210315SgrAstar_SADA_21176                               ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ïˇ›?r‘£@Ïˇﬁ?r‘£30602122001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÏˇÏy\Î$␀␀ÍûHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ÛWe propose two long (143 ks) continuous NuSTAR exposures to cover 8 nights of VLTI-Gravity+(XMM-or-Chandra) observations of Sgr A*. The required exposure time of Gravity, XMM and Chandra have been already secured. The Gravity team has recently measured the astrometric motion of the near infrared (NIR) source during three bright NIR flux excursions of Sgr A*. Simultaneous NuSTAR+Gravity observations will allow us to understand the evolution of the radiative mechanism and to test whether, during bright X-ray flares, the NIR source will display similar circular orbital motions or whether it will be characterised by a dramatically different pattern, such as by linear motions, reminiscent of jet like ejections. This will provide us with a groundbreaking test of accretion physics.               Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Ponti                         Gabriele                      NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N06       THE MOTION OF SGR A*'S NIR SOURCE DURING X-RAY FLARES                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR / SADA setup                                                                                                    archived  20150316SgrAstar                                          @p¶ô0æÌ¿=
