s of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀ToO / idiagnostics / Sun proximity no CHU4                                                                              archived  20210315Sol_21321_DL                                      ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÌıÕ´∏1@Ìˆ[‰õø20601017001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì‚û†#␀␀ËîHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀sThe goal of this proposal is to take advantage of opportunities for co-observation between NuSTAR and the Parker Solar Probe (PSP) during six of the PSP perihelia ocurring during NuSTAR GO Cycles 6 & 7. These Earth-facing perihelia provide compelling opportunities to combine NuSTAR s capability for highly sensitive remote X-ray observation with PSP s powerful suite of in-situ instruments. By arranging these co-observations, the capacity of NuSTAR and PSP will be used in tandem to examine connectivity between the corona and the inner heliosphere. Additionally, solar observations performed at these times will allow the NuSTAR observatory to continue to contribute to the rich, multi-instrument solar datasets achieved when the heliophysics community unites in support of each PSP perihelia.    Solar System Objects                                        ␀1    Duncan                        Jessie                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N06       COORDINATED NUSTAR OBSERVATION IN SUPPORT OF SIX EARTH-SIDE PARKER SOLAR PROBE PERIHELIA                                ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR / idiagnostics / Sun proximity no CHU4                                                                          archived  20150316Sol_21321_SADA                                    ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ìˆ[‰õø@ÌˆÕ´∏120601018001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì‚ãHpC␀␀ËîHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀sThe goal of this proposal is to take advantage of opportunities for co-observation between NuSTAR and the Parker Solar Probe (PSP) during six of the PSP perihelia ocurring during NuSTAR GO Cycles 6 & 7. These Earth-facing perihelia provide compelling opportunities to combine NuSTAR s capability for highly sensitive remote X-ray observation with PSP s powerful suite of in-situ instruments. By arranging these co-observations, the capacity of NuSTAR and PSP will be used in tandem to examine connectivity between the corona and the inner heliosphere. Additionally, solar observations performed a