                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀ToO / Sun proximity no CHU4 / idiagnostics / SL-A3B3 (GX 9+1)                                                           archived  20210315AT2021ehb                                         ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ì[‰õø@ÌxVb‹80701509001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì·´Ê5€␀␀ÈSHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀»A growing number of tidal disruption events (TDEs) are expected to be discovered by the ongoing Spektrum-Roentgen-Gamma (SRG) all-sky X-ray survey. We propose 2x40ks NuSTAR observations on two subgroups of SRG-discovered TDEs with hard X-ray emission. For non-relativistic TDEs with non-thermal X-ray emission, the observation will allow us to search for spectral features characteristic of relativistic reflection. For relativistic TDEs, this will provide the highest resolution hard X-ray spectrum ever obtained, shedding light on the power mechanism of TDE jets.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Yao                           Yuhan                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N07       NUSTAR OBSERVATIONS OF TIDAL DISRUPTION EVENTS                                                                          ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316AT2021ehb                                         @Gm„º”[@D'␀h€ã¨@b†D–©*¿/xbM“Ú@Fê«‚Ç@∏@ÌxVb‹@Ì<èFj80701509002@Â¸«À)@‰‡n_ˆî@Êæ‹–©*@Ê¿\–©*SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì·å˝X^␀␀ÈSHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀»A growing number of tidal disruption events (TDEs) are expected to be discovered by the ongoing Spektrum-Roentgen-Gamma (SRG) all-sky X-ray survey. We propose 2x40ks NuSTAR observations on two subgroups of SRG-discovered TDEs with hard X-ray emission. For non-relativistic TDEs with non-thermal X-ray emission, the observation will allow us to search for spectral features characteristic of relativistic reflection. For relativistic TDEs, this will provide the highest resolution hard X-ray spectrum ever obtained, shedding light on the power mechanism of TDE jets.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Yao                           Yuhan                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N07       NUSTAR OBSERVATIONS OF TIDAL DISRUPTION EVENTS                                                                          ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              NICER                                                                                               ␀␀␀␀ToO / idiagnostics / SL-B01 (NGC 1275)                                                                                  archived  20210315Sol_21323_DL                                      ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ì<èFj@Ì=?r‘£20601019001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì·\A;ã␀␀ËùHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀sThe goal of this proposal is to take advantage of opportunities for co-observation between NuSTAR and the Parker Solar Probe (PSP) during six of the PSP perihelia ocurring during NuSTAR GO Cycles 6 & 7. These Earth-facing perihelia provide compelling opportunities to combine NuSTAR s capability for highly sensitive remote X-ray observation with PSP s powerful suite of in-situ instruments. By arranging these co-observations, the capacity of NuSTAR and PSP will be used in tandem to examine connectivity between the corona and the inner heliosphere. Additionally, solar observations performed at these times will allow the NuSTAR observatory to continue to contribute to the rich, multi-instrument solar datasets achieved when the heliophysics community unites in support of each PSP perihelia.    Solar System Objects                                        ␀1    Duncan                        Jessie                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N06       COORDINATED NUSTAR OBSERVATION IN SUPPORT OF SIX EARTH-SIDE PARKER SOLAR PROBE PERIHELIA                                ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀