Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              NICER                                                                                               ␀␀␀␀ToO                                                                                                                     archived  20210315Cen_X3                                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ì‚î»)¯@Ì„Õ´∏130701019001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì1Møá␀␀Í@Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀GWe propose a 180 ks NuSTAR observation of the high mass X-ray binary Cen X-3. The duration covers two orbital periods of the system. Through the orbital- and pulse-phase resolved spectroscopy, it is possible to track variations of spectral parameters such as the photon index, CRSF line energy, and cut-off energy. Combined with Monte Carlo simulation, these spectral parameters can be connected with certain physical interpretations by simulating complex physical processes taking place in the accretion column, such as thermal bremsstrahlung, Comptonization, and magnetic field effects. The observation data with two successive orbits will also reveal long-term stability of surrounding photo-ionized plasma in the wind of the companion by examining spectral variations of the successive orbits.   Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Tamba                         Tsubasa                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N07       THREE-DIMENSIONAL VIEW OF THE MAGNETIZED ACCRETION FLOW ONTO CENTAURUS X-3                                              ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Cen_X3                                            @eMöu%¿NNäqﬁi≠@r?ùIQÇ™?€∑È˘rG@h[ˆîFt@Ì„Õ´∏1@Ìlî»)¯30701019002Ac‚M“ÚAú≠w1êAâ„A [¿Aã#tSéÛSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ìï¿E…␀␀Í@Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀GWe propose a 180 ks NuSTAR observation of the high mass X-ray binary Cen X-3. The duration covers two orbital periods of the system. Through the orbital- and pulse-phase resolved spectroscopy, it is possible to track variations of spectral parameters such as the photon index, CRSF line energy, and cut-off energy. Combined with Monte Carlo simulation, these spectral parameters can be connected with certain physical interpretations by simulating complex physical processes taking place in the accretion column, such as thermal bremsstrahlung, Comptonization, and magnetic field effects. The observation data with two successive orbits will also reveal long-term stability of surrounding photo-ionized plasma in the wind of the companion by examining spectral variations of the successive orbits.   Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Tamba                         Tsubasa                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N07       THREE-DIMENSIONAL VIEW OF THE MAGNETIZED ACCRETION FLOW ONTO CENTAURUS X-3                                              ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              Solar flare                                                                                         ␀␀␀idiagnostics / M-class solar flare / Kp=6                                                                               archived  20210315AKARI_J1126p1639                                  ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ìlî»)¯@Ìm[‰õø60701030001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌåÎÕ␀␀Í@Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ÙULIRGs/HyLIRGs are thought to represent the rapidly growing phase of massive galaxies before quenching of star formation by AGN-driven outflows. A HyLIRG, J1126 at z ~ 0.5, was found with the fastest ionized outflow among ULIRGs/AGNs at z < 1. However, the star formation in J1126 is vigorous with SFR over 1000 Msun/yr. In order to reveal the physical mechanism behind the puzzling co-existence of the extreme outflow and SFR, we try to constrain the dust covering factor (CF) using the intrinsic AGN X-ray luminosity with NuSTAR observation. A large CF could imply that the powerful wind is limited by a small opening angle and has not affected the main part of the nuclear starburst; while a CF similar to typical AGNs could suggest AGN wind is not effective in the quenching of star formation.   Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Chen                          Xiaoyang                      NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N07       X-RAY VIEW OF A Z ~ 0.5 HYLIRG: SHARING EXTREME OUTFLOW AND STARBURST IN ONE PLACE                                      ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316AKARI_J1126p1639                                  @eyµsÍ≥@0Æz·GÆ@mÉdZ¨@PÌLò_˜@eìtºj@Ìm[‰õø@Ì©èFj60701030002@ÙâS&@ÛAWôôôö@ıåª/ÏW@ıÄºª/ÏWSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì√≤(3î␀␀Í@Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1          