ry as well as the observatory optical alignment. NuSTAR will also participate in cross-calibration campaigns with the Chandra, XMM-Newton, Swift, and Suzaku X-ray observatories.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Calibration Observations                                    ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀CAL       NuSTAR calibration campaign                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20210315Crab_deepbkgd                                     @RøjÁ’fœ@*Àí:*@gm´üUõ=¿1· ¿Éo@tuVlÙ!@Ì}ÍN@ÌòÍN10802004002@‚␀ ƒõ¶@·’“[¿7@„h0␀␀␀␀@„h0␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì¬U=ç␀␀Ë˝Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀␀␀Observations of celestial sources will be undertaken throughout the mission to determine, and then monitor changes to, the calibration of the X-ray observatory. Observations will enable the calibration of absolute flux, spectral sensitivity, point spread function, and the timing capabilities of the observatory as well as the observatory optical alignment. NuSTAR will also participate in cross-calibration campaigns with the Chandra, XMM-Newton, Swift, and Suzaku X-ray observatories.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Calibration Observations                                    ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀CAL       NuSTAR calibration campaign                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀Background Calibration / idiagnostics                                                                                   archived  20210315Sol_22057_DL                                      ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÌòÍN@ÌôÕ´∏120601027001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì»I+<␀␀Ë˝Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀sThe goal of this proposal is to take advantage of opportunities for co-observation between NuSTAR and the Parker Solar Probe (PSP) during six of the PSP perihelia ocurring during NuSTAR GO Cycles 6 & 7. These Earth-facing perihelia provide compelling opportunities to combine NuSTAR s capability for highly sensitive remote X-ray observation with PSP s powerful suite of in-situ instruments. By arranging these co-observations, the capacity of NuSTAR and PSP will be used in tandem to examine connectivity between the corona and the inner heliosphere. Additionally, solar observations performed at these times will allow the NuSTAR observatory to continue to contribute to the rich, multi-instrument solar datasets achieved when the heliophysics community unites in support of each PSP perihelia.    Solar System Objects                                        ␀