ia.    Solar System Objects                                        ␀1    Duncan                        Jessie                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N06       COORDINATED NUSTAR OBSERVATION IN SUPPORT OF SIX EARTH-SIDE PARKER SOLAR PROBE PERIHELIA                                ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR / dogleg                                                                                                        archived  20150316GRS_1758m258                                      ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ì£Õ´∏1@Ì§ÍN90801302001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì«ë␀␀Ë˝Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316GRS_1758m258                                      @pÂ©˚Álã¿9≤ WßÜ¬@´Ö∏QÏøÒœAÚ◊s@c%T…Öo@Ì§ÍN@Ìµî»)¯90801302002@‘∏ìtºj@‘õªÒA \@◊UüAÚ◊@◊X_AÚ◊SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì∆ÎÖ∏␀␀Ë˝Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀ToO / idiagnostics                                                                                                      archived  202103154U_1543m475                                       @mõí:)«z¿G‘64Í@t¨≈m\˙≠@{J#9¿Ï@e@‡uˆ˝"@Ìµî»)¯@Ì∂èFj80701319001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì«bR≠≥␀␀È±Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀UX-ray reflection in accreting black holes probes the inner region of the accretion disc, and proper modelling of the spectral and timing properties of this emission enables measurement of the black hole mass and spin. The unique combination of NICER s soft and NuSTAR's hard coverage provide the broad bandpass, high count rates and energy and timing resolution required to constrain models of the time averaged energy spectrum and the reverberation lag energy spectrum on different timescales. We propose to observe any black hole transient, known or unknown, exceeding 30 mCrab during the bright hard state for 30 ks with simultaneous NICER and NuSTAR observation in order to access unprecedented characterisation of black hole spin and mass.                                                        Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Mastroserio                   Gugleilmo                     NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀R03       MEASURING BLACK HOLE SPIN AND MASS THROUGH X-RAY REFLECTION SPECTRA AND REVERBERATION LAGS                              ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  201503164U_1543m475                                       @mõ$tSéÛ¿G“◊s¸P@t¨√…ÓÀ˚@â†'RTa@eI¶µ(@Ì∂èFj@Ì–Õ´∏180701319002@„o\üæv…@„N3¿6„@Â^ÀK∆ß@Â_ÎK∆ßSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIG