allow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar flare                                                                                                                       ␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20220215EFEDS_SRCID_56                                    @a‚e+‘?¯ù≤-V@là∆?@>|C,•zx@uŸy¶µ@Ì&QÕ´∏1@Ì&RxVb‹60762004001@nN;Õ5®@mø∞â†'R@p␀␀␀␀␀@p␀␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì&a˝—∫˙␀␀Í©Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀qThe eROSITA instrument on-board Spectrum-Roentgen-Gamma (SRG) has performed the first imaging all-sky survey in the hard X-ray (2-10keV) band. The final survey will be over 30 times deeper than previous hard X-ray surveys, yielding a large and very pure sample of AGN. Combining eROSITA data with observations from other multi-wavelength missions, a detailed picture of the AGN population can be constructed, including black hole mass, luminosity, and spectral shape. We propose simultaneous NuSTAR+XMM-Newton follow up observations of a group of hard X-ray selected AGN observed with eROSITA. This pilot study will demonstrate the power of joint NuSTAR and XMM observations to break degeneracies present in different spectral models, motivating future joint NuSTAR, XMM and eROSITA investigations.  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Waddell                       Sophia                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N07       PHYSICAL CONSTRAINTS FROM AGN X-RAY SPECTRA: A PILOT NUSTAR-XMM STUDY OF EROSITA-SELECTED SOURCES                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20220215EFEDS_SRCID_56                                    @ar∞ ƒú?¯∂E° ¿É@làSéÛMj@>zêñªô@u€∫«À)@Ì&RxVb‹@Ì&ÇÍN60762004002@fvQÎÖ@:˘Œp:˚@Òåkπå~@Òç{kπå~SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì&§ºﬂ␀␀Í©Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀qThe eROSITA instrument on-board Spectrum-Roentgen-Gamma (SRG) has performed the first imaging all-sky survey in the hard X-ray (2-10keV) band. The final survey will be over 30 times deeper than previous hard X-ray surveys, yielding a large and very pure sample of AGN. Combining eROSITA data with observations from other multi-wavelength missions, a detailed picture of the AGN population can be constructed, including black hole mass, luminosity, and spectral shape. We propose simultaneous NuSTAR+XMM-Newton follow up observations of a group of hard X-ray selected AGN observed with eROSITA. This pilot study will demonstrate the power of joint NuSTAR and XMM observations to break degeneracies present in different spectral models, motivating future joint NuSTAR, XMM and eROSITA investigations.  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Waddell                       Sophia                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N07       PHYSICAL CONSTRAINTS FROM AGN X-RAY SPECTRA: A PILOT NUSTAR-XMM STUDY OF EROSITA-SELECTED SOURCES                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar flare                   XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀X-class solar flare CME Kp=5                                                                                            archived  20220215CGCG312m012                                       ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ì&ÇÍN@Ì&Éî»)¯60160365001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì&£ﬁ–ó¥␀␀È<Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316CGCG312m012                                       @a…a‰˜e˛@OC˛\ë—N@bÌcàeîØ@Dæ§®¡T @vOﬂ;dZ@Ì&Éî»)¯@Ì&íÍN60160365002@÷Éf≈m\˚@÷G¯<ûÏ¿@ÿ'˜ŒŸ@ÿg˜ŒŸSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì&€fñÒ¯␀␀È<Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20220215Cyg_X2                                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ì&íÍN@Ì&ì±9Ò30801012001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì&£§‚	‹␀␀ÈÙHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀gWe propose one 20 ks NuSTAR observation of Cyg X-2 to measure the geometry of the innermost accretion region in this NS LMXB. Our observation will be taken on the same day as the pre-decided IXPE observation of the same source. The proposed NuSTAR observation will provide a complementary spectral view of the reflection spectrum of the accretion disk in Cyg X-2. By modeling the reflection spectrum, we will be able to compare our spectral measurements of the disk with the first polarization measurement of the source. Meanwhile, NuSTAR will also provide a broadband monitoring of the source during the day and look for any significant flux changes, e.g. dips or thermonuclear outbursts.                                                                                                               Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Jiang                         Jiachen                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       SIMULTANEOUS NUSTAR AND IXPE MEASUREMENTS OF THE DISK REFLECTION SPECTRUM IN CYG X-2                                    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Cyg_X2                                            @tcÑµ‹∆?@C.;Õ5®X@UÀo“ÚÂ¿&âÓÀ˚µ@cÁlãCñ@Ì&ì±9Ò@Ì&£èFj30801012002@Õ´√¿6„@Œ<‘"h	’@◊TU…‰@◊TU…‰SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì&◊≠À©á␀␀ÈÙHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀gWe propose one 20 ks NuSTAR observation of Cyg X-2 to measure the geometry of the innermost accretion region in this NS LMXB. Our observation will be taken on the same day as the pre-decided IXPE observation of the same source. The proposed NuSTAR observation will provide a complementary spectral view of the reflection spectrum of the accretion disk in Cyg X-2. By modeling the reflection spectrum, we will be able to compare our spectral measurements of the disk with the first polarization measurement of the source. Meanwhile, NuSTAR will also provide a broadband monitoring of the source during the day and look for any significant flux changes, e.g. dips or thermonuclear outbursts.                                                                                                               Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Jiang                         Jiachen                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       SIMULTANEOUS NUSTAR AND IXPE MEASUREMENTS OF THE DISK REFLECTION SPECTRUM IN CYG X-2                                    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              IXPE                                                                                                ␀␀␀␀idiagnostics                                                                                                            archived  20220215SDSSJ1100p0846                                    @düÁlãCñ@!|Ìëhs@nB‹]càf@LﬁßÔù≤-@vg¯7¥¢4@Ì&£èFj@Ì&§#Ü60763001001@P(…Öoi@OÚ~˘€"—@Q4–©*0@Q4–©*0SCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì&◊ä=p§␀␀Í©Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀áThe intrinsic column density (NH) distribution of quasars is poorly known. Many optically selected obscured quasars show indirect evidence of being heavily obscured, at or above the Compton-thick threshold. Such buried QSO2s are extremely challenging to study at X-ray energies of E < 10 keV. NuSTAR is unique in its ability to constrain NH for buried QSO2s, and thus reveal the hidden accretion power of these most extreme sources. Despite this, only five buried QSO2s have been detected with NuSTAR, with even fewer having sufficient counts for spectral modelling. The primary aim of this proposal is to double the number of NuSTAR-observed buried QSO2s with direct constraints on NH (at a precision of D log NH < 0.2), by observing five promising new targets, with a total exposure of 220 ks.     Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Lansbury                      George                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N07       HIDDEN POWER: DOUBLING THE NUSTAR CENSUS OF BURIED TYPE 2 QUASARS                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20220215SDSSJ1100p0846                                    @d†␀—∑Y@!Ç&ÄùIR@nB∫«À)@Lﬂ_o“Û@vg$›/@Ì&§#Ü@Ì&·Õ´∏160763001002@Û∑g˛\ë—@ÛÑˇûÉ‰&@ı »á+@ı#(á+SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì'_IÙü␀␀Í©Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀áThe intrinsic column density (NH) distribution of quasars is poorly known. Many optically selected obscured quasars show indirect evidence of being heavily obscured, at or above the Compton-thick threshold. Such buried QSO2s are extremely challenging to study at X-ray energies of E < 10 keV. NuSTAR is unique in its ability to constrain NH for buried QSO2s, and thus reveal the hidden accretion power of these most extreme sources. Despite this, only five buried QSO2s have been detected with NuSTAR, with even fewer having sufficient counts for spectral modelling. The primary aim of this proposal is to double the number of NuSTAR-observed buried QSO2s with direct constraints on NH (at a precision of D log NH < 0.2), by observing five promising new targets, with a total exposure of 220 ks.     Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Lansbury                      George                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N07       HIDDEN POWER: DOUBLING THE NUSTAR CENSUS OF BURIED TYPE 2 QUASARS                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar flare                                                                                                                       ␀␀␀X-class solar flare                                                                                                     archived  20220215PG1116p215                                        ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ì&·Õ´∏1@Ì&‚#Ü60463034001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì'¸˜G␀␀È<Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316PG1116p215                                        @e7Ü¬&Äù@5Pê-‡@kŸ"–Â`B@P¸µ‹∆?@®r∞ ƒú@Ì&‚#Ü@Ì&ÚÍN60463034002@’ê}øH@‘œÇ+jÁ’@÷Ö	∫^5?@÷á	∫^5?SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì';ã0␀␀È<Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar flare                                                                                                                       ␀␀␀M-class solar flare                                                                                                     archived  20220215MKN421                                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ì&ÚÍN@Ì&Û?r‘£60701031001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì'üÏ_í∆␀␀Í∞Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀˙The investigators propose to observe up to 6 X-ray bright blazars plus the radio galaxy Cen A with NuSTAR during X-ray linear polarization measurements by the Imaging X-ray Polarimetry Explorer (IXPE). The 0.3-70 keV continuum spectrum derived from synchronous NuSTAR and Swift observations will allow modeling needed to interpret the IXPE polarization data. Comparison of millimeter-wave, optical, and X-ray polarization, and measurement of the mm/optical/UV/X-ray continuum spectra of the blazars and Cen A with NuSTAR, Swift, and ground-based telescopes, will provide data needed to determine the mechanism and location of the X-ray emission, which have yet to be determined conclusively. It will also test models for particle acceleration that produces high-energy emission in relativistic jets. Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Marscher                      Alan                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N07       MULTI-ENERGY X-RAY OBSERVATIONS OF IXPE BLAZAR TARGETS                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316MKN421                                            @d¡4÷°aÂ@CÎC,•@fyC,•z@P-fœAÚ@"ÓÛMj@Ì&Û?r‘£@Ì'èFj60701031002@ÿ(Wa@O@◊Í∞ﬁ“àŒ@⁄˘∫^5?@⁄π∫^5?SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì'†l/5␀␀Í∞Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀˙The investigators propose to observe up to 6 X-ray bright blazars plus the radio galaxy Cen A with NuSTAR during X-ray linear polarization measurements by the Imaging X-ray Polarimetry Explorer (IXPE). The 0.3-70 keV continuum spectrum derived from synchronous NuSTAR and Swift observations will allow modeling needed to interpret the IXPE polarization data. Comparison of millimeter-wave, optical, and X-ray polarization, and measurement of the mm/optical/UV/X-ray continuum spectra of the blazars and Cen A with NuSTAR, Swift, and ground-based telescopes, will provide data needed to determine the mechanism and location of the X-ray emission, which have yet to be determined conclusively. It will also test models for particle acceleration that produces high-energy emission in relativistic jets. Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Marscher                      Alan                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N07       MULTI-ENERGY X-RAY OBSERVATIONS OF IXPE BLAZAR TARGETS                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              IXPE MAGIC XMM                                                                                      ␀␀␀M-class solar flares                                                                                                    archived  20220215MCGp00m29m023                                     ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ì'èFj@Ì'î»)¯60701041001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì'†Œ˚”␀␀Í∞Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀The proposed observation of six obscured AGN are necessary to obtain a complete and uniform coverage of the X-ray emission for the sample of Seyfert-2 galaxies from the 12micron galaxy sample (12MGS). Coupled with the broad-band X-ray observations available for the remaining 12MGS AGN, the proposed observations will allow us to investigate the column density distribution at low redshift for a complete and unbiased AGN sample (because of its mid-IR selection) and to connect the accretion properties to those of the hosts by exploiting the unique multi-band characterization and coverage of the proposed sample.                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Salvestrini                   Francesco                     NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N07       UNVEILING THE INTRINSIC X-RAY PROPERTIES OF THE 12 MICRON SY2 SAMPLE: TOWARDS A COMPLETE X-RAY COVERAGE                 ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316MCGp00m29m023                                     @eHsÅ◊€ı¿ˇó$tT@ppóˆ+jË@J_™ÕûÉ‰@v≈m\˙≠@Ì'î»)¯@Ì'î»)¯60701041002@Ÿó®xG@ŸVg8~@€QCK∆ß@€R√K∆ßSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì'°˝X^␀␀Í∞Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀The proposed observation of six obscured AGN are necessary to obtain a complete and uniform coverage of the X-ray emission for the sample of Seyfert-2 galaxies from the 12micron galaxy sample (12MGS). Coupled with the broad-band X-ray observations available for the remaining 12MGS AGN, the proposed observations will allow us to investigate the column density distribution at low redshift for a complete and unbiased AGN sample (because of its mid-IR selection) and to connect the accretion properties to those of the hosts by exploiting the unique multi-band characterization and coverage of the proposed sample.                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Salvestrini                   Francesco                     NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N07       UNVEILING THE INTRINSIC X-RAY PROPERTIES OF THE 12 MICRON SY2 SAMPLE: TOWARDS A COMPLETE X-RAY COVERAGE                 ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar flare                   XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀M-class flare                                                                                                           archived  202202152MASXJ11475508p0902284                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ì'î»)¯@Ì'ÍN60160454001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì'•∏ÀHp␀␀ÈCHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                          