utmost importance to understanding the heating of the primordial IGM. This program, to observe five starbursting, High Mass X-ray Binary (HMXB)-dominated galaxies, for a total of 1.49 Ms with NuSTAR and 207 ks with XMM-Newton, will provide a representative sample of starburst galaxies for establishing the connection between the 12-25~keV emission arising from neutron star and black hole populations and their host galaxy properties that is highly relevant to high-z galaxies. We will double the number of HMXB-dominated galaxies with measured 0.5-30~keV Spectral Energy Distributions, so we may correctly interpret high-z galaxies' X-ray emission where we only sample the rest-frame hard X-ray emission.               Normal galaxies                                             ␀1    Hornschemeier                 Ann                           NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N07       THE BIRTH OF BLACK HOLES AND NEUTRON STARS IN STARBURSTS: A LEGACY FOR NUSTAR BUILDING ON A HST TREASURY PROGRAM        ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316NGC_4490                                          @grÜYJÙÒ@D‘64Í@aWoiDg@R™E° ¿É@!å<ûÏø±@Ì*„ÍN@Ì+0±9Ò50760003004@˙«ò/É{J@˙}
