CER, to supplement existing coverage of Cyg X-1, LMC X-3, and GRS 1915+105: three persistently bright, variable, and impactful black hole systems. Regular monitoring of these dynamic systems at the ~100 day timescale commensurate to their variability enables a multitude of science return and establishes a lasting data archive of some of the richest sources in the X-ray sky.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Steiner                       James                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       NUSTAR+NICER MONITORING OF THREE PERSISTENT AND VARIABLE BLACK HOLES                                                    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316LMC_X3                                            @U, ƒõ•„¿P˛≈m\˚@q≈m\˙≠¿@ÛMj@Tw‰%ÆÊ2@Ì.ïxVb‹@Ì.£?r‘£30802016002@÷m3ökP±@÷7∏ØOÑ@ÿ#k]ÃcÒ@ÿ'k]ÃcÒSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì.ƒVÒ˜®␀␀ÎJHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀£We propose a monitoring campaign, using NuSTAR plus NICER, to supplement existing coverage of Cyg X-1, LMC X-3, and GRS 1915+105: three persistently bright, variable, and impactful black hole systems. Regular monitoring of these dynamic systems at the ~100 day timescale commensurate to their variability enables a multitude of science return and establishes a lasting data archive of some of the richest sources in the X-ray sky.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Steiner                       James                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       NUSTAR+NICER MONITORING OF THREE PERSISTENT AND VARIABLE BLACK HOLES                                                    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀(1/4)                                                                                                                   archived  20220215MS_22549m3712                                     ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ì.£?r‘£@Ì.£ÍN60801032001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì.ƒ50Ï®␀␀Í:Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ We request 200ks NuSTAR observations of the AGN MS 22549-3712 and PG 1244+026, the two remaining members of the sample of Seyfert galaxies in which iron K reverberation time delays have been significantly detected that have not yet been observed by NuSTAR. The primary objective is to measure the spectrum of the X-rays reflected from the accretion disk that are expected to give rise to these time delays. These measurements will be important to validate the X-ray reverberation model, to determine the consistency between the X-ray spectrum and the observed time lags, and to enable the tightest constrains on the structure of the corona and the spin of the black holes.                                                                                                                                Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Wilkins                       Daniel                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       COMPLETING HARD X-RAY OBSERVATIONS OF THE IRON K REVERBERATION SAMPLE OF SEYFERT GALAXIES                               ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316MS_22549m3712                                     @uÜ˙¨ŸË>¿Bt˙¨ŸË>@∫)«y¶µ¿OÏûÏø±[@c.∆?@Ì.£ÍN@Ì//èFj60801032002AárGE9AEcI∫^A
