nóçPSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì2Éå¥á␀␀ÈûHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20220215PG_1244p026                                       ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ì2qÕ´∏1@Ì2sèFj60801033001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì2ÉlGL˝␀␀Í]Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ We request 200ks NuSTAR observations of the AGN MS 22549-3712 and PG 1244+026, the two remaining members of the sample of Seyfert galaxies in which iron K reverberation time delays have been significantly detected that have not yet been observed by NuSTAR. The primary objective is to measure the spectrum of the X-rays reflected from the accretion disk that are expected to give rise to these time delays. These measurements will be important to validate the X-ray reverberation model, to determine the consistency between the X-ray spectrum and the observed time lags, and to enable the tightest constrains on the structure of the corona and the spin of the black holes.                                                                                                                                Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Wilkins                       Daniel                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       COMPLETING HARD X-RAY OBSERVATIONS OF THE IRON K REVERBERATION SAMPLE OF SEYFERT GALAXIES                               ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316PG_1244p026                                       @gÚŒp:˚@∆
