%*€␀␀ÍìHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀ The ultraluminous X-ray source population is now broadly expected to be dominated by super-Eddington accretors, thanks to the broadband spectroscopy provided by NuSTAR and XMM in combination, and the detection of X-ray pulsations from a growing subset of ULXs (unambiguously confirming them as super-Eddington neutron stars). IC5052 ULX and ESO501-023 ULX are extreme ULXs (Lx,peak > 1e40 erg/s) that have received very little observational attention to date. Here, we propose coordinated 100+50 ks NuSTAR+XMM observations of these sources in order to constrain their broadband spectra and search for pulsations. These observations will provide the first robust constraints on the nature of these two extreme binary systems.                                                                            Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Walton                        Dominic                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       BROADBAND OBSERVATIONS OF NEW ULXS: IC5052 ULX AND ESO501-023 ULX                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20220215IC5052_ULX                                        @sê™ÕûÉ‰¿QQ:í£@tQ%ÆÊ1˘¿AÀ◊
