         Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              IXPE                                                                                                ␀␀␀␀DDT / idiagnostics                                                                                                      archived  20220215SWIFT_J2103d3m2144                                @sºÌ˙C˛]¿5€üUõ=@9O!-w1ê¿BˇˆîFt@s∑˛\ë—N@Ì:ûî»)¯@Ì:ü#Ü60860010001@c∑Œ_p@cáüUõ=@dÁ˝ä⁄πı@dÁ˝ä⁄πıSCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì:¢Ωπu1␀␀ÍìHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀óNearby powerful AGN provide the best way to understand the growth of supermassive black holes and their effect on galaxies. Most recently, the BASS survey has identified a sample of 12 highly luminous obscured AGN (5e44-1e46 ergs/s) at 0.2<z<0.4, that have never before been observed in the X-rays outside of short Swift XRT exposures. NuSTAR observations enable accurate X-ray spectral modeling of of NH, Fe Ka, and intrinsic X-ray luminosity to test models of Eddington limited feedback. This survey would form a complete census of the 17 most luminous obscured AGN at z<0.6 detected in the ultra-hard X-rays, providing a template of high luminosity luminosity obscured AGN emission above 10 keV.                                                                                                      Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Koss                          Michael                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       A SURVEY OF THE MOST LUMINOUS HARD X-RAY SELECTED OBSCURED QUASARS AT Z=0.2-0.4                                         ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀       