␀␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌB®iX␀␀Í“Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀ We request to observe 11 high redshift blazars with NuSTAR for a total of 400 ks. All found beyond redshift 4, these sources are prototypical MeV blazars, and some of the most powerful of their class. However, they crucially lack hard-Xray measurements. NuSTAR will allow us to accurately detect the rising part of the inverse Compton spectrum up to 50 keV, expected to be very hard. This will be fundamental to determine the position of the high-energy peak, hence confirming their MeV blazar nature. Further, NuSTAR will enable us to determine the power of the jet, deriving the underlying electron population responsible for the emission and measuring the location of the emission region.                                                                                                             Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Marcotulli                    Lea                           NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       UNCOVERING THE MOST POWERFUL JETS AT THE DAWN OF COSMIC TIME                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20220215BZQ_J2102p6015                                    @s∫v_ÿ≠¨@NéÛMj@Xsˆ+jÁ’@!¯_ˆîF@ri®¡T…Ü@ÌB£î»)¯@ÌBÃ±9Ò60863010002@ÓMfœAÚ@Ì˛:›/†@'≤ƒ2 X@(¬ƒ2 XSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÌBÎ4œ’Ü␀␀Í“Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀ We request to observe 11 high redshift blazars with NuSTAR for a total of 400 ks. All found beyond redshift 4, these sources 