                ␀␀«Masquerading BL Lacs are an elusive class of blazars, which comprises of FSRQs appearing as disguised BL Lac objects. In this work, we will unveil a potential target in an attempt to understand the nature of these sources and how they fit in the blazar population. We propose this source to be observed with {\it NuSTAR} and XMM-Newton to help us construct a multiwavelength Spectral Energy Distribution. This will assist us in revealing some essential characteristics of this intriguing object. As the recent detection of high-energy neutrinos by IceCube in the direction of TXS 0506+056 shows, these masquerading BL Lacs may be responsible for the astrophysical IceCube neutrino flux, proving that there is more to them than meets the eye.                                                           Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Rajagopal                     Changam                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       UNVEILING MASQUERADING BL LAC OBJECTS                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316NVSS_J152048m034850                               @l»QÎÖ∏¿Yá+@v_ﬂ;dZ@E`eîØO@eæ0U2a|@ÌG¶?r‘£@ÌGÃÕ´∏160801021002@Ëä`ûö@ËGI&¡æ@ÍG,)«yß@ÍG¨)«yßSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÌGÈÓ¶ï␀␀Í˚Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀«Masquerading BL Lacs are an elusive class of blazars, which comprises of FSRQs appearing as disguised BL Lac objects. In this work, we will unveil a potential target in an attempt to understand the nature of these sources and how they fit in the blazar population. We propose this source to be observed with {\it NuSTAR} and XMM-Newton to help us construct a multiwavelength Spectral Energy Distribution. This will assist us in revealing some essential characteristics of this intriguing object. As the recent detection of high-energy neutrinos by IceCube in the direction of TXS 0506+056 shows, these masquerading BL Lacs may be responsible for the astrophysical IceCube neutrino flux, proving that there is more to them than meets the eye.                                                           Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Rajagopal                     Changam                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       UNVEILING MASQUERADING BL LAC OBJECTS                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM SARA                                                                                            ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20220215eRASSU_J012422m724248                             ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÌGÃÕ´∏1@ÌGÕ±9Ò90901301001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌGÈªªªº␀␀ÍFHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                               