 blazars.                                                                                                                                                                                             Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Paliya                        Vaidehi                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       THE QUEST FOR ELUSIVE COSMIC MONSTERS                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316BZQ_J1100m4249                                    @d®…Öoi¿Eh¸PH@q†¬&ÄùI@/9≥–|Ñ∂@iÏSéÛMj@ÌH5xVb‹@ÌHd[‰õø60862009002@Ô&©S&@ÓœÑeîØO@£$Y≥–}@¢‘Y≥–}SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÌHä€¯j␀␀ÎHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀ÌWe propose joint XMM and NuSTAR observations of 12 high-redshift (z > 3) blazars which exhibit brightest and flattest X-ray spectra and host massive (>1e9 Msun) black holes. Joint Xmm and NuSTAR observations will lead to the most accurate estimation of the beaming factor which will allow us to put stringent constraint on the space density of blazar parent population, and in turn, the evolution of massive black holes in jetted AGNs within the first two billion years. Using XMM+NuSTAR data, we will also probe the role played by the intergalactic medium in the X-ray absorption towards high-redshift blazars.                                                                                                                                                                                             Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Paliya                        Vaidehi                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       THE QUEST FOR ELUSIVE COSMIC MONSTERS                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM                                                                                                 ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20220215BZQ_J1445p0958                                    ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÌHd[‰õø@ÌHeèFj60862003001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌHâ€ˆ$␀␀ÎHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ÌWe propose joint XMM and NuSTAR observations of 12 high-redshift (z > 3) blazars which exhibit brightest and flattest X-ray spectra and host massive (>1e9 Msun) black holes. Joint Xmm and NuSTAR observations will lead to the most accurate estimation of the beaming factor which will allow us to put stringent constraint on the space density of blazar parent population, and in turn, the evolution of massive black holes in jetted AGNs within the first two billion years. Using XMM+NuSTAR data, we will also probe the role played by the intergalactic medium in the X-ray absorption towards high-redshift blazars.                                                                                                                                                                                             Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Paliya                        Vaidehi                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       THE QUEST FOR ELUSIVE COSMIC MONSTERS                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀