                                                        ␀␀␀␀SADA rally / INERTIAL only                                                                                              archived  20220215G351d9m0d9                                        ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÌKî»)¯@ÌK #Ü40801004001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌKB=Í␀¬␀␀ÎHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ÖThe black hole X-ray binary Swift J1728.9-3613 is coincident with the supernova remnant G351.9-0.9. An extensive analysis concludes that the two are likely associated, marking this remnant as window on a black hole progenitor star, a black hole formation event, and subsequent interactions between the compact object and ejecta. G351.9-0.9 is detected in radio bands, in soft X-rays, and with Fermi. We request an 80 ks observation with NuSTAR in order to explore the spatial variation in non-thermal X-ray emission, and to determine spectral slopes with the accuracy required to constrain emission mechanisms via comparisons to radio and gamma-ray slopes.                                                                                                                                                Non-ToO Supernovae, Supernova Remnants, and Galactic diffuse␀1    Miller                        Jon                           NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       A NUSTAR LOOK AT G351.9-0.9                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316G351d9m0d9                                        @pdÅ$›/¿BŒp:˚@u˝´6zëøÊ1&