                      ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  202202154U1630m472                                        ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÌMäî»)¯@ÌMãî»)¯80801327001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌM±Ω@␀␀Î/Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀iWe propose a 30 ks NuSTAR ToO observation of a black hole X-ray binary in the very high state. With this observation, we will combine the two leading relativistic spectroscopy methods, relativistic reflection and continuum fitting, to make two simultaneous, independent measurements of the spin of the central BH. This combined approach is more powerful than either method applied individually, and has great potential for expanding our knowledge of BH formation and growth, accretion physics and strong gravity. In addition, an extended disk reflection model with a variable density parameter for the surface of the disk will be considered particularly.                                                                                                                                                  Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Jiang                         Jiachen                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       STUDYING THE VERY HIGH STATE OF BLACK HOLE TRANSIENTS USING RELATIVISTIC SPECTROSCOPY                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  201503164U1630m472                                        @o£n.≤¿GÆ§®¡T @u¡Ω•ù?ﬂI∫^5@dµá+@ÌMãî»)¯@ÌMßèFj80801327002@«¿C›óˆ+@»ºuoiD@ÿü„9¿ÎÓ@ÿ†£9¿ÎÓSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÌM∆∞␀␀Î/Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀iWe propose a 30 ks NuSTAR ToO observation of a black hole X-ray binary in the very high state. With this observation, we will combine the two leading relativistic spectroscopy methods, relativistic reflection and continuum fitting, to make two simultaneous, independent measurements of the spin of the central BH. This combined approach is more powerful than either method applied individually, and has great potential for expanding our knowledge of BH formation and growth, accretion physics and strong gravity. In addition, an extended disk reflection model with a variable density parameter for the surface of the disk will be considered particularly.                                                                                                                                                  Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Jiang                         Jiachen                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       STUDYING THE VERY HIGH STATE OF BLACK HOLE TRANSIENTS USING RELATIVISTIC SPECTROSCOPY                                   ␀␀_„␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀ToO / idiagnostics / data gaps 24547s                                                                                   archived  20220215MAXI_J1834m021                                    ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÌMßèFj@ÌMßî»)¯90901309001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌM≈Á“}(␀␀ÍwHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           No