M‰bÉ9E␀␀Î/Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀óNearby powerful AGN provide the best way to understand the growth of supermassive black holes and their effect on galaxies. Most recently, the BASS survey has identified a sample of 12 highly luminous obscured AGN (5e44-1e46 ergs/s) at 0.2<z<0.4, that have never before been observed in the X-rays outside of short Swift XRT exposures. NuSTAR observations enable accurate X-ray spectral modeling of of NH, Fe Ka, and intrinsic X-ray luminosity to test models of Eddington limited feedback. This survey would form a complete census of the 17 most luminous obscured AGN at z<0.6 detected in the ultra-hard X-rays, providing a template of high luminosity luminosity obscured AGN emission above 10 keV.                                                                                                      Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Koss                          Michael                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       A SURVEY OF THE MOST LUMINOUS HARD X-RAY SELECTED OBSCURED QUASARS AT Z=0.2-0.4                                         ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  201503162MASS_J17422050                                   @pöq≤ïÍ¿I›≤-V@u>S&¡æ¿%˚•„S˜œ@c)%F
