n-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  201503164U_1820m303                                       @q?>´6z¿>Q∑X‚@tá¸π#£¿ë∑X‚@c],•zxl@ÌRSxVb‹@ÌRaÍN90902308004@ÕõÙá¸π$@ŒGr˛≈m]@÷ÛMj@÷ÛMjSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÌRä Ü␀␀ÍöHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              IXPE                                                                                                ␀␀␀␀(2/2) DDT / idiagnostics                                                                                                archived  20220215SLX_1746m331                                      ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÌRaÍN@ÌRb?r‘£80802346005␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌRâÒ3ı␀␀ÎQHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ The distribution of spins across stellar mass black holes (BH) is currently not well understood. NuSTAR is the instrument best suited for spin measurements of BH in X-ray binaries using relativistic reflection. We propose dedicating 60 ks spread in two 30 ks observations to four upcoming, previously unobserved by NuSTAR, BH transients with fluxes above 50 mCrab. For this flux threshold, a 30ks observation would suffice to measure the BH spin, while two observations taken ~15 days apart in different spectral states allow probing the evolution of the system. This treatment followed over the next observing cycles will maximize the number of new BHs observed and, together with gravitational wave observations, will allow developing a unifying view of the distribution of stellar mass BHs.       Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Draghis                       Paul                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       MEASURING THE SPIN OF FUTURE BLACK HOLE TRANSIENTS                                                                      ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                        