Râô8Çw␀␀ÍöHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316ESO399m20                                         @r‹Dg8~¿AA^ûö@å/É{J#¿=tõ•„S¯@a∆p:˚~ë@ÌRyÍN@ÌRÑxVb‹60160725002@Õ`Î"–Â`@Õùëhr∞@œs„P∞Ú|@œs„P∞Ú|SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÌR©Ëı¬è␀␀ÍöHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20220215SgrAstar                                          @pßF‹]cà¿<˚P∞Ú{≥@v}.±ƒ2 ?À¨q≤ïÍ@cÎ„º”@ÌRÑxVb‹@ÌRÑÍN30801024005@tÂ`™d¬¯@t≈∑Ä4m∆@v¬fffff@v¬fffffSCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌR©Àx˚‘␀␀ÎYHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀ÚFollowing successful joint NuSTAR and EHT observation in previous years, we proposal a 100 ks NuSTAR observation to overlap with the EHT observation window in spring 2023 during NuSTAR cycle 8. Our primary science goals include: 1) Detect at least one bright X-ray flare, determine start-stop time, X-ray variability and spectrum during a flare, and feed these information to the EHT Sgr A* analysis; 2) Enlarge the NuSTAR Sgr A* flare sample by detecting characterizing new flares, and test the trend that brighter X-ray flares have harder spectra. A bonus science goal of this observation is to further investigate a newly discovered hard X-ray source located merely 1 pc from Sgr A*.                                                                                                                  Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Zhang                         Shuo                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       JOINT NUSTAR AND EHT PROBE OF SGR A*: FLARES, BLACK HOLE SHADOW AND A NEW HARD X-RAY SOURCE                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20220215SgrAstar                                          @pßHé¿<¯†ê-‡@v}S˜ŒŸ?ÃV’œ™Õü@cÍµ'ª@ÌRÑÍN@ÌRñ[‰õø30801024006@’œV’œ´@’©Gúæ‡@◊‚Ã˜e˝ã@◊‰L˜e˝ãSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÌR©≥ß¢␀␀ÎYHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀ÚFollowing successful joint NuSTAR and EHT observation in previous years, we proposal a 100 ks NuSTAR observation to overlap with the EHT observation window in spring 2023 during NuSTAR cycle 8. Our primary science goals include: 1) Detect at least one bright X-ray flare, determine start-stop time, X-ray variability and spectrum during a flare, and feed these information to the EHT Sgr A* analysis; 2) Enlarge the NuSTAR Sgr A* flare sample by detecting characterizing new flares, and test the trend that brighter X-ray flares have harder spectra. A bonus science goal of this observation is to further investigate a newly discovered hard X-ray source located merely 1 pc from Sgr A*.                                                                                                                  Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Zhang                         Shuo                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       JOINT NUSTAR AND EHT PROBE OF SGR A*: FLARES, BLACK HOLE SHADOW AND A NEW HARD X-RAY SOURCE                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              EHT Chandra                                                                                         ␀␀␀␀(3/4) / idiagnostics                                                                                                    archived  20220215ABELL_3266_POS2                                   @P¯õ•„S¯¿N∞¡T…Ö@q‡qv¿DI∫^5?@6üv_ÿ≠¨@ÌRñ[‰õø@ÌRó#Ü70801002001@X®†ê-‡@XSiDg8@ZAôôôôö@ZAôôôôöSCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌR©êg(ï␀␀Î`Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀˙The most energetic events in the Universe since the Big Bang have been galaxy clusters merging. In rare cases, multiple subclusters have been observed merging together. Abell 3266 is one such cluster. As the subclusters merge, shock fronts form and can be distinguished with telltale signs like a surface brightness edge. Such an edge was observed in this cluster with eROSITA, however it is located in a complex temperature environment with multiple hot regions that is difficult to constrain with that telescope. NuSTAR's ability to probe hard X-ray energies can provide key insights into this region and allow us to constrain the Mach number of the shock as well as potential inverse Compton scattering that may occur from the reacceleration of electrons by the shock.                             Galaxy clusters and extragalactic diffuse objects           ␀1    Rojas                         Randall                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       THE FASCINATING MERGER OF ABELL 3266                                                                                    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20220215ABELL_3266_POS2                                   @PˆˆîFsÇ¿NØ␀h€ã¨@qÆz·H¿DRΩ<6@7B∞ ƒõ¶@ÌRó#Ü@ÌR¬xVb‹70801002002@Ò1^3úø@ÒÖF
