Ns. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20220215SDSSJ102103d08                                    @cgs¸PH¿\(ı¬è@nΩF‹]cà@Ey¯†ê-‡@vº@ÌU9ÍN@ÌU:ÍN60860011001@l ˝Û∂E¢@k›,•zxl@pp␀␀␀␀␀@pp␀␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌUXo·®≈␀␀ÎgHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀óNearby powerful AGN provide the best way to understand the growth of supermassive black holes and their effect on galaxies. Most recently, the BASS survey has identified a sample of 12 highly luminous obscured AGN (5e44-1e46 ergs/s) at 0.2<z<0.4, that have never before been observed in the X-rays outside of short Swift XRT exposures. NuSTAR observations enable accurate X-ray spectral modeling of of NH, Fe Ka, and intrinsic X-ray luminosity to test models of Eddington limited feedback. This survey would form a complete census of the 17 most luminous obscured AGN at z<0.6 detected in the ultra-hard X-rays, providing a template of high luminosity luminosity obscured AGN emission above 10 keV.                                                                                                      Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Koss                          Michael                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       A SURVEY OF THE MOST LUMINOUS HARD X-RAY SELECTED OBSCURED QUASARS AT Z=0.2-0.4                                         ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20220215SDSSJ102103d08                                    @cgDg8~¿hr∞ ≈@nΩ%F
