ing NuSTAR plus NICER, to supplement existing coverage of Cyg X-1, LMC X-3, and GRS 1915+105: three persistently bright, variable, and impactful black hole systems. Regular monitoring of these dynamic systems at the ~100 day timescale commensurate to their variability enables a multitude of science return and establishes a lasting data archive of some of the richest sources in the X-ray sky.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Steiner                       James                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       NUSTAR+NICER MONITORING OF THREE PERSISTENT AND VARIABLE BLACK HOLES                                                    ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20220215GRS_1915p105                                      @rxF‹@%¸¨1&È@F†∫«À)?tz·GÆ{@_©o␀h€å@ÌU˙[‰õø@ÌV	#Ü30802017006@‘gI∫@”Â¿g8~@’⁄,ËßÁ@’⁄,ËßÁSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÌVBì?V␀␀ÎnHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀£We propose a monitoring campaign, using NuSTAR plus NICER, to supplement existing coverage of Cyg X-1, LMC X-3, and GRS 1915+105: three persistently bright, variable, and impactful black hole systems. Regular monitoring of these dynamic systems at the ~100 day timescale commensurate to their variability enables