                                      ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar flare CME                                                                                                                   ␀␀␀(3/4) / CME Kp=5 / M-class solar flare                                                                                  archived  20220215MCGm01m54m008                                     @sÙÒ©˚Ám¿∂4ÍK@F-ˆ˝!ˇ.¿AçS&¡æ@`ÍÁØ∑È@ÌVè[‰õø@ÌVêî»)¯60864005001@|¯ÎÖ∏R@|ßûö@~–␀␀␀␀␀@~–␀␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌV£π␀␀ÎuHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀ +Post-merger galaxies are highly disturbed, coalesced mergers featuring shells and tidal tails, expected to host LLAGN. With deep Chandra/XMM data, we found a high X-ray AGN fraction of ~62% in a sample of 79 post mergers (0.02<z<0.06, logM>10.5) with L~10^41.5 erg/s in 2-10keV. As strong obscuration is expected to be present in late-stage mergers, these LLAGN could be highly obscured which are intrinsically luminous. While the true nature of these LLAGN remains ambiguous with Chandra/XMM data, NuSTAR hard X-ray data can distinguish the obscured luminous AGN from truly low-luminosity AGN. We request 205 ks of NuSTAR time for a well selected sample of 10 Chandra/XMM detected post mergers. Together with the archive data, this work will improve our knowledge of the history of AGN in mergers.  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Li                            Wenhao                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       A NUSTAR VIEW OF AGN IN POST-MERGER GALAXIES                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20220215MCGm01m54m008                                     @sÙ—∑X‚¿Ω<64@F,m≈÷8Ü¿Aå‡uˆ˝"@`Ïñªò«„@ÌVêî»)¯@ÌVüî»)¯60864005002@”ªäŸá+@”Ég|Ìëh@’à	‘ï@’à	‘ïSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÌV¢Ò˜®␀␀ÎuHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀ +Post-merger galaxies are highly disturbed, coalesced mergers featuring shells and tidal tails, expected to host LLAGN. With deep Chandra/XMM data, we found a high X-ray AGN fraction of ~62% in a sample of 79 post mergers (0.02<z<0.06, logM>10.5) with L~10^41.5 erg/s in 2-10keV. As strong obscuration is expected to be present in late-stage mergers, these LLAGN could be highly obscured which are intrinsically luminous. While the true nature of these LLAGN remains ambiguous with Chandra/XMM data, NuSTAR hard X-ray data can distinguish the obscured luminous AGN from truly low-luminosity AGN. We request 205 ks of NuSTAR time for a well selected sample of 10 Chandra/XMM detected post mergers. Together with the archive data, this work will improve our knowledge of the history of AGN in mergers.  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Li                            Wenhao                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       A NUSTAR VIEW OF AGN IN POST-MERGER GALAXIES                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar flare                                                                                                                       ␀␀␀M-class solar flare                                                                                                     archived  20220215NEP_DTDF_MOS08007                                 ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÌVüî»)¯@ÌV†[‰õø60810007001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌV√x˚‘␀␀ÎuHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀ÙThe JWST Deep Time-Domain Field in the NEP (NEP DTDF) is a GTO target that will have excellent 8-band deep (m~28) imaging and grism spectra in the NIR by JWST and already has exquisite multiwavelength data. As JWST is now at its L2 location, the NEP observations are planned to start in June/July and will repeat every 90 days. Given the interesting results from Cycle 5+6 NuSTAR programs, we request 855 ks (3 epochs simultaneous with JWST) for monitoring the NEP in the hard band to focus on variability, 0.3-24 keV spectroscopy through simultaneous XMM observations, the faint end of the AGN population at >8 keV, the obscured fraction, and a variable z>1 FSRQ. Combining Cycle 5+6+8 data, we will get the deepest NuSTAR survey, with 65-70 sources in 3-24 keV, and ~20 single epoch detections.    Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Civano                        Francesca                     NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀N08       THE FIRST TIME DOMAIN NUSTAR AND JWST SURVEY                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316NEP_DTDF_MOS08007                                 @pGÀ)^û@PoÆz·H@WÚÆ}VlÙ@@‹ºj~˘€@T—}øHÃ@ÌV†[‰õø@ÌV◊xVb‹60810007002@Úò3úø@Òÿµ—∑Y@Û;ØAâ7L@Û=Aâ7LSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÌVÒ]Øô␀␀ÎuHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀ÙThe JWST Deep Time-Domain Field in the NEP (NEP DTDF) is a GTO target that will have excellent 8-band deep (m~28) imaging and grism spectra in the NIR by JWST and already has exquisite multiwavelength data. As JWST 