o combine the information about the central engine (particle acceleration) coming from spectra and light curves acquired with NuSTAR with information about the dynamics from astrometry and polarization observed by GRAVITY during flares.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                Normal galaxies                                             ␀1    Stel                          Giovanni                      NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       SGR A* FLARES: CONNECTING PARTICLE ACCELERATION MECHANISM FROM NUSTAR WITH DYNAMICS FROM GRAVITY                        ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              VLT-Gravity                                                                                         ␀␀␀␀(2/5)                                                                                                                   processed 20230530SWIFTJ2056d5m7315                                 ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ì_≠xVb‹@Ì_Æ#Ü60464183001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì_¬ÌÀ™␀␀ÎHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316SWIFTJ2056d5m7315                                 @s¢§?Â…¿RRàŒp:˚@t€ã¨q¿ADÅo␀h‹@n#„º”@Ì_Æ#Ü@Ì_∏#Ü60464183002@–4ì–|Ñ∂@–h€ã¨q@—Tl	‘ï@—Tl	‘ïSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì_¡˚*␀␀ÎHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                      