Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316DS_TucA                                           @v0àŒp:˚¿QLF‹]d@sÇ◊s¸¿G?RT`™e@h…&Èx‘˛@Ì`,î»)¯@Ì`K±9Ò90902319002@ËÄU´üUõ@ËGˆ4m≈÷@ÍJ’T…Ö@ÍK†á¸π$SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì`i›≈ò␀␀Î
Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Non-Proposal ToOs                                           ␀	1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar flare                   NICER HST AAT ATCA                                                                                  ␀␀␀DDT / M-class solar flares / CME Kp=7                                                                                   archived  20230530IGR_J16418m4532                                   ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ì`K±9Ò@Ì`L[‰õø30901022001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì`iÆ,¿™␀␀Î¬Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀#«The magnetic field of the Neutron Star in Supergiant Fast X-ray Transients can be a powerful discriminator between different accretion models invoking accretion from a clumpy stellar wind, mechanisms regulating accretion onto the NS like the propeller effect or magnetic gating. The proposed simultaneous NuSTAR (80 ks) and NICER (20 ks) observations would aim to estimate the magnetic field of the NS in IGR J16418-4532 and carry out broadband analysis of the X-ray flares in the system.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Islam                         Nazma                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       ESTIMATION OF THE MAGNETIC FIELD OF THE SFXT IGR J16418-4532 WITH NUSTAR AND NICER OBSERVATIONS                         ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316IGR_J16418m4532                                   @oM|Ìëhs¿F…†'RTa@u/∫^5?}?ÁÑM:í£@tö1&Èx’@Ì`L[‰õø@Ì`É±9Ò30901022002@ÛSF˚Álã@Ûb9cä	@ı.\e+‘@ı.¨e+‘SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì`£\YÅT␀␀Î¬Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀#«The magnetic field of the Neutron Star in Supergiant Fast X-ray Transients can be a powerful discriminator between different accretion models invoking accretion from a clumpy stellar wind, mechanisms regulating accretion onto the NS like the propeller effect or magnetic gating. The proposed simultaneous NuSTAR (80 ks) and NICER (20 ks) observations would aim to estimate the magnetic field of the NS in IGR J16418-4532 and carry out broadband analysis of the X-ray flares in the system.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Islam                         Nazma                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       ESTIMATION OF THE MAGNETIC FIELD OF THE SFXT IGR J16418-4532 WITH NUSTAR AND NICER OBSERVATIONS                         ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar flare                   NICER                                                                                               ␀␀␀SL-A12 (AX J1631.9-4752) / M-class solar flares                                                                         archived  20230530IGR_16194m2810                                    ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ì`É±9Ò@Ì`ÑèFj30901015001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì`£◊kU␀␀Î¬Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀#\Symbiotic X-ray binaries (SyXBs) are rare low mass X-ray binaries hosting a Gyr-old red giant and a neutron star (NS) accreting from the slow wind of its companion. The NS in these systems is suspected to be strongly magnetized and thus only Myr-old. The puzzling question about SyXBs is how is it possible to have a young strongly magnetized NS coupled with a Gyr-old companion. So far, only in two cases (one to be confirmed) a cyclotron line could be observed to confirm the young age of the NS. We aim at searching for cyclotron lines in a second source of this class (IGR 16194-2810), using a 30 ks-long NuSTAR observation.                                                                                                                    