                     ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Fairall296                                        @B2ÎC,•¿Oõ…ÓÀ˚@qÈ(ı¬è\¿I]®Xy=Ÿ@h·∞â†'@Ìd»ÍN@Ìd’xVb‹60160105002@”©æÖáìﬁ@”z≈m\˚@’åŒp:˚@’åŒp:˚SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ìd‰îÙ>3␀␀Î-Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swif