 Draghis                       Paul                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	R05       TRACKING TWO FUTURE BLACK HOLE OUTBURST WITH NICER AND NUSTAR                                                           ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              NICER                                                                                               ␀␀␀␀(3/3) ToO                                                                                                               archived  20230530ARTXCJ1737d2                                      ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ìeaî»)¯@Ìeb[‰õø60963001001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌeÑñH,␀␀ÎÍHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀$;NuSATR has provided an uninterrupted view towards the energy range covering the peak of the Cosmic X-ray Background (CXB). To bridge the gap of current NuSTAR surveys between the wide-shallow and narrow-deep approaches, we propose joint NuSTAR-XMM observations for 23 sources based on the SRG ART-XC detections in the 200 deg2 North Ecliptic Pole field. The almost identical energy range between ART-XC and NuSTAR and the flux limit of the sample assures high quality spectra for the proposed observations. The NuSTAR-XMM broad-band X-ray observations will measure the physical properties of the sample accurately, providing insights into how a population of z<1.5, moderate luminosity sources contribute to the CXB and fit into the general picture of galaxy and AGN evolution.                       Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Chen                          Chien-Ting                    NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       A NUSTAR AND XMM-NEWTON SURVEY FOR THE SRG/ART-XC NEP CATALOG                                                    