‚â2ïÈ‚A%˙NŸáA%«quéSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÌfP∑.¶␀␀ÎÚHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀$AGNs are powered by their supermassive black hole. Its spin is an important property for the understanding of the accretion in AGNs. However, the spin measurement is not straightforward requiring long observations and the knowledge in advance that the SMBH is actually spinning. Only approximately a dozens of measurements performed at high energies have fully constrained spin values. Recent observations of Mrk 876 report evidence that its SMBH is spinning. The fortunate geometry of the sources and its properties allow for an exceptionally clean view on the active nucleus, which facilitates the spin measurement due to the Compton hump above 10 keV and the skewed Fe-line system. We propose to perform this important measurement by observing Mrk 876 for 200 ks with NuSTAR.                      Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Bottacini                     Eugenio                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       MEASURING THE SPIN OF A SUPERMASSIVE BLACK HOLE WITH NUSTAR                                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀CME                                                                                                                               ␀␀␀CME Kp=5                                                                                                                archived  20230530RBS1640                                           ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ìf"±9Ò@Ìf##Ü60160663001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌfO˙O§˙␀␀Î;Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316RBS1640                                           @pG-V@Eõ⁄QŒ@Q#¸π#¢ú@AÅ◊€Ùà@tê4ÍJå@Ìf##Ü@Ìf3#Ü60160663002@◊^˘â7K«@◊ ^¿Éo@ÿ¸©˚Ám@ÿ¸©˚ÁmSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÌfO„é8‰␀␀Î;Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20230530HESS_J1626m490                                    ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ìf3#Ü@Ìf4èFj30901043001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌfO¡Õ-‰␀␀ÎÚHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀$HESS J1626-490 is an unidentified Galactic TeV source. Analysis of archival Chandra and XMM-Newton data have uncovered a highly obscured potential counterpart with a hard X-ray spectrum near the source center (how offset?). The source resides in a crowded environment making it difficult to use any multiwavelength counterparts to understand its nature. Here we propose a 100 ks NuSTAR observation to help elucidate the nature of this interesting X-ray source and to understand if it is responsible for the observed TeV emission.                                                                                                                                   