=p£◊@i∂„º”ZÜ¿7:^5?|Ó@d:ßÔù≤-@Ìgˆ?r‘£@ÌgˆÕ´∏130901030001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ìh}—∫˙␀␀Ï␀Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀#ŸWe propose independent 50ks observations of three HMXB candidates discovered in the all-sky survey being conducted by eROSITA on board the Spectrum-Roentgen-Gamma mission. The candidates are all persistent across four eROSITA scans with a near-constant flux above 10^-12 erg/s. The proposed observations are imperative in order to conduct detailed spectral and timing analysis of the candidates. The goal of this analysis would be to confirm their characterisation as X-ray binaries and to determine the nature of the compact object. This will increase the number of known low luminosity HMXBs and help subsequently probe their behaviour at low luminosities. We expect between 5000-15000 counts in the total exposure time proposed for, sufficient to conduct detailed studies to achieve the above.    Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Mohideen                      Aafia                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       FOLLOW-UP OF EROSITA X-RAY BINARY CANDIDATES                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316ERASSU_J051651                                    @S–D–©*¿î…Öoi@i∂Æ}VlÙ¿7<æﬂ§@@dDÿD–©@ÌgˆÕ´∏1@ÌhèFj30901030002@ËìGhr∞!@ËUƒá¸π$@Íz_,•zx@Í{ﬂ,•zxSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ìh*ﬁË›}␀␀Ï␀Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀#ŸWe propose independent 50ks observations of three HMXB candidates discovered in the all-sky survey being conducted by eROSITA on board the Spectrum-Roentgen-Gamma mission. The candidates are all persistent across four eROSITA scans with a near-constant flux above 10^-12 erg/s. The proposed observations are imperative in order to conduct detailed spectral and timing analysis of the candidates. The goal of this analysis would be to confirm their characterisation as X-ray binaries and to determine the nature of the compact object. This will increase the number of known low luminosity HMXBs and help subsequently probe their behaviour at low luminosities. We expect between 5000-15000 counts in the total exposure time proposed for, sufficient to conduct detailed studies to achieve the above.    Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Mohideen                      Aafia                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       FOLLOW-UP OF EROSITA X-RAY BINARY CANDIDATES                                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20230530PKS1143m696                                       @fÍJå¿Qv:)«yß@rí´üUõ=¿d˜e˝ä€@TùVlÙ!@ÌhèFj@ÌhÕ´∏160160453001@u’|Ñµ‹∆@u¢[¿6„@w`␀␀␀␀␀@w`␀␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ìh*©o{␀␀ÎIHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 