he thermal/soft state, the black hole undergoes a protracted thermal decline. The thermal/soft state includes only modest contribution from nonthermal components; instead, most of the emission comes from the thermal accretion disk continuum. Accordingly, this state is the gold-standard for spin measurements via X-ray continuum fitting. We request 4x20 ks NuSTAR observations during the thermal phase of the outburst, to monitor a bright black-hole transient in decline, in order to determine its spin. We request a corresponding set of 4x5 ks NICER observations, which significantly improves the constraint.     Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Steiner                       James                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       CONTINUUM-FITTING SPIN MEASUREMENT OF A BLACK-HOLE TRANSIENT                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀(1b/4) / ToO                                                                                                            processed 20230530PKS2300m18                                        @uõÛ∂E°À¿2∫åLò_@F§”ZÖáî¿O¿∑Ä4m∆@sQŒ_@Ìk8î»)¯@Ìk9[‰õø60160816001@jB1&Èy@j/–|Ñµ›@o‡␀␀␀␀␀@o‡␀␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌkA˜`U␀␀ÎlHea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20230530PKS2300m18                                        @uõÙá¸π$¿2æŸá+@F†l"h	’¿O¡ñRΩ<6@s	ú‡uˆ˝@Ìk9[‰õø@ÌkGÕ´∏160160816002@”§Y(åÁ@”v\‚e,@’"ó.HËß@’"ó.HËßSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ìl[†ŒQ)␀␀ÎlHea_16Dec2022_V6.31.1_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20230530MS_22549m3712                                     @uÜOÑM¿Bv˘€"–Â@ç∏∫«À¿OÊlÙ!-@r™◊€Ùá˝@ÌkGÕ´∏1@ÌkH#Ü60901012001@q…s¸PH@qñ;dZ¨@s␀fœAÚ@s␀fœAÚSCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌkV•*€6␀␀Ï"Hea_04Aug2021_V6.29b_nustardas_04May21_v2.1.1                                   ␀␀#¨MS 22549-3712 is a unique AGN that shows both a quasi-periodic oscillation (QPO) and X-ray reflection and reverberation from the inner accretion disk. QPOs hold the potential to probe General Relativity and the detailed physics of the accretion process onto black holes, and to provide independent constraints on the black hole spin. Taking advantage of QPOs, however, requires a detailed understanding of the mechanism by which they are produced. We request deep, simultaneous observations of MS 22549-3712 using NuSTAR and XMM-Newton, to take advantage of the X-ray reflection and reverberation in this AGN to probe the origin of the QPO, by studying how the QPO corresponds to variability of the inner accretion disk and/or corona.                                                                  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Wilkins                       Daniel                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       PROBING THE ORIGIN OF THE QPO IN THE AGN MS 22549-3712                                                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20230530MS_22549m3712                                     @uÜzêñº¿B|˝Û∂E¢@
