otal of 90ks of NGC 1275 observations to occur in three separate visits. We plan to carry out an SED modeling study with simultaneous observations from Swift-UVOT, Swift-XRT, Fermi-LAT and VERITAS.  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Talluri                       Anjana                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       PROBING A MULTI-COMPONENT SED OF NGC 1275 WITH NUSTAR IN FLARING AND NON-FLARING TEV GAMMA-RAY STATES                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 processed 20230530NGC_1275                                          @HıOﬂ;dZ@D≈„º”[@b ›/üæ¿*Ùá¸π#£@QÙ'RT`™@ÌlÉ#Ü@ÌlõxVb‹60902033004@ﬂ[`>BZÓ@ﬂ!›5®Xy@·Ipu%F@·K∞u%FSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ìlπb:gÎ␀␀ÏˆHea_16Dec2022_V6.31.1_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                  ␀␀$9NGC 1275 is one of the few radio galaxies known to emit very high energy gamma rays. The physical mechanisms are not entirely understood in either the flare or quiescent state. Studies without NuSTAR data show a multi-component model is needed to fit the multi-wavelength spectral energy distribution (SED) of the 2017 flare while a single-zone model fits the quiescent SED. NuSTAR is the only instrument capable of probing the hard X-ray range of the SED and will clearly determine whether a single zone SSC is sufficient for the quiescent state or an additional component is required. We request a total of 90ks of NGC 1275 observations to occur in three separate visits. We plan to carry out an SED modeling study with simultaneous observations from Swift-UVOT, Swift-XRT, Fermi-LAT and VERITAS.  Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Talluri                       Anjana                        NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       PROBING A MULTI-COMPONENT SED OF NGC 1275 WITH NUSTAR IN FLARING AND NON-FLARING TEV GAMMA-RAY STATES                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              VERITAS                                                                                             ␀␀␀␀(2/3)                                                                                                                   processed 20230530UU_Aqr                                            @tƒ	‘ï+¿í£S&@L*‰éäqﬁ¿FN¬&ÄùI@s∏Aâ7K«@ÌlõxVb‹@Ìlú[‰õø30901019001@t˙v_ÿ≠¨@t»?º@vê␀␀␀␀␀@vê␀␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌlπöåSp␀␀Ï"Hea_16Dec2022_V6.31.1_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                  ␀␀#ìEclipsing Cataclysmic Variables (CVs) provide an unique opportunity to investigate deeply into their X-ray emitting regions by disentangling the soft X-ray emission and the hard X-ray emission. The proposal requests simultaneous NuSTAR and XMM observations of two eclipsing CVs: UU Aqr, a nova-like variable and V902 Mon, an intermediate polar. The joint observations are requested over the two orbital cycles of the source: 29 ks for UU Aqr and 59 ks for V902 Mon, each with NuSTAR and XMM. The observations would be used to detect X-ray eclipses and infer the origin of the hard X-rays                                                                                                                                                                                                                     Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Islam                         Nazma                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       CONSTRAINING THE X-RAY EMITTING REGIONS IN TWO ECLIPSING CVS WITH JOINT NUSTAR AND XMM OBSERVATIONS                     ␀␀␀␀