y will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316NGC_1068                                          @DR£S&ø©rGE8Ô5@e{_o“Û¿J!„º”@s≠∞â†'R@ÌuÑÍN@Ìu≠#Ü60160467002@Íº1çOﬂ;@Íz¿6„@Ï¿÷d¬¯8@Ï¬d¬¯8SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÌvºÈË|f␀␀Î≤Hea_16Dec2022_V6.31.1_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar flare                                                                                                                       ␀␀␀Solar flare                                                                                                             archived  20230530SwiftJ1727_SADA_23024                             ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ìu≠#Ü@ÌuÆÍN80901048001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌvΩ(NÇ␀␀ÏÑHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀$IStellar-mass black holes in X-ray transients undergo months-long outbursts during which they explore wide-ranging accretion rates and spectral-timing states. Following transitioning to the thermal/soft state, the black hole undergoes a protracted thermal decline. The thermal/soft state includes only modest contribution from nonthermal components; instead, most of the emission comes from the thermal accretion disk continuum. Accordingly, this state is the gold-standard for spin measurements via X-ray continuum fitting. We request 4x20 ks NuSTAR observations during the thermal phase of the outburst, to monitor a bright black-hole transient in decline, in order to determine its spin. We request a corresponding set of 4x5 ks NICER observations, which significantly improves the constraint.     Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Steiner                       James                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       CONTINUUM-FITTING SPIN MEASUREMENT OF A BLACK-HOLE TRANSIENT                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR /                                                                                                               processed 20150316SwiftJ1727d8m1613                                 @p_ØOÑM¿01‰˜e˝ã@!
¶L/É@%zxl"h@d°µsÍ≥@ÌuÆÍN@Ìu¡Õ´∏180902348003@∞c¡4ÍK@∞i.Ov_Ÿ@≥D8åÁ∞@≥D8åÁ∞SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÌvΩJm¸5␀␀ÏÑHea_16Dec2022_V6.31.1_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                  ␀␀$IStellar-mass black holes in X-ray transients undergo months-long outbursts during which they explore wide-ranging accretion rates and spectral-timing states. Following transitioning to the thermal/soft state, the black hole undergoes a protracted thermal decline. The thermal/soft state includes only modest contribution from nonthermal components; instead, most of the emission comes from the thermal accretion disk continuum. Accordingly, this state is the gold-standard for spin measurements via X-ray continuum fitting. We request 4x20 ks NuSTAR observations during the thermal phase of the outburst, to monitor a bright black-hole transient in decline, in order to determine its spin. We request a corresponding set of 4x5 ks NICER observations, which significantly improves the constraint.     Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Steiner                       James                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       CONTINUUM-FITTING SPIN MEASUREMENT OF A BLACK-HOLE TRANSIENT                                                            ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀(2/4)                                                                                                                   processed 202305302MASXJ01492228m5015073                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ìu¡Õ´∏1@Ìu¬Õ´∏160161076001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ìu·w‘c␀␀ÎπHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is compris