␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌxGŸ8Çw␀␀Î«Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀#ûWe request a 30ks NuSTAR observation of Cen X-3 contemporaneous with XRISM observations of the HMXB, Cen X-3. The XRISM+NuSTAR observation will span a broadband energy range and enable us to perform self-consistent modeling of the astrophysical plasma by measuring the ionization structure and emission spectra of photoionized gas clouds in the source. NuSTAR will be indispensable in measuring the hard X-ray radiation as the powering source of the photoionization and fluorescence processes. In addition, we will also perform broadband spectro-timing studies with XRISM+ NuSTAR to disentangle the physical causes of aperiodic X-ray variability seen in Cen X-3 caused either by clumpy winds, instabilities in the accretion disk or by onset of magnetic/centrifugal gating.                            Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Pradhan                       Pragati                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       MODELLING THE ASTROPHYSICAL PLASMA IN CEN X-3 WITH NUSTAR DURING XRISM/PV OBSERVATIONS                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Cen_X3                                            @eM|Ìëhs¿NQ&Èx‘˛@r?õ=»K?€'ª/ÏW@k©É{J#:@Ìx<xVb‹@ÌxUÍN30901020002@÷od›/†@÷ÒOÑM@·ñË∫«À@·ô(∫«ÀSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÌxcfOD␀␀Î«Hea_16Dec2022_V6.31.1_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                  ␀␀#ûWe request a 30ks NuSTAR observation of Cen X-3 contemporaneous with XRISM observations of the HMXB, Cen X-3. The XRISM+NuSTAR observation will span a broadband energy range and enable us to perform self-consistent modeling of the astrophysical plasma by measuring the ionization structure and emission spectra of photoionized gas clouds in the source. NuSTAR will be indispensable in measuring the hard X-ray radiation as the powering source of the photoionization and fluorescence processes. In addition, we will also perform broadband spectro-timing studies with XRISM+ NuSTAR to disentangle the physical causes of aperiodic X-ray variability seen in Cen X-3 caused either by clumpy winds, instabilities in the accretion disk or by onset of magnetic/centrifugal gating.                            Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Pradhan                       Pragati                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       MODELLING THE ASTROPHYSICAL PLASMA IN CEN X-3 WITH NUSTAR DURING XRISM/PV OBSERVATIONS                                  ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XRISM                                                                                               ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20230530GX339m4                                           ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÌxUÍN@ÌxVxVb‹91002306001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌxcR4Vy␀␀ÎŒHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.          