JÄ␀␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ìx™UŒ≤@␀␀ÏÑHea_16Dec2022_V6.31.1_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                  ␀␀$3The JWST Time-Domain Field in the NEP (NEP) is a GTO target currently being observed every 90 days (4 epochs) with JWST NIRCAM and NIRISS. The NEP has exquisite multiwavelength data. NuSTAR+XMM (Cycle 8) are currently observing it simultaneously with JWST. In JWST Cycle 2, a new proposal to observe the NEP for 2 more years has been submitted. Given the interesting results from NuSTAR Cycle 5+6+8, we request 900 ks (4 epochs) for continuing to monitor the NEP in the hard X-ray band simultaneously with JWST: this dataset will be unique for X-ray-NIR time-domain studies. This additional monitoring will allow studies of AGN variability, 0.3-24 keV spectroscopy through simultaneous XMM observations, the faint end of the AGN population at >8 keV, and the obscured fraction.                       Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Civano                        Francesca                     NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       TIME-DOMAIN STUDIES IN THE NEP FIELD WITH NUSTAR AND JWST                                                               ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 processed 20230530NEPTDF3_POS1                                      @pRY≥–|Ö@Pz«À)_@W¸•zxl"@@¥ÍJåM@fRbM“Ò™@ÌxîÕ´∏1@Ìx≈±9Ò60910007002@Ú‰)v_ÿÆ@ÚπY‡uˆ˝@Ù=€Èx‘˛@Ù>+Èx‘˛SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÌxÍvÕé˚␀␀ÏÑHea_16Dec2022_V6.31.1_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                  ␀␀$3The JWST Time-Domain Field in the NEP (NEP) is a GTO target currently being observed every 90 days (4 epochs) with JWST NIRCAM and NIRISS. The NEP has exquisite multiwavelength data. NuSTAR+XMM (Cycle 8) are currently observing it simultaneously with JWST. In JWST Cycle 2, a new proposal to observe the NEP for 2 more years has been submitted. Given the interesting results from NuSTAR Cycle 5+6+8, we request 900 ks (4 epochs) for continuing to monitor the NEP in the hard X-ray band simultaneously with JWST: this dataset will be unique for X-ray-NIR time-domain studies. This additional monitoring will allow studies of AGN variability, 0.3-24 keV spectroscopy through simultaneous XMM observations, the faint end of the AGN population at >8 keV, and the obscured fraction.                       Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Civano                        Francesca                     NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       TIME-DOMAIN STUDIES IN THE NEP FIELD WITH NUSTAR AND JWST                                                               ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        processed 20230530NEPTDF3_POS3                                      ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ìx≈±9Ò@Ìx≈ÍN60910009001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌxÍ[«ﬁ†␀␀ÏÑHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀$3The JWST Time-Domain Field in the NEP (NEP) is a GTO target currently being observed every 90 days (4 epochs) with JWST NIRCAM and NIRISS. The NEP has exquisite multiwavelength data. NuSTAR+XMM (Cycle 8) are currently observing it simultaneously with JWST. In JWST Cycle 2, a new proposal to observe the NEP for 2 more years has been submitted. Given the interesting results from NuSTAR Cycle 5+6+8,