␀—∑Y@eÑ␀—∑YSCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì{Ö∞␀␀ÎÍHea_16Dec2022_V6.31.1_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                  ␀␀#°Ultra-Fast Outflows (UFOs) potentially provide the most significant AGN feedback. PDS 456 hosts the archetypical, persistent UFO, which made it a Performance Verification target for XRISM. XRISM will resolve the velocity profile of the UFO and its associated emission lines at an unprecedented high resolution of E<7eV, in order to measure its kinetic power most accurately. This goal cannot be achieved without properly measuring the hard X-ray continuum, which only NuSTAR can. NuSTAR will also uniquely constrain the coronal temperature. The demonstrated variability of PDS 456 requires a coordinated campaign of NuSTAR, XRISM, XMM-Newton, and approved Swift/XRT monitoring. XMM/RGS will crucially provide the highest spectral resolution below 1 keV.                                               Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Behar                         Ehud                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       NUSTAR-XRISM OBSERVATIONS OF THE ARCHETYPICAL ULTRA FAST OUTFLOW OF PDS 456                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20230530PDS_456                                           @paÒA [¿¿,y¿ÎÌ˙D@$å"h	‘ï@&ﬂ|Ìëhs@c≥RT`™e@Ì{#Ü@Ì{˜î»)¯60901011002An√;dZA4ü$›/Aˆ√‚∂Æ}A¯Î‚∂Æ}SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì|√≤¢␀␀ÎÍHea_16Dec2022_V6.31.1_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                  ␀␀#°Ultra-Fast Outflows (UFOs) potentially provide the most significant AGN feedback. PDS 456 hosts the archetypical, persistent UFO, which made it a Performance Verification target for XRISM. XRISM will resolve the velocity profile of the UFO and its associated emission lines at an unprecedented high resolution of E<7eV, in order to measure its kinetic power most accurately. This goal cannot be achieved without properly measuring the hard X-ray continuum, which only NuSTAR can. NuSTAR will also uniquely constrain the coronal temperature. The demonstrated variability of PDS 456 requires a coordinated campaign of NuSTAR, XRISM, XMM-Newton, and approved Swift/XRT monitoring. XMM/RGS will crucially provide the highest spectral resolution below 1 keV.                                               Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Behar                         Ehud                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       NUSTAR-XRISM OBSERVATIONS OF THE ARCHETYPICAL ULTRA FAST OUTFLOW OF PDS 456                                             ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              XMM/XRISM                                                                                           ␀␀␀ SL-B01 (GX 9+9)                                                                                                        archived  20230530OP_313                                            ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ì{˜î»)¯@Ì{¯[‰õø91002609003␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì|·Òñë␀␀ÎÍHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀␀␀Time has been allocated to respond to targets of opportunity during the NuSTAR primary mission. Targets may include, but are not limited to; 1) Core collapse SN and associated shocks, 2) Tidal disruption flare, 3) extreme gamma-ray bursts, 4) Solar flares, 5) SLN SN-1. The response time from a ToO trigger for the NuSTAR observatory is 48 hours, but faster response times are anticipated.    