sed of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20230530RXJ2044d0p2833                                    @sqz·GÆ@<èù≤-V@QÀÂ…‰¿!-´üUõ=@e≠Y≥–|Ö@Ì}[‰õø@Ì} èFj60160745002@÷;.∞ ƒú@÷hâ†'R@◊ÒN{≤˛≈@◊ÒŒ{≤˛≈SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì}ün]L␀␀ÎÒHea_23Feb2024_V6.33_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar flare                                                                                                                       ␀␀␀                                                                                                                        archived  20230530Cyg_X3                                            @sBŒp:˚@D{ïÅ$›@SÓu%F?Á·∞â†'R@f8Vìu@Ì} èFj@Ì} [‰õø30901046001@vV’œ™Œ@v)9XbN@{ê␀␀␀␀␀@{ê␀␀␀␀␀SCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì}OΩ'“}␀␀ÎÒHea_16Dec2022_V6.31.1_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                  ␀␀$-A key goal of the XRISM observations of Cyg X-3 is to observe the spectrum in the iron K line region, between 5-9 keV. Simultaneous observations using both NuSTAR and XRISM will greatly help in characterizing the continuum in this energy band, and this is needed in order to study the iron K lines. XRISM has approved a 40ks observation of Cyg X-3 as part of the performance verification (PV) phase of the satellite commissioning. We request simultaneous Nustar coverage for the full 40ks of our XRISM time. Furthermore, Cyg X-3 can be very bright during its high state, and NuSTAR will allow characterization of the continuum without bright source limitations, and thus can aid in interpreting the XRISM observations of the iron lines in such a state.                                                Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Kallman                       Timothy                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       JOINT XRISM-NUSTAR OBSERVATIONS OF CYG X-3                                                                              ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20230530Cyg_X3                                            @sB£n.±ƒ@D|ŸË>B[@SÓ8ÜYJı?ËE° ¿É@f'˝ä⁄πı@Ì} [‰õø@Ì}=±9Ò30901046002@ÿ˝i“Ò©¸@ŸIµÇ©ì@·õ@’œ™Œ@·õ†’œ™ŒSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì}Oß(î´␀␀ÎÒHea_16Dec2022_V6.31.1_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                  ␀␀$-A key goal of the XRISM observations of Cyg X-3 is to observe the spectrum in the iron K line region, between 5-9 keV. Simultaneous observations using both NuSTAR and XRISM will greatly help in characterizing the continuum in this energy band, and this is needed in order to study the iron K lines. XRISM has approved a 40ks observation of Cyg X-3 as part of the performance verification (PV) phase of the satellite commissioning. We request simultaneous Nustar coverage for the full 40ks of our XRISM time. Furthermore, Cyg X-3 can be very bright during its high state, and NuSTAR will allow characterization of the continuum without bright source limitations, and thus can aid in interpreting the XRISM observations of the iron lines in such a state.                                                Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Kallman                       Timothy                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       JOINT XRISM-NUSTAR OBSERVATIONS OF CYG X-3                                                                              ␀␀<Å␀␀␀␀Solar CME                     XRISM                                                                                               ␀␀␀ Kp=8                                                                                                                   archived  20230530IGR_J19552p0044                                   @r≠∏QÎÖ?ÈŸb∂Æ}@Dt!-w2¿+'¸π#¢ú@c WßÜ¬@Ì}=±9Ò@Ì}>?r‘£30901034001@|ñÎÌ˙C˛@|Zcä	@~“ÃÃÃÃÕ@~“ÃÃÃÃÕSCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì}OìWõ‡␀␀Ï®Hea_16Dec2022_V6.31.1_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                  ␀␀#ÒThe spectra of magnetic Cataclysmic Variables(mCVs) consist of multi-temperature thermal plasma emission, modified with Compton reflection, complex intrinsic absorber, and the characteristic Fe 6.4 keV line. Precise measurement of Compton reflection requires modelling the underlying continuum along with constraining the complex absorber and resolving the Fe 6.4 keV line. We therefore propose joint NuSTAR (50x3=150ks) and XMM (25x3=75ks) observation for three Asynchronous Polars (APs) (BY Cam, V1432 Aql, IGR J19552+0044), a unique and rare sub-category of mCVs, to determine the Compton reflection which aims to address geometry and accretion physics of these systems. From the shock temperature obtained from the multi-temperature continuum, we will also provide an accurate estimate of the    Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Dutta                         Anirban                       NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       MEASURING THE COMPTON REFLECTION FOR THREE ASYNCHRONOUS POLARS USING JOINT NUSTAR-XMM OBSERVATION                       ␀␀␀␀␀