ee components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20230530B22107p35A                                        @s◊;dZ¨@A«»K]Ãd@Tπå~($¿ ú¨1&È@fv1&Èx’@Ì}gèFj@Ì}vî»)¯60160750002@‘IÃ_ˆî@‘+Æz·@’Ìúı¬è\@’Ô¨ı¬è\SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì}Ü◊SÀ␀␀ÎÒHea_16Dec2022_V6.31.1_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                  ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMO