SCIENCE                 CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @Ì~©†˛‹ª␀␀ÎˇHea_23Feb2024_V6.33_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                    ␀␀#âWe propose four 20 ks NuSTAR observations of the high-inclination dipping low-mass X-ray binaries (LMXB) XB1916-053 and X1624-490 quasi simultaneous to XRISM PV Phase observations of these targets. The XRISM observations are needed to characterise the absorbers (column densities, line ratios and velocity width and shift) throughout the orbit. The NuSTAR observations are crucial to determine the ionising continuum and derive the ionisation parameter (and ultimately the density and location) of the plasmas from the line ratios. We will use the changes in the absorbers' properties to model the complex spectral changes throughout the orbit, including during dips, and to trace the variability of the absorber associated with changes in the source luminosity and hardness to make an accretion map.Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Trigo                         Maria                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       MAPPING THE ACCRETION DISC WITH IONISED PLASMAS IN DIPPING SOURCES                                                      ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  202305304U_1624m49                                        @n‚[¿6„¿Hñ‚ÎC-@tÏßÜ¬&Åøü;dZ¨@fçsÍ≥g°@Ì~ïÕ´∏1@Ì~§[‰õø30902018004@“yUøHÃ@“pºé@’\81&Èy@’\¯1&ÈySCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @Ì~…Ÿ˙∞º␀␀ÎˇHea_23Feb2024_V6.33_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                    ␀␀#âWe propose four 20 ks NuSTAR observations of the high-inclination dipping low-mass X-ray binaries (LMXB) XB1916-053 and X1624-490 