lativistically broadened emission from the innermost regions of the accretion disk around the black hole in Cygnus X-1 with unprecedented sensitivity, which will enable a black hole spin measurement with an unparalleled understanding of the systematic uncertainties associated.                                                                                                                            Galactic Compact Sources                                    ␀1    Draghis                       Paul                          NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	N09       JOINT XRISM AND NUSTAR OBSERVATIONS OF CYGNUS X-1                                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 archived  20150316Cygnus_X1                                         @r∫RΩ<6@A†öu%F@Q–çπ@	oiDg8@cVéäqﬁj@Ì[‰õø@Ì(î»)¯30901039002@–{’∫^5?@–ﬁÈ≥–|Ö@ŸW¡è≈Å@ŸW¡è≈ÅSCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÌI˛ìÈ?␀␀ÎˇHea_23Feb2024_V6.33_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                    ␀␀$With the launch of XRISM planned in May 2023, it will observe Cygnus X-1 during its product verification (PV) phase. We propose to use NuSTAR to observe Cygnus X-1 for 30ks simultaneously with the 100ks XRISM PV observation which would enable unlocking the full potential of the two instruments. By constraining the narrow emission and absorption features using XRISM spectra, we will measure the relativistically broadened emission from the innermost regions of the accretion disk around the black hole in Cygnus X-1 with unprecedented sensitivity, which will enable a black hole spin measurement with an unparalleled understanding of the systematic uncertainties associated