TOO       Targets of Opportunity                                                                                                  ␀␀XΩ␀␀␀␀Solar flare                                                                                                                       ␀␀␀(3/3) DDT / bursting pixel FPMB-DET1 / data gaps 22717s / Solar flare                                                   archived  20240422CGCG333m038                                       @cŒcä	@R@«‚Ç@∏@`{≤˛≈m@D3¿6‚Î@'^5?|Ó@ÌÅ4#Ü@ÌÅ>±9Ò60161400002@–¥∑Ä4n@√µÑM;@—E¨ŸË>@—E¨ŸË>SCIENCE                 CPMODEINERTIAL  EIGEN     @ÌÅT¥Vxõ␀␀ÏHea_23Feb2024_V6.33_nustardas_16Feb22_v2.1.2                                    ␀␀␀␀The baseline NuSTAR extragalactic survey is comprised of three components: one deg^2 of the COSMOS field (50ks per position), 0.3 deg^2 of the ECDFS (200ks per position), and a ~3 deg^2 shallow survey (5ks per position), achieved by targeting 100 Swift-BAT identified AGNs.  Models predict that NuSTAR will detect ~200 AGNs in the COSMOS+E-CDF-S surveys and ~19 Compton-thick AGNs. The shallow survey will deliver a sample of serendipitous detection of AGNs in the NuSTAR field of view.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Harrison                      Fiona                         NULL                          NULL                          USA                           ␀EGS       Extragalactic Surveys                                                                                                   ␀␀˜␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀ data gaps 1020s                                                                                                        archived  20240422Mrk_231                                           ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÌÅ>±9Ò@ÌÅ?èFj60902002001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌÅTÙ%Ì	␀␀ÌòHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀gÄWe propose a simultaneous 240 ks XMM & 120 ks NuSTAR observation to study the properties of the disk wind detected in Mrk231. The nearby ULIRG/QSO Mrk231 is an exceptional QSO and a prototypical object, where we are viewing the feedback in action with overwhelming evidence of multiphase outflows. Mrk231 is a BAL QSO, where both a X-ray wind and galaxy-scale outflows were detected and appears to follow the prediction for an energy conserving scenario. Despite that, the physical properties of the X-ray wind are poorly known. Our proposed observation will be the first broad-band observation deep enough to properly investigate this wind. This observation will allow us to put stronger constraints on the energetics of the disk wind and test if it is one of the few energy conserving winds.       Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Braito                        Valentina                     NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀	X22       The extraordinary case of Mrk 231                                                                                       ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                                  ␀␀␀␀STELLAR                                                                                                                 processed 20150316Mrk_231                                           @h?6zêó@Lr∂Æ}Vm@^ª/ÏV÷@NPH@EıOﬂ;dZ@ÌÅ?èFj@ÌÅkxVb‹60902002002@Ó˚≤ïÈ·±@Ó´Å◊€ı@ûÉï*ô@