           NULL                                                        ␀	N09       TIME-DOMAIN STUDIES IN THE NEP FIELD WITH NUSTAR AND JWST                                                               ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Solar flare                                                                                                                       ␀␀␀Solar flare                                                                                                             processed 20240422MCG_03_58_007                                     ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@ÌÇ∂ÍN@ÌÇ∑Õ´∏161002005001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌÇ¬=åµ␀␀Ì§Hea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀pùWe propose a new intense monitoring campaign consisting of 12x60 ksec XMM-Newton observations coordinated with 6 x 40 ksec NuSTAR exposures of MCG -03- 58-007, which is a powerful and extremely variable disk wind. Past X-ray observations of this remarkable wind revealed a dramatic and fast variability of the velocity of the disk wind, which dropped from v/c~-0.2 to v/c~-0.074 in just 16 days. Such variability is at odds with other disk winds and challenging for current models, and therefore it deserves a further investigation. With the new observations we will: (i) confirm the velocity variations and their timescales, (ii) probe the presence of multiple velocity components and (iii) investigate the wind acceleration mechanism.                                                                Active galaxies and Quasars                                 ␀1    Braito                        Valentina                     NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀
