N10       PROBING THE HARD X-RAY PROPERTIES OF MS 1603.6+2600 WITH NICER AND NUSTAR                                               ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀                              NICER                                                                                               ␀␀␀␀                                                                                                                        processed 20240422ZTF24aaoxmyb                                      ¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀¿X¿␀␀␀␀␀@Ìâ¡Õ´∏1@Ìâ¬#Ü81001628001␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀SLEW                    CPMODESTELLAR   POWER     @ÌâÓ_IÙü␀␀ÌHea_30Jun2014_V6.16_nustardas_28May14_v1.4.1                                    ␀␀'wTidal disruption events (TDEs) offer great opportunities to study the physics of black hole accretion in the super-Eddington regime. A growing number of X-ray bright TDEs are being discovered by current and upcoming time domain surveys. We propose two epochs of 50ks NuSTAR + 15ks Swift ToO observations on TDEs with bright hard X-ray emission. For jetted TDEs, this program will shed light on the location, composition and radiation mechanism of relativistic jets launched from super-Eddington accreting black holes. For non-jetted TDEs with non-thermal X-ray emission, this program will provide a broadband X-ray spectrum with relativistic reflection features that allows us to measure key physical quantities of the accretion flow (e.g., disk ionization state, BH spin, inclination).              Proposed ToOs and Directors Discretionary Time              ␀1    Yao                           Yuhan                         NULL                          NULL                                                        ␀
